{"id": "age-of-empires-ii-2013", "title": "Age of Empires II (2013)", "steam": 221380, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-05"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Steam starts Launcher.exe. The launcher forwards its own command line to AoK HD.exe. After OK on Validating Subscriptions, the game opens resources/_common/movies/aoeiihd_x2.wmv and the process ends at the log line \"Opening video...\". With SKIPINTRO the same log says \"Skipping due to commandline\" and the main menu is created. Highball passes SKIPINTRO on Play. A match was not played, and Wine's own Direct3D was not tried. A report on an M4 Pro rates it playable over 38 minutes with DXMT on the default engine (r28), without saying what wasn't perfect (highball-db#1004)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "After OK on Validating Subscriptions, the game closes.", "cause": "The game opens the intro movie aoeiihd_x2.wmv. Its log stops at \"Opening video...\" and the process is gone. Seen 2026-10-06 on an M3 Pro, macOS 26.7.1, engine x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r22, DXMT.", "fix": "Launch with SKIPINTRO. Highball adds that argument on Play. The launcher passes it through to AoK HD.exe."}], "verified": {"date": null, "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r22", "chip": "Apple M3 Pro"}, "source": "db/games/age-of-empires-ii-2013.json"},
{"id": "age-of-empires-ii-definitive-edition", "title": "Age of Empires II: Definitive Edition", "steam": 813780, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 3, "last": "2026-11-11"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["This game has a native macOS version on Steam, so the Mac Steam app runs it directly without Highball. Through Highball, the Windows build crashed before its splash screen on the Wine 10 engine (r21) and ran on the Wine 11 engine (r19, DXMT) for the same player. No measurement here yet. On an M5 Max with the same Wine 11 engine (r19) it runs out of memory unless Steam and the game are quit after each match (highball-db#1149)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crashes before the splash screen on the Wine 10 engine, with an illegal instruction exception in one report", "cause": "not measured. Seen on an M3 Pro with engine r21 (highball-db#399) and on an M2 with macOS 15.8.2 and engine r28 (highball-db#977)", "fix": "Play the native Mac version, or use the Wine 11 engine (Advanced, Engine on the environment's page), where it ran."}, {"symptom": "Memory use keeps growing during play, until the Mac runs out of memory after a match (reported on an M3 Pro and an M5 Max, Wine 11 engine r19, highball-db#400 and #1149)", "cause": "not investigated. A Sikarugir report describes the same (Sikarugir-App/Sikarugir#233)", "fix": "quit Steam and the game fully after each match (highball-db#1149, credit trca7)."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/age-of-empires-ii-definitive-edition.json"},
