{"id": "age-of-history-3", "title": "Age of History 3", "steam": 2772750, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxvk"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-09-20"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect after an 85-minute session on DXVK on an M5 Pro with macOS 26.6.2, long enough to cover real play rather than only the launch; frame rate not recorded yet."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/age-of-history-3.json"},
{"id": "age-of-mythology-extended-edition", "title": "Age of Mythology: Extended Edition", "steam": 266840, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 3, "last": "2026-11-16"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["A 32-bit game, and AoMX.exe isn't marked large address aware, so it has 2 GB of address space. Longer matches run out of it: the game crashes to the desktop after about 4 to 6 minutes of a random map, on the default engine r28 and on the Wine 11 engine r31, with DXMT or D3DMetal (highball-db#1282). The reporter's fix is the Wine 11 engine r31 with WINE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE=1 in the environment's variables, which played a 20 minute random map with no errors. The first report rated it perfect after 11 minutes on an M4 Pro with DXMT on the default engine, too short to hit the crash (highball-db#1196). Age of Mythology: Retold has its own page."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crashes to the desktop after about 4 to 6 minutes of a random map, after hundreds of 'out of memory for allocation' errors in the log (M4 Pro, Wine 10 r28 and Wine 11 r31, DXMT and D3DMetal, highball-db#1282)", "cause": "AoMX.exe is 32-bit and not marked large address aware (PE characteristics 0x102), so it gets 2 GB of address space, found by the reporter", "fix": "use the Wine 11 engine r31 and add WINE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE=1 to the environment's variables, which played 20 minutes with no errors for the reporter. The reporter found that the default engine r28 doesn't read it. Don't set the flag in AoMX.exe itself: Steam then fails the file's signature check and won't start the game"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/age-of-mythology-extended-edition.json"},
{"id": "age-of-mythology-retold", "title": "Age of Mythology: Retold", "steam": 1934680, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on D3DMetal on the Wine 11 engine r15 on an M4 Pro. Two of the reporter's settings match what the game's own Steam page asks for, DirectX 12 and a processor with AVX. D3DMetal is the DirectX 12 route, and AVX advertised lets the game see AVX. Whether it starts without AVX advertised, in another graphics mode, or on the default engine was not reported, no frame rate was given, and nothing was measured here. A second player rates it playable with minor issues they did not describe after 95 minutes on an M2, also on D3DMetal on the Wine 11 engine with AVX advertised. At 4K Retina on an M4 Max on the Wine 11 engine with D3DMetal, 70 to 100 fps, after one hang and a slow first start. A 4 minute report rates it playable with a bit of stutter on a base M5 with the Wine 11 engine r31, D3DMetal by the report (highball-db#1229)."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/age-of-mythology-retold.json"},
{"id": "agent-a-a-puzzle-in-disguise", "title": "Agent A: A puzzle in disguise", "steam": 801480, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 2, "last": "2026-11-03"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The Windows version doesn't get past the title screen in one report on an M1, with D3DMetal or DXMT, the Epic copy: the game says Authentication failed. The Epic purchase includes a Mac version, which works for the same player through Highball 0.10.27 (highball-db#943). A Unity game, Direct3D 11."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "'Authentication failed' on the title screen (Epic copy, M1, D3DMetal and DXMT, Wine 10 r29)", "cause": "not diagnosed. The log shows D3DMetal answering 'Unsupported: IDXGIResource::GetSharedHandle', then crash dumps and the Epic overlay's crash reporter starting. Whether that is what fails the sign-in is not known", "fix": "play the Epic Mac version, which Highball installs since 0.10.27 (highball-db#943, credit udance4ever)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/agent-a-a-puzzle-in-disguise.json"},
{"id": "aimlabs", "title": "Aimlabs", "steam": 714010, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-27"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on an M3 with DXMT. Signing in with Google did not work."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Signing in with Google does not work", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/aimlabs.json"},
{"id": "aion-2", "title": "AION 2", "steam": 3393110, "status": "blocked", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["NCGuard"], "verdict": "blocked"}, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Does not start, NCGuard, the game's anti-cheat, stops it. With msync NCGuard exits about 8 seconds in with 0xE0000015 on a fresh environment (2 of 2 tries). With sync off NCGuard finishes its setup, then the game spins on its splash screen at about 157% CPU for over seven minutes without loading anything (3 of 3). With esync Steam crashes before the game starts (1 of 1)."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/aion-2.json"},
{"id": "akane", "title": "Akane", "steam": 884260, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-06"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on an M4 Pro with DXMT on the default engine (r28) in a 5 minute session. The game also has a native Mac version on Steam."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/akane.json"},
{"id": "alice-madness-returns", "title": "Alice: Madness Returns", "steam": 19680, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-10-10"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\AliceMadnessReturns.exe\\X11 Driver", "name": "EmulateModeset", "valueType": "REG_SZ", "data": "y", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Playable once two things are handled, by udance4ever's report. The game folder held 4,407 macOS '._' metadata files, and the game only ran after they were deleted. DXSETUP shows errors on the first start only and can be dismissed. Clicking in the game switched the resolution so only a quarter of the picture showed, and Emulate display mode changes on the game's page stops that, so the mouse works too (confirmed by the reporter, 2026-10-23). Once in game it ran perfectly. Turn Steam Input on for a controller.", "Clicking in the game switched the resolution so only a quarter of the picture showed (highball-db#429, Apple M1, macOS 27.0.1). With EmulateModeset for AliceMadnessReturns.exe, Wine emulates the game's display mode changes instead of switching the Mac's display, and the reporter could play with the mouse again. It is the same setting as Emulate display mode changes on the game's page. Scoped to the game's executable; nothing else in the environment changes."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The game fails until thousands of '._' files are deleted from its folder", "cause": "the folder held 4,407 '._' files, the kind macOS writes beside files on drives not formatted for a Mac (here an exFAT drive holding the Steam library), and the game trips over them. A reinstall brings them back. Highball 0.10.20 removed them only from the engines it installs", "fix": "from the next Highball version, Play removes them from the game's folder before each launch when the folder is on such a drive (highball#457). Until then delete every file whose name starts with '._' in the game's folder, for example with find in Terminal from the steamapps/common folder: find 'Alice Madness Returns' -name '._*' -delete"}, {"symptom": "DXSETUP.exe shows errors on the first start", "cause": "the DirectX setup the game runs once", "fix": "dismiss them, they do not come back"}, {"symptom": "Clicking in the game switches the resolution so only a quarter of the picture shows (reported on an M1, macOS 27.0.1, D3DMetal environment, highball-db#429)", "cause": "the game changes the display mode when clicked. Not measured further", "fix": "turn on Emulate display mode changes on the game's page (or EmulateModeset=y for AliceMadnessReturns.exe by hand), confirmed by the reporter. The game's recipe sets it from the next Highball version. Playing with a gamepad also avoids it"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/alice-madness-returns.json"},
