{"id": "american-truck-simulator", "title": "American Truck Simulator", "steam": 270880, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-09-27"}, "nativeMac": true, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable on DXMT on the Wine 11 engine r4. Two issues reported: Quit Game freezes the screen and the game has to be closed from Highball, and a custom ESP32 Bluetooth controller is not recognised. Nothing was measured here. The game has a native Mac version on Steam as well. A second reporter (highball-db#288, 2026-10-03, Apple M1, macOS 27.0.1, Highball 0.10.3) has it and Euro Truck Simulator 2 fail to start on the Wine 11 engine r15 in DXMT mode while the default engine starts both on the same Mac, see the known issue. The same reporter then confirmed both run on the Wine 11 engine r16 from the 0.10.4 beta, with faster map loading than the default engine."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Quit Game freezes the screen instead of exiting (reported on an M4, DXMT, engine x64-crossover26.3-r4).", "cause": "not measured.", "fix": "close the game from Highball. Not yet tried on the current engines."}, {"symptom": "A custom ESP32 Bluetooth game controller is not recognised (reported on an M4).", "cause": "not measured. A controller Wine's raw HID path does not map is the case the SDL driver handles.", "fix": "worth trying the dependency \"Controllers through SDL\" (recipe controller-sdl), then restart the environment. Not verified for this controller."}, {"symptom": "On the Wine 11 engine r15 in DXMT mode the game does not start, Euro Truck Simulator 2 the same, while the default engine starts both on the same Mac (reported on an M1, macOS 27.0.1, Highball 0.10.3, highball-db#288).", "cause": "The DXMT build the Wine 11 engine carried from r11 to r15 built its clear pipelines before the Metal device they read was set up and could crash at start-up. The default engine lost it in 0.10.1 and the Wine 11 engine in r16. Confirmed by the reporter's r16 run rather than measured here.", "fix": "Confirmed fixed by the same reporter on the Wine 11 engine r16 (Highball 0.10.4 beta, 2026-10-03): both games start, and the maps load faster there than on the default engine. Pick r16 on the game's Full page under Advanced, Engine."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/american-truck-simulator.json"},
{"id": "among-us", "title": "Among Us", "steam": 945360, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 6, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-02"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on DXMT on the default engine, a short session. Online play is the whole game and the reporter did not say whether a lobby was joined. Measured on an M4 with macOS 27.0 on 2026-09-30, DXMT, the first menus only (age check and sign-in screen), not played. On engine r13 the current 64-bit build often closed by itself right after starting on DXMT, which engine r15 fixes, see known issues. A 57-minute session on an M4 rated it playable, the one flaw being lost input after switching to another app, the focus fault that engine r15 fixes. Checked here on 2026-10-05 on an M4 with engine r21 (DEP kept on), DXMT: the main menu comes up with the age verification dialog at 90 s; not played past it."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Closes by itself within two seconds of starting on DXMT, often. On an M4 with macOS 27.0 that happened in 8 of 12 launches on engine r13", "cause": "A bug in DXMT (also upstream, 3Shain/dxmt#219): it created its first Metal pipelines before its Metal device was set, so the game died on a garbage object. Measured on an M4 with macOS 27.0: 0 of 12 launches failed with the fixed DXMT, 0 of 6 with engine r5's older DXMT, and 0 of 8 on DXVK", "fix": "Fixed in engine r15, which environments on the default engine pick up by themselves once Steam is closed. Until then, press Play again, or set this game's graphics mode to DXVK"}, {"symptom": "After switching to another app and back, the game keeps drawing but ignores clicks and keys until it is restarted", "cause": "Wine 10's Mac driver sent the game a made-up click in its title bar whenever macOS gave it focus back, and Unity ignores the focus gain that follows such a click, so it keeps drawing but drops every click and key (Wine bug 48121, highball#182). Measured on an M4 with macOS 27.0: after Cmd+Tab the age check took no clicks on engine r13 and takes them on r15", "fix": "Fixed in engine r15, which environments on the default engine pick up by themselves once Steam is closed. On an older engine, restart the game."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/among-us.json"},
