{"id": "aperture-desk-job", "title": "Aperture Desk Job", "steam": 1902490, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxvk"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-08-23"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Re-verified on engine r2 on 2026-09-10: the Valve logo, the office scene and the Start/Options/Quit menu all render on DXVK at 30.8 fps, GPU bound at 29 ms per frame. The game puts up a 'Controller Required' banner and needs a gamepad to actually play, which is the game's own requirement. It also shows a 'This game has been optimized for play on the Steam Deck' notice on first run that has to be dismissed. DXVK is the verified renderer: office scene renders clean, ~40 fps, ReShade 6.8.0 works on top (re-verified 2026-08-25). On our macOS 14 test machine the other renderers misbehave with current builds: DXMT 0.80 black screen (it targets macOS 15+), D3DMetal severe texture corruption (GPU identity keys and ReShade ruled out by A/B). On macOS 15+ your results may differ. Checked here on 2026-10-05 on an M4 with engine r21, DXVK: Steam stops at its \"Grab your controller!\" dialog before the game, so a controller is needed to get further; not an engine matter.", "Free Valve title, Source 2, D3D11, steam appid 1902490. Needs a game controller for actual play (menu works with keyboard)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Black screen with DXMT 0.80 (frames present at ~48 fps but nothing rendered; -sw windowed does not help)", "cause": "DXMT + Source 2 presentation issue on this engine", "fix": "use dxvk (correct) or d3dmetal (fast but corrupted)"}, {"symptom": "Severe block-pattern texture corruption with D3DMetal 3.0 (menu and world visible, ~38-44 fps)", "cause": "unknown; D3DMetal + Source 2 on Wine 10 Sikarugir engine", "fix": "use dxvk"}], "verified": {"date": "2026-08-23", "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r0", "chip": "Apple M1 Pro"}, "source": "db/games/aperture-desk-job.json"},
