{"id": "armored-core-vi", "title": "Armored Core VI", "steam": 1888160, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["Easy Anti-Cheat"], "verdict": "warning"}, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-03"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["reported working via GPTK-class stacks. Reported playable on an M1 Pro with D3DMetal, offline with Easy Anti-Cheat skipped, borderless at 1440x810 on low settings. The first launch needs a lower macOS resolution to get through, see the known issues."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The first launch crashes to a black screen and Wine's debugger when GraphicsConfig.xml doesn't exist yet and macOS is at 1800x1169, with 'MTLTextureDescriptor has width of zero' in the log (M1 Pro, D3DMetal, Wine 10 r28)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "set the Mac's display to 1512x982 for the first launch, so the game writes GraphicsConfig.xml, then go back to 1800x1169. Later launches use the saved file (highball-db#948)"}, {"symptom": "Switching between borderless and fullscreen, or changing the resolution in the game, sometimes crashes or freezes it, and the picture can sit offset with unused space around it", "cause": "not diagnosed. The log shows Wine refusing a display mode change (ChangeDisplaySettings returned -2)", "fix": "none known. Emulate display mode changes did not reliably help the reporter"}, {"symptom": "Played only without its anti-cheat, started offline with the exe renamed so Easy Anti-Cheat is skipped, so online play is unavailable", "cause": "Easy Anti-Cheat. Its support for Proton on Linux doesn't extend to Wine on a Mac.", "fix": "none for online play"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/armored-core-vi.json"},
