{"id": "assassins-creed", "title": "Assassin's Creed", "steam": 15100, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 2, "last": "2026-11-02"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays in one report on an M1 on the Wine 11 engine r30 with athei's x87sidecar switched on (HB_X87SIDECAR=1 in the environment's variables, Highball 0.10.26) and DXVK, at about 40 fps (highball-db#901). Without the sidecar the title screen ran at about 7 fps, and D3DMetal crashed on the way in. Choose the controller in the game's settings at every start. It's a 32-bit game."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The title screen stutters at about 7 fps and the game crashes on the way in (M1, Wine 11 r28, D3DMetal)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "put the environment on the Wine 11 engine r30 or r31, add HB_X87SIDECAR=1 to its variables and use DXVK. The game is then snappy at about 40 fps on an M1 (highball-db#901, 2026-11-06, credit udance4ever). On DXVK it doesn't crash"}, {"symptom": "The opening logo plays in slow motion on the Wine 10 engine", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "the Wine 11 engine plays it normally"}, {"symptom": "No controller input until a controller is chosen in the game's settings, at every start. On a DualSense RT isn't recognized", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "with the mouse, open the game's controller settings and scroll to Xbox 360 controller, then apply. On a DualSense map High Profile to RB, Action Camera to L3 and Center Camera to R3 (highball-db#901, credit udance4ever, from a Steam community discussion). EaglePatch through the Ultimate ASI Loader loads under Wine with dinput8=n,b in the environment's DLL overrides (log, highball-db#901, 2026-11-07), but it didn't change the controller for the reporter (highball-db#901, 2026-11-08)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/assassins-creed.json"},
{"id": "assassins-creed-brotherhood", "title": "Assassin's Creed Brotherhood", "steam": 48190, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-22"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable over two hours on an M1 with the default engine and DXMT, at 1680x1050 with the game's default settings, with freezes in some cutscenes. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Freezes in some cutscenes (reported on an M1, macOS 26.6.2, DXMT, engine r28)", "cause": "not measured", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/assassins-creed-brotherhood.json"},
{"id": "assassins-creed-ii", "title": "Assassin's Creed II", "steam": 33230, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-17"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["A Direct3D 9 game. Reported playable on an M4 Pro with the Ubisoft Connect copy, DXVK and msync on the Wine 11 engine r31. Switching away from the game in fullscreen crashes it, so save first and don't use Cmd+Tab while playing. The environment Highball sets up for Ubisoft Connect uses DXMT with sync off, which lagged in this game until the player switched it to DXVK and msync."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Switching away with Cmd+Tab in fullscreen crashes the game (M4 Pro, Wine 11 r31, DXVK, highball-db#1284)", "cause": "the game resizes its render targets to the minimized window's size, per the player. The DXVK log shows a texture of 4294935456x4294935327", "fix": "don't switch away while playing, save first, and turn on Do Not Disturb so nothing takes focus. DXVK_FORCE_WINDOWED=1 forces a window, but the game doesn't resize it"}, {"symptom": "Laggy in the environment Highball sets up for Ubisoft Connect, which uses DXMT with sync off (M4 Pro, Wine 11 r31, highball-db#1284)", "cause": "DXMT has no Direct3D 9, so the game falls back to Wine's own Direct3D, per the player, and sync off made it worse", "fix": "set the environment to DXVK and msync, as the reporter did"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/assassins-creed-ii.json"},
{"id": "assassins-creed-syndicate", "title": "Assassin's Creed Syndicate", "steam": 368500, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-03"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on an M4 with DXMT over 7 minutes, on the Wine 11 engine (r27) with AVX advertised and a 60 fps cap. Whether AVX is needed is not known."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/assassins-creed-syndicate.json"},
{"id": "assetto-corsa", "title": "Assetto Corsa", "steam": 244210, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-09"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": ["dotnet48"], "steps": [{"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\acs.exe\\DllOverrides", "name": "dwrite", "valueType": "REG_SZ", "data": "native,builtin", "platforms": ["mac"]}, {"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\acs_x86.exe\\DllOverrides", "name": "dwrite", "valueType": "REG_SZ", "data": "native,builtin", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Works end to end with two things in place: install the .NET Framework 4.8 dependency first (bottle settings → Dependencies; took 6 minutes here on 2026-09-02, can take 20-40 and looks frozen — let it finish), and use the D3DMetal renderer. The stock launcher is a 32-bit .NET/WPF app: without .NET it dies silently, which was the long-standing 'AC won't launch' failure (re-confirmed 2026-09-02: on a bottle whose registry claimed 4.8 but only had Wine Mono, the launcher died with a Mono TypeLoadException on CEF3; after the real dotnet48 install it rendered fully). Re-verified on macOS 26.6.2, 2026-09-02, D3DMetal: launcher intro movie and main menu render, a practice session (Ferrari 458 at Laguna Seca) loads and runs at 127-128 fps at 1728x1117 (Metal HUD). On macOS 14.6 (2026-08-28) sessions ran at 150-170 fps fullscreen with a clean exit. DXMT: on macOS 14.6 it black-screened the session (engine runs, never paints); on macOS 26.6.2 (2026-09-02) the same session rendered and drove under DXMT 0.80 at 69-136 fps, so the black screen looks tied to the older OS. If you get a black screen on session start, switch the bottle to D3DMetal, stop all bottle processes, and relaunch. Launcher news panels may spin forever; cosmetic. Re-checked on 2026-10-05 on an M4 with engine r21 (DEP kept on): without .NET 4.8 the launcher dies on Mono's CEF3 load as described; the recipe installs .NET 4.8 and the launcher then opens on its language screen. No session was driven in that run. A player on an M1 Max reached 136 fps in the benchmark at 2560x1440 (highball#241) after a long road: what worked was a fresh environment on the default Wine 10 engine, D3DMetal for the game, Stop all processes, then .NET Framework 4.8 from Windows components with nothing else running, then Play from Highball. An environment first set up on the Wine 11 engine did not recover, and with a scaled second display Steam's window only appeared once that display was unplugged (highball#241, being fixed). A 42 minute report on an M1 with the game's recipe rates it perfect on DXMT (highball-db#1112).", "Before first launch, install .NET Framework 4.8 from the bottle's Dependencies section (20 to 40 minutes; looks frozen for long stretches, let it finish). AC's launcher is a 32-bit .NET/WPF app and dies silently without it — this was the historical 'AC won't launch' failure.", "Use D3DMetal. Under DXMT the session loads and the engine runs (physics ticks, log fills) but nothing ever paints — black screen after clicking start. Verified on this engine 2026-08-28.", "The launcher's news panels can spin forever (embedded Chromium fetching old feeds). Cosmetic — Drive, Career and settings all work.", "Custom Shaders Patch, if you install it through Content Manager, hooks the game through a dwrite.dll it drops next to acs.exe. Wine prefers its own dwrite unless told otherwise, so this setup lets the game's copy load first, for acs.exe only (nothing changes for a game without CSP, Wine's own dwrite is used as before). CSP then wants Windows fonts its config names, Segoe UI, Consolas and Orbitron among them, which an environment does not have and Highball cannot ship. Put them in the environment's C:\\windows\\Fonts folder (a Windows install or the community font pack has them). Without them the session crashes at start with CSP on. Measured by a player on an M1 Pro with Highball 0.10.4 (highball#243)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The launcher (AssettoCorsa.exe, .NET/WPF) shows 'Configuration system failed to initialize' and exits; the game itself never starts from Steam's Play.", "cause": "Reproduced 2026-09-04 on M1 Pro / macOS 26.6.2 with .NET 4.8 installed: System.Configuration rejects machine.config line 6 ('Section names beginning with config are reserved', the standard configProtectedData section) — a .NET-configuration-init-under-Wine failure affecting every .NET app in that bottle; machine.config itself is valid. Engine-independent (same on Wine 10 and our Wine 11 build).", "fix": "The game binary works: launching acs.exe directly (with steam_appid.txt = 244210, Steam running, D3DMetal) starts the sim. A launcher-bypass pin is the practical route until the .NET config init is fixed."}, {"symptom": "acs.exe exits immediately with no error and no log when started directly.", "cause": "the game needs Steam's app identity, which Steam sets when you press Play. Without SteamAppId=244210 in the environment it quits before it initialises anything, which looks like a broken game rather than a missing variable.", "fix": "launch it from Steam, or from Highball's Play, which is what sets it. Only relevant to launching the executable by hand."}, {"symptom": "On D3DMetal the session dies on Start with a Metal assertion, a texture of width and height 4294967295 (reported on a 13-inch M1 with 8 GB, macOS 26.6.2, highball#94)", "cause": "measured from the reporter's video.ini (highball#94): SHADOW_MAP_SIZE=-1, which the launcher writes when Shadows is set to off, becomes a shadow texture of size 4294967295 on D3DMetal and Metal refuses it. Mirror and cubemap SIZE=0 are the same class of value", "fix": "confirmed by the reporter (highball#94): in the launcher's Options, Video set Shadows to Low or higher (SHADOW_MAP_SIZE 1024 or 2048 in cfg/video.ini) and give Mirrors and Reflections a size (512 here), then the session starts on a 13-inch M1 with 8 GB"}, {"symptom": "Black screen when starting a session, menu/launcher fine", "cause": "DXMT on macOS 14.6: AC's D3D11 path ran but never presented on this engine (log shows the run loop ticking with heavy 'WAS LATE' spam). Not reproduced on macOS 26.6.2, where DXMT renders the session.", "fix": "set the bottle renderer to d3dmetal and restart the bottle (Stop all processes first — a running Steam session keeps the old renderer)"}, {"symptom": "Launcher never appears / game won't start at all", "cause": "missing .NET Framework: the stock launcher is 32-bit .NET 4 WPF and Wine-Mono has no WPF", "fix": "install the dotnet48 dependency, then launch normally through Steam"}, {"symptom": "With Custom Shaders Patch installed, its apps (Pure, Pure Planner) never appear, or the session crashes at start (reported on an M1 Pro, Highball 0.10.4, highball#243)", "cause": "Wine loads its own dwrite ahead of the dwrite.dll CSP drops in the game folder, so CSP never hooks the game. Once it does load, it asks for Windows fonts the environment lacks and crashes without them.", "fix": "The setup now sets dwrite to native,builtin for acs.exe. Add the fonts CSP names (Segoe UI, Consolas, Orbitron) to the environment's C:\\windows\\Fonts, then Stop All Windows Processes and start a session."}], "verified": {"date": "2026-09-02", "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r0", "chip": "Apple M1 Pro"}, "source": "db/games/assetto-corsa.json"},
