{"id": "beamng-drive", "title": "BeamNG.drive", "steam": 284160, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 12, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-12"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable at 40-60 fps on an Apple M4 with the bottle set to D3DMetal, installed through Steam inside the bottle and launched from Highball. No workarounds, launch options or DLL overrides were needed. BeamNG probes for Direct3D 12, finds no usable device and falls back to Direct3D 11 on its own, so it does not depend on the D3D12-only path. Reported on Highball 0.7.14 with game Alpha v0.39.4, windowed at 1470x934, 6 GB reported to the game as video memory. DXMT is untested on this hardware: the earlier DXMT note came from the DXMT changelog rather than a run. A second, short report on an M5 with DXMT rates it playable, with the laptop heating up at once and story mode unable to generate a seed. On D3DMetal the game now picks DirectX 12, where the terrain does not load (highball-db#474), so Play passes -gfx dx11 to keep it on DirectX 11. Frame spikes come from the CPU side under Rosetta rather than the GPU. With more than one vehicle on the map performance drops even at the lowest settings on an M4 (highball-db#508). On a base M4 a player gets 40 fps at low settings with 80% resolution scaling (highball-db#1140). On an M5 with the Wine 11 engine r30 and D3DMetal it held 60 fps with occasional drops at low details over 26 minutes (highball-db#1169)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Story mode cannot generate a seed", "cause": "reported once (DXMT, M5, engine r19), not diagnosed", "fix": "none known yet (highball-db#329)"}, {"symptom": "Stuck on the loading screen while it enables the UI, in DXVK mode (M4 Mac mini, highball#521)", "cause": "assumed: BeamNG draws its menus with a built-in browser in a separate process, and DXVK on the Mac cannot share that picture with the game (MoltenVK has no Windows external memory). Not measured", "fix": "set the game's mode to DXMT (most reports) or D3DMetal under Game settings"}, {"symptom": "Some of the game's preset keys aren't mapped properly (M5 Pro, Wine 10 r28)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/beamng-drive.json"},
