{"id": "binary-domain", "title": "Binary Domain", "steam": 203750, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 1, "last": "2026-10-05"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Gets in game with high frame rates once its configuration tool and the game run the same way, and the sound is broken. The game stores the graphics card's ID from BinaryDomainConfiguration.exe and refuses to start when the game sees another one. On the default engine in D3DMetal or DXVK mode a Direct3D 9 game sees the Mac's chip with an ID that stays the same from run to run, while Wine's own Direct3D and the Wine 11 engine show a different card (measured on an M4, 2026-10-05). The player added the configuration tool to the environment's programs so both run in the same mode. The CRI audio middleware loads XAudio 2.7, which the Linux fix replaces with Microsoft's own; the 'Microsoft XAudio 2.7 and XACT' dependency does that here, and on Binary Domain it did not stop the stutter (the player still hears and sees it, 0.10.9). Highball's limiter in the 0.10.15 engines did not change the stutter either, so it is not clipping (highball-db#345)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "'Critical Error! Graphics device is invalid, please run the configuration tool' and the game quits", "cause": "The configuration tool saved a graphics card ID that differs from the one the game sees, after a change of graphics mode or engine", "fix": "Run BinaryDomainConfiguration.exe from the game folder in the same environment and mode as the game (adding it to the environment's programs keeps it there), save, then start the game"}, {"symptom": "Sound and picture stutter together in game", "cause": "Not diagnosed. Microsoft's XAudio 2.7 (the Linux fix for this game's CRI audio) did not change it here (highball-db#345, 0.10.9). Sound and picture stuttering together points at the CPU side of a 2012 32-bit game under Rosetta rather than at audio. Highball's limiter in the 0.10.15 engines did not change it either, so it is not clipping (highball-db#345, 2026-10-12)", "fix": "None known yet. DXVK async shader compilation in the environment's Graphics settings removes only the stutter of shaders compiling for the first time"}, {"symptom": "The picture spans the external monitor and the laptop screen", "cause": "The game's default display setting", "fix": "Set 1920x1080 and Windowed in the game's options"}, {"symptom": "A controller works in menus but not in play", "cause": "Steam Input sits between the controller and the game's XInput path (the same on Linux)", "fix": "Turn Steam Input off for the game in its Steam properties"}, {"symptom": "A 'Microsoft .NET Framework 3.5 Setup' error box ('You must use Turn Windows features on or off...') behind Steam's 'Setup is loading installation components', at every start", "cause": "Steam runs the game's first-start step, which installs .NET 3.5 from Steam's redistributables, before each launch, and Microsoft's 3.5 installer refuses to run on the Windows 10 that Wine reports (screenshot in highball-db#345). Installing dotnet35sp1 with winetricks did not silence it for the reporter", "fix": "harmless: press OK and the game starts"}, {"symptom": "Controller button hints show as plain black squares", "cause": "Not diagnosed", "fix": "None known yet (highball-db#345)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/binary-domain.json"},
{"id": "bionic-commando-rearmed", "title": "Bionic Commando: Rearmed", "steam": 21680, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-26"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": ["physx"], "steps": [], "notes": ["Runs once NVIDIA's PhysX System Software is in the environment, which the recipe now installs (the reporter of highball#375 and #428 confirmed it on an M2 Max, 2026-10-26). Without it the game crashed on launch on DXVK and on Wine's own Direct3D alike: it starts a second copy of itself, loads PhysX's loader and cooking DLLs from its folder but never PhysXCore, and raises its own fatal error. Nothing was measured here.", "The game loads NVIDIA's PhysX through its own loader and needs the PhysX System Software, which Windows players get from NVIDIA's drivers. Without it the game raises its own fatal error right after starting. With the PhysX component installed it runs (confirmed by the reporter of highball#375 and #428, 2026-10-26). Nothing else in the environment changes."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crash on launch, on DXVK and on Wine's own Direct3D alike (highball#375)", "cause": "NVIDIA's PhysX System Software missing from the environment: PhysXCore never loads (confirmed by the fix)", "fix": "the recipe installs the PhysX component (Highball's Windows components, from the version after 0.10.22). By hand now, NVIDIA's PhysX_9.23.1019_SystemSoftware.exe run with Run a Windows program in the environment"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/bionic-commando-rearmed.json"},
