{"id": "black-desert", "title": "Black Desert", "steam": 582660, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["XIGNCODE3"], "verdict": "warning"}, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-16"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on an Apple M6 with DXMT as the game's own mode on the default engine (r28): about 230 fps in a grind zone at 2560x1440 uncapped, with the game in Full Screen Window, read from the Metal HUD. The player logged in and played online. On DXMT the game's launcher opens as a blank grey window until two lines in Documents/Black Desert/GameOptionLauncher.txt are set to 0, see the known issues. DXVK plays too but much slower. On DXMT leave the frame rate uncapped, a 120 cap held only 90 on a 180 Hz display."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The game's launcher (BlackDesertPatcher32.pae) opens as a blank grey window on DXMT (Apple M6, Wine 10 r28, highball-db#1271)", "cause": "the launcher is Chromium based and draws through another process's window, which DXMT refuses here: its log says 'cross-process swapchain not supported yet'", "fix": "with the launcher closed, set launcherGpu = 0 and launcherOffScreen = 0 in Documents/Black Desert/GameOptionLauncher.txt. The launcher then draws on DXMT and DXVK and keeps the values (highball-db#1271). DXMT_ALLOW_CROSS_PROCESS_SWAPCHAIN=1 wasn't tested"}, {"symptom": "With a 120 fps cap on DXMT the game holds 90 fps on a 180 Hz display (Apple M6, Wine 10 r28, highball-db#1271)", "cause": "not confirmed. The reporter's guess is that DXMT's limiter only holds rates that divide the refresh rate. DXVK holds 120 with the same cap", "fix": "leave the frame rate uncapped, which gave about 230 fps"}, {"symptom": "A change to the frame rate cap doesn't reach the game while Steam is still running in the environment (Apple M6, highball-db#1271)", "cause": "the running Steam starts the game, which inherits Steam's environment from before the change", "fix": "quit Steam in the environment, then press Play"}, {"symptom": "On DXVK the game is much slower (high 90s fps against about 230 on DXMT), and in Full Screen Window it rebuilds its swap chain about 80 times a second, growing blackdesert64_d3d11.log by about 10 MB a session (Apple M6, Wine 10 r28, highball-db#1271)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "use DXMT. On DXVK the game's Game Window mode stops the rebuilds"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/black-desert.json"},
{"id": "black-mesa", "title": "Black Mesa", "steam": 362890, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays on the Wine 11 engine for the one player so far (M5 Pro, macOS 27.2) in Wine's own Direct3D, DXMT or Apple's DirectX 12 support, with some frame drops in heavy scenes, and the recipe makes Play offer that engine. The game needs -oldgameui to start, which Play passes. On the default engine it runs at 5 to 10 fps on Wine's own Direct3D and crashes at the loading screen in every other mode. DXVK crashes at the loading screen on both engines. Nothing was measured here.", "Asks for the Wine 11 engine r27 or newer. On the default engine a player on an M5 Pro got 5 to 10 fps on Wine's own Direct3D and a crash at the loading screen in every other mode. On the Wine 11 engine the same player plays it in Wine's own Direct3D, DXMT or Apple's DirectX 12 support, with some frame drops in heavy scenes (highball#385, 2026-10-25). DXVK crashes at the loading screen on both engines, so pick another mode if the environment is set to DXVK. Play passes -oldgameui, which the game needs to start. Everything installed in the environment stays."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crash at the loading screen, or the GPU device lost (MoltenVK Internal Error 0000010d), on DXVK", "cause": "not diagnosed here; the same Metal error came from Source's HDR exposure pass in Portal 2, and its fix there (mat_tonemapping_occlusion_use_stencil 1) gave Black Mesa visual glitches", "fix": "play in Wine's own Direct3D, DXMT or Apple's DirectX 12 support on the Wine 11 engine"}, {"symptom": "5 to 10 fps on Wine's own Direct3D and a crash at the loading screen in every other mode, on the default engine", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "the Wine 11 engine the recipe offers on Play (r27 or newer), or by hand on the environment's full page, Advanced, Engine"}, {"symptom": "The game does not start without -oldgameui", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "Play passes -oldgameui"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/black-mesa.json"},
