{"id": "bleach-brave-souls", "title": "BLEACH Brave Souls", "steam": 1201240, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-05"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable on D3DMetal (free to play). After the logo the intro video stays black while its audio plays; it can be skipped after a few seconds, and the game does not play it again after the first start. It is a port of the mobile game, so some dialogs need the mouse even though a controller works in play."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The intro video after the logo is black while its audio plays", "cause": "Not diagnosed. A game video played through Windows Media Foundation is the usual cause of picture-less video under Wine", "fix": "Skip it after a few seconds. It only plays on the first start (highball-db#342)"}, {"symptom": "Some dialogs ignore the controller", "cause": "The game is a mobile port that expects a touch, which the mouse stands in for", "fix": "Click those dialogs with the mouse"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/bleach-brave-souls.json"},
{"id": "blood-bowl-3", "title": "Blood Bowl 3", "steam": 1016950, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable on DXMT after a 40-minute session on an M3 with the steam and vcrun2022 recipes. The reporter gave 4 of 5 without saying what was less than perfect. No frame rate was given and nothing was measured here. An M2 rated it playable over 80 minutes of matches with DXMT on the default engine (r28), with some lag now and then and some videos showing only a black screen (highball-db#1263)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Some videos show a black screen and have to be skipped (M2, DXMT, Wine 10 r28, highball-db#1263)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "skip them"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/blood-bowl-3.json"},
{"id": "bloodbreaker-labyrinth-of-the-witch-demo", "title": "Bloodbreaker: Labyrinth of the Witch Demo", "steam": 3649940, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-05"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable on D3DMetal, where four GameMaker error boxes come up before the game starts and the game plays after OK on each. On an M4 the demo started on DXMT went straight to its Choose a Language screen with no box, while D3DMetal stopped at the first box, so DXMT is the mode to use. The game itself was not played here. The full game is a separate Steam app (3530380), not tested."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Four boxes saying 'Win32 function failed: HRESULT 0x80070057' from GR_D3D_Device->CheckMultisampleQualityLevels before the game starts", "cause": "The game is made with GameMaker, whose runner shows every failed graphics query in a box. Asked for 8 or more samples, D3DMetal answers Direct3D 11's multisample quality query with E_INVALIDARG, where Windows, DXMT and DXVK answer success with zero quality levels (measured on an M4 with engine r21, 2026-10-05)", "fix": "Set the game to DXMT on its page, which goes straight to the game (seen on an M4). On D3DMetal, press OK on each box and the game starts and plays (highball-db#343)"}], "verified": {"date": "2026-10-06", "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r21", "chip": "Apple M4"}, "source": "db/games/bloodbreaker-labyrinth-of-the-witch-demo.json"},
{"id": "bloody-spell", "title": "Bloody Spell", "steam": 992300, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-10-04"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": ["corefonts"], "steps": [{"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\BloodySpell.exe\\DllOverrides", "name": "mfplat", "valueType": "REG_SZ", "data": "", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Playable with the recipe. Reaches play on D3DMetal on the default engine, about 28 fps at 1920x1080 on an M1 in the reporter's screenshot. Without the recipe its videos freeze it a few seconds in (the opening one, the one after the difficulty selection), on every graphics mode, with Wine's media pipeline deadlocked in the log. The recipe turns Media Foundation off for BloodySpell.exe only: the reporter then saw the intro play and got in game. It also installs Microsoft's core fonts, which the title screen's text needs. A DualSense controller was read without Steam Input on one run and only with it on the next.", "The game's videos (the opening one and the one after the difficulty selection) freeze it a few seconds in: Wine's media pipeline deadlocks on them, on every graphics mode. With Media Foundation's platform library disabled for BloodySpell.exe only, the game no longer hangs, the intro still plays, and it goes in game (confirmed by the reporter of highball-db#316 with the same override set by hand). Microsoft's core fonts come along because the title screen's text does not render without them. Nothing else in the environment changes."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Title screen text missing", "cause": "the game's fonts fall back to ones the environment does not ship", "fix": "Microsoft's core fonts, which the recipe installs"}, {"symptom": "Freezes a few seconds into a video (the opening one, or the one after the difficulty selection), on every graphics mode", "cause": "the video deadlocks Wine's media pipeline (GStreamer caps assertion, then winegstreamer's media_source critical section waiting forever)", "fix": "the recipe turns Media Foundation off for BloodySpell.exe (confirmed by the reporter, highball-db#316)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/bloody-spell.json"},
