{"id": "company-of-heroes-3", "title": "Company of Heroes 3", "steam": 1677280, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 3, "last": "2026-10-22"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Single-player plays on the Wine 10 engine with D3DMetal, about 50 fps on the Metal HUD at 2560x1440 in the campaign, after a manual fix for a start-up crash. Multiplayer needs Microsoft's ucrtbase.dll: with Wine's own, matches desync. Both fixes are by hand for now; Highball's recipes cannot yet move or copy a game's own files. The reporter found the Wine 11 engine (r19) desyncs the same way, and Steam's window draws black there with Microsoft's ucrtbase, so stay on the Wine 10 engine. A second player on an M5 got it running with the same ucrtbase steps, Advertise AVX, Automatic graphics (D3DMetal for the game) and Synchronization set to None, which cleared a black-screen freeze for them (highball-db#631)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crash at start-up", "cause": "the game folder ships ucrtbase.dll and msvcrt.dll; Wine registers its builtin C runtime under the game folder's path and GetModuleHandle(\"api-ms-win-crt-heap-l1-1-0.dll\") returns NULL (reporter's analysis). A DLL override does not help", "fix": "move ucrtbase.dll and msvcrt.dll out of the game folder, for example into a backup folder inside it; redo after a game update or a file check"}, {"symptom": "Multiplayer: \"Sync error detected\" about 26 seconds into a match", "cause": "Wine's builtin ucrtbase math differs from Microsoft's, so the lockstep simulation drifts (reporter's analysis; a replay of a Windows match then plays to the end)", "fix": "copy the game's Microsoft ucrtbase.dll (x86-64) into drive_c/windows/system32 after backing up Wine's, and add the DLL override ucrtbase=n. A live online match was not tested yet"}, {"symptom": "Crash when leaving a multiplayer match", "cause": "Steam's overlay", "fix": "disable the overlay, for example with the DLL override gameoverlayrenderer64="}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/company-of-heroes-3.json"},
{"id": "conarium", "title": "Conarium", "steam": 313780, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-01"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on an M1 with D3DMetal."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "DualSense controller not recognized by the game (an Xbox style XInput pad works)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "use an XInput pad, or start the game through Steam with Steam Input on (a non-Steam shortcut in the environment's Steam)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/conarium.json"},
