{"id": "csgo-legacy", "title": "Counter-Strike: Global Offensive (Legacy)", "steam": 4465480, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["VAC"], "verdict": "warning"}, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-31"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\csgo.exe\\DllOverrides", "name": "d3d9", "valueType": "REG_SZ", "data": "n,b", "platforms": ["mac"]}, {"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\csgo.exe\\Direct3D", "name": "VideoPciVendorID", "valueType": "REG_DWORD", "data": "4318", "platforms": ["mac"]}, {"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\csgo.exe\\Direct3D", "name": "VideoPciDeviceID", "valueType": "REG_DWORD", "data": "7040", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Plays on macOS 26 with engine x64-crossover26.3-r7 or later and the csgo-legacy recipe: the game alone gets the engine's wined3d Direct3D 9 (a native d3d9.dll in its bin folder, taken first for csgo.exe) and an NVIDIA identity; r7 carries the 32-bit NVAPI stub the game then needs. The environment stays on DXMT, so Steam and every other game are untouched. 17 fps at 1728x1117 with the defaults on an M1 Pro, so lower the resolution or the settings. Why this route: on DXVK's Direct3D 9 the map load on macOS 26 either loses the GPU device on Source's HDR pass (highball#34) or never finishes after the console reaches INGAME, and on the Wine 10 engine it freezes in a lost wake-up; wined3d (CodeWeavers' Direct3D 9 on OpenGL, the route CrossOver users take) has none of those, and it fails Source's shadow-map check only with an AMD identity. History: NVAPI 0xFFFFFFFE with any non-AMD identity was a dead end while the stub was placed beside the game; NVIDIA's SDK loads nvapi.dll from the system directory only. After moving a bottle to r7, Repair it once so the stub's placeholder is written. On macOS 14 and 15 the game also runs on DXVK's Direct3D 9 (verified 2026-09-02 on the Wine 10 engine). Cold check 2026-09-11 on Highball 0.9.7 (M1 Pro, macOS 26.6.2, engine r7): the game deleted and downloaded again by Steam launched from Play, which put the d3d9.dll back and started it on wined3d with the NVAPI stub loaded; it held its 1728x1117 window for three minutes. No round played in that check. Re-checked on 2026-10-05 on an M4 with macOS 27.0 and the Wine 11 engine r15: with the recipe applied the game loads de_dust2 straight from +map and plays the round (console INGAME); without it, the CSM check error with the AMD identity.", "Needs engine x64-crossover26.3-r7 or later. The game gets the engine's own Direct3D 9 (wined3d, on OpenGL) as a d3d9.dll in its bin folder, loaded first for csgo.exe only, so this one game runs on wined3d while the environment and the Steam client keep their graphics mode. On DXVK's Direct3D 9 the map load on macOS 26 either loses the GPU device on Source's HDR pass or never finishes.", "The two registry values give csgo.exe alone an NVIDIA identity (GeForce GTX 1080, 0x10de:0x1b80). Source's shadow-map check passes on NVIDIA's depth-texture path, which wined3d supports, and fails on AMD's, which it does not. With an NVIDIA identity the game insists on NVIDIA's driver library, which r7's engine answers with a stub. Other programs in the bottle keep Highball's AMD identity.", "Legacy CS:GO is Valve's free standalone app 4465480; Highball launches it directly. The Metal HUD does not show on this game because OpenGL presents the frames, so use the game's own cl_showfps or net_graph for a frame rate."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "On DXVK's Direct3D 9 (the default graphics mode) on macOS 26: the map load stops at 'Initializing game data', or the screen goes black at the end of the load.", "cause": "MoltenVK loses the device on Source's zero-attachment HDR pass (highball#34), and a second stall after INGAME that is not explained.", "fix": "The csgo-legacy recipe on engine r7 or later: wined3d plus an NVIDIA identity for csgo.exe."}, {"symptom": "On the Wine 10 engine (macOS 26): freezes at 'Initializing game data' with the process idle.", "cause": "A lost wake-up in Source's job hand-off, a scheduling-order race macOS 26 exposes (wineserver trace, 2026-09-02).", "fix": "Use engine r7 and the recipe."}, {"symptom": "On the default (DXVK) graphics mode on macOS 26: the map load stops at 'Initializing game data' or the screen goes black at the end of the load.", "cause": "MoltenVK loses the device on Source's zero-attachment HDR pass (highball#34), and a second stall after the console reaches INGAME that is not yet explained.", "fix": "This recipe: wined3d plus the NVIDIA identity for csgo.exe on engine r7."}], "verified": {"date": "2026-09-11", "engine": "x64-crossover26.3-r7", "chip": "Apple M1 Pro"}, "source": "db/games/csgo-legacy.json"},
{"id": "cyberpunk-2077", "title": "Cyberpunk 2077", "steam": 1091500, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-15"}, "nativeMac": true, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "env", "name": "ROSETTA_ADVERTISE_AVX", "value": "1", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Playable. M4: ~17 fps avg, 1920x1200 Steam Deck preset + FSR 2.1. M5: 60-82 fps in gameplay (Metal HUD; the built-in benchmark's summary under-reads because of first-frames shader compilation), fullscreen 1920x1200, FSR 2.1 Balanced, ray-traced local shadows ON. Mandatory: Advertise AVX ON (engine crashes at launch otherwise); Steam launch option --launcher-skip (REDlauncher fails on OpenGL context / libEGL.dll); Steam Overlay OFF (black screen). Fullscreen beats borderless for frame pacing. First runs stutter while shaders compile, then settle. See recipe cyberpunk-2077.", "One manual step: in Steam, right-click Cyberpunk 2077 → Properties → Launch Options, add --launcher-skip. REDlauncher cannot create its OpenGL context under Wine; skipping it costs nothing.", "In the same Properties window, turn the Steam Overlay OFF for this game — it black-screens the launch.", "In-game: keep Ray Tracing OFF (software-translated, ~10 fps). Steam Deck preset + FSR 2.1 is the reported baseline (~17 fps avg on a base M5). First runs stutter while shaders compile; it settles."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Engine crash immediately at launch", "cause": "AVX not advertised through Rosetta", "fix": "this recipe sets ROSETTA_ADVERTISE_AVX=1 on the bottle (same as the Advertise AVX toggle)"}, {"symptom": "REDlauncher error mentioning QSurfaceFormat / libEGL.dll", "cause": "launcher needs an OpenGL context Wine cannot provide", "fix": "add --launcher-skip to the game's Steam launch options"}, {"symptom": "Black screen at launch", "cause": "Steam Overlay hooks", "fix": "disable the Steam Overlay for this game"}, {"symptom": "Slideshow (~10 fps)", "cause": "Ray Tracing enabled", "fix": "turn Ray Tracing off"}], "verified": {"date": "2026-08-24", "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r0", "chip": "Apple M4"}, "source": "db/games/cyberpunk-2077.json"},
{"id": "dark-souls-iii", "title": "Dark Souls III", "steam": 374320, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-25"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["works offline; anti-cheat softban risk online. Direct3D 11. On an M4 Pro DXMT froze the game on every kill and hung macOS's window server; D3DMetal (Apple's DirectX 12 support in the app) plays through kills there, confirmed 2026-09-25 by the reporter, so it is the mode the page recommends. A player on an M5 with the Wine 10 engine r21 rated it playable on DXMT over 38 minutes, and a player on an M1 with the Wine 11 engine r27 rated it perfect on DXMT after about three hours with only minor stutters, so the freeze on kills may not happen on every Mac or engine. The page keeps D3DMetal until more reports agree."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The game freezes when an enemy is killed, then crashes (reported on an M4 Pro, macOS 26.6.2, engine x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r7, DXMT, Highball 0.9.35, highball-db#204, rated 2, launches but not playable).", "cause": "not in the game's log, which ends normally. The file the reporter attached is a WindowServer watchdog stackshot: macOS's window server stopped answering while the game ran (display state OFF at capture), which is the GPU or its driver hanging on the M4 Pro, not a fault inside Wine. Every kill triggers it for the reporter. Not reproduced on the M1 Pro here.", "fix": "use D3DMetal for this game (Apple's DirectX 12 support in the app). Confirmed by the reporter on the M4 Pro: kills no longer freeze it."}, {"symptom": "The game crashes when its settings open (reported on an M5, engine r28, D3DMetal, highball-db#583)", "cause": "not diagnosed. Turning on Emulate display mode changes stopped it, which points at the display mode list the game reads there", "fix": "turn on Emulate display mode changes in the environment's settings, as the reporter did"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/dark-souls-iii.json"},
{"id": "dark-souls-remastered", "title": "Dark Souls: Remastered", "steam": 570940, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-14"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Works offline in the one report, perfect on DXMT after a short session; sustained frame rate and longer play are not recorded yet. Like other FromSoftware titles it has a server-side anti-cheat with a softban risk if played online through Wine, so keep it offline. Steam AppID 570940. A player on a base M5 rated it playable over 41 minutes on the default engine (r28), DXVK by the report: the sky flickered in Blighttown, and it played fine at least up to Ornstein and Smough (highball-db#1219)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The sky flickers in Blighttown (M5, Wine 10 r28, DXVK by the report, highball-db#1219)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/dark-souls-remastered.json"},
{"id": "darkenstein-3d", "title": "Darkenstein 3D", "steam": 2195910, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-24"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported flawless on DXMT on an M5 Pro over 18 minutes. In the reporter's DXVK environment the game crashed at startup, right after Steam's overlay notice, so this page has Play pick DXMT. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The game crashes at startup, after Steam's overlay notice, on DXVK (reported on an M5 Pro, macOS 27.2, engine r29)", "cause": "not known", "fix": "DXMT, which this page picks. In an environment set to DXVK, set Mode for this game to DXMT"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/darkenstein-3d.json"},
{"id": "darkest-dungeon", "title": "Darkest Dungeon", "steam": 262060, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-02"}, "nativeMac": true, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect over an hour on DXMT on the default engine, the Windows build from Epic run through Highball on an M1 Pro. The game also has a native Mac build on Steam, so the Windows build is only needed for a copy without one. No frame rate was given and nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/darkest-dungeon.json"},
{"id": "darksiders-ii-deathinitive-edition", "title": "Darksiders II Deathinitive Edition", "steam": 388410, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-09"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable on an M1 Pro with DXVK, around 60 fps in the areas tested by the Metal HUD at 1800x1169, with sound, controller, saves and resolution changes working and occasional flickering and stuttering. In windowed mode the game sometimes stays on a black screen until its window is dragged by the title bar or minimized and restored, after which the intro videos play, on both the default engine r28 and the Wine 11 engine r27. Fullscreen starts without that, and Emulate display mode changes fixed a wrongly scaled or offset fullscreen picture. A controller has to be connected before the game starts. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "In windowed mode the game sometimes stays on a black screen with no response to keyboard or mouse (reported on an M1 Pro, macOS 26.7, DXVK, engine r28 and the Wine 11 engine r27)", "cause": "not measured. The reporter suspects window state changes or event handling", "fix": "drag the game window by its title bar, or minimize and restore it, and the intro videos start. Starting in fullscreen avoids it"}, {"symptom": "The fullscreen picture is wrongly scaled or positioned (reported on an M1 Pro, macOS 26.7, DXVK, engine r28)", "cause": "not measured", "fix": "turn on Emulate display mode changes in Highball, by the report"}, {"symptom": "A controller connected after the game has started is not picked up (reported on an M1 Pro, macOS 26.7, DXVK, engine r28)", "cause": "not measured", "fix": "connect the controller before starting the game"}, {"symptom": "Occasional flickering and stuttering (reported on an M1 Pro, macOS 26.7, DXVK, engine r28)", "cause": "not measured", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/darksiders-ii-deathinitive-edition.json"},
