{"id": "days-gone", "title": "Days Gone", "steam": 1259420, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-11-10"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays on an M5 Pro with DXMT on the Wine 11 engine r30 at 60 fps once the four intro videos are moved out of BendGame/Content/Movies (highball-db#1139). Steam's Verify files and game updates put them back. Untested here: disabling Media Foundation (mfplat) for DaysGone.exe made other Unreal games skip their videos (Fort Solis), and a DLL override is something a recipe can set. The game has no FSR or DLSS, render scale 80% with a 60 fps cap works best on a 120 Hz display."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Freezes on a still frame at start, with sound playing but the picture never changing (M5 Pro, Wine 11 r30, DXMT)", "cause": "by the reporter's reading of the log, Wine's GStreamer can't play the four H.264 intro videos (gst_caps_is_fixed assertion). Not measured here", "fix": "move ps_studios.mp4, bend_studio.mp4, sie_presents.mp4 and Climax_2024_Ident_wAudio.mp4 out of Days Gone/BendGame/Content/Movies. They are logo intros only, and Verify files or an update puts them back (highball-db#1139, credit Clemens00505)"}, {"symptom": "Occasional minor stutter at a 60 fps cap (M5 Pro, Wine 11 r30, DXMT)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/days-gone.json"},
{"id": "dcs-world-steam-edition", "title": "DCS World Steam Edition", "steam": 223750, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Crashed at start on an M5 with the default engine (r28). Wine's crash report shows a read of address 4 inside Wine's C runtime (ucrtbase), after the game had loaded its terrain, world and renderer modules and Apple's D3DMetal. The game's own log had only two proxy warnings. Nothing more is known yet, the reporter removed the game."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crash at start, Wine's debugger opens with an unhandled page fault reading address 4 (M5, engine r28, highball#673).", "cause": "not found. The fault is inside Wine's ucrtbase, most likely a null pointer the game passes to the C runtime.", "fix": "none known."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/dcs-world-steam-edition.json"},
{"id": "dead-by-daylight", "title": "Dead by Daylight", "steam": 381210, "status": "blocked", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["Easy Anti-Cheat"], "verdict": "blocked"}, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Anti-cheat: Easy Anti-Cheat. The game refuses to start without the anti-cheat's kernel driver, which cannot run under Wine on macOS, so no mode or engine changes this. The reporter saw the anti-cheat block on an M5."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/dead-by-daylight.json"},
{"id": "dead-island-2", "title": "Dead Island 2", "steam": 934700, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Dead Island 2 needs DirectX 12 (Steam lists DirectX version 12), so this page has Play pick D3DMetal, Apple's DirectX 12 layer. A player on an M1 Pro reached the menu in DXVK mode, where DirectX 12 has no proper path, and the game then quit. On D3DMetal the same player got to the opening copyright screen, where the game stopped with its music still playing (highball#451, 2026-10-23). Whether it was still building shaders there is not known. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Smooth to the menu, then the game quits (reported on an M1 Pro, macOS 26.5.2, DXVK, engine r28)", "cause": "the game needs DirectX 12, which DXVK mode does not provide", "fix": "D3DMetal, which this page now picks. Untested here"}, {"symptom": "On D3DMetal the game stops on the opening copyright screen with the music playing (reported on an M1 Pro, macOS 26.5.2, highball#451)", "cause": "not known. A first start can spend a long time building shaders around this point", "fix": "none confirmed. Give a first start 15 minutes and press Enter once"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/dead-island-2.json"},
{"id": "dead-rising-3", "title": "Dead Rising 3 Apocalypse Edition", "steam": 265550, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Runs, with two problems reported: the mouse could not move the character or aim, and split screen froze the game. The mouse problem comes from the game's switch to a 1280x720 fullscreen mode the Mac did not list. Since Highball 0.10.11 (0.10.15 for everyone) Emulate display mode changes on the game's page makes Wine list that mode and scale the picture, with the pointer where it belongs. Keep the game on DXVK, since DXMT could not build some of its shaders. The game was not run here and the reporter did not confirm the fix."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The mouse cannot move the character or aim (reported on an M5, macOS 26.6.2)", "cause": "the game switches to 1280x720 fullscreen, a mode the Mac does not list, so the picture and the pointer disagree", "fix": "Emulate display mode changes on the game's page, Highball 0.10.15 or later, untested on this game"}, {"symptom": "Split screen freezes the game (reported on an M5, macOS 26.6.2)", "cause": "not investigated", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/dead-rising-3.json"},
{"id": "deadlock", "title": "Deadlock", "steam": 1422450, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["VAC"], "verdict": "warning"}, "reports": {"count": 12, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["DXMT's changelog lists the MetalFX temporal scaler output as fixed. A report has a full standard match playable on DXMT on an M5 Pro, with two costs: about ten minutes of shader compilation before the game stops stuttering, and audio crackle, which that player fixed by setting the Mac's output to 88.2 kHz in Audio MIDI Setup. A second M5 Pro report (19 minutes on DXMT) says it runs very well and only runs warm. One report on D3DMetal too (M5, 4 of 5 after 8 minutes), so both modes start it. Rated perfect on an M5 Pro with DXMT on the default engine (r28) over 153 minutes (highball-db#1159). On an M4 Pro with macOS 15.8.2 and the Wine 11 engine r27 on DXMT, rated playable over 32 minutes with freezes in heavy fights, and on the first launch even in the main menu (highball-db#1230). An M3 Pro rated it playable with workarounds after 42 hours on the Wine 10 engine r29, with input lag, random stutters and drops to 30 to 40 fps in hectic fights at the lowest settings (highball-db#1257)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Audio crackles (reported in the main hub on an M5 MacBook Air, highball#187, and in matches on an M5 Pro, highball-db#243).", "cause": "Most likely the same as Counter-Strike 2's, another Source 2 game: it keeps very little sound queued and at 48 kHz the Mac asked Wine for more at a time than it had (measured on Counter-Strike 2, highball#127). Not measured on Deadlock itself", "fix": "Highball 0.10.3 and later carry the fix that cured Counter-Strike 2's crackle (default engine r19 and later, Wine 11 engine r14 and later), not yet confirmed on Deadlock (highball#187). On older engines, setting the Mac's output to 88.2 kHz in Audio MIDI Setup worked for one player"}, {"symptom": "Stutter for the first minutes of a match (reported on an M5 Pro, DXMT).", "cause": "shader compilation, per the reporter.", "fix": "none needed, it settles after about ten minutes."}, {"symptom": "Noticeable input lag with vSync off, in borderless and in fullscreen (M3 Pro, Wine 10 r29, DXMT, highball-db#1257)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "lowering the resolution to 1920x1080 in fullscreen helped the reporter but didn't remove it"}, {"symptom": "In borderless windowed mode, a resolution below the display's own stays in a window instead of filling the screen (M3 Pro, Wine 10 r29, DXMT, highball-db#1257)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/deadlock.json"},
{"id": "deadly-days-roadtrip", "title": "Deadly Days: Roadtrip", "steam": 3026450, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-12"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on an M3 MacBook Air with DXMT on the default engine (r28), over several sessions. Also reported perfect on an M3 Pro with DXMT on the default engine (r28) over 25 minutes (highball-db#1180)."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/deadly-days-roadtrip.json"},
{"id": "death-stranding", "title": "Death Stranding", "steam": 1190460, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-04"}, "nativeMac": true, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "env", "name": "ROSETTA_ADVERTISE_AVX", "value": "1", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["DirectX 12, so D3DMetal. The game refuses to start without AVX (\"Death Stranding requires a CPU with AVX support\", highball#107 on an M5), which Rosetta hides unless asked, so the recipe advertises it to the game. Confirmed by the reporter on an M5 with Highball 0.9.19. A second perfect report, 74 minutes on D3DMetal on an M5 with the death-stranding recipe.", "The game checks for AVX at launch and stops with \"Death Stranding requires a CPU with AVX support\" when Rosetta hides it (highball#107, M5). The recipe advertises AVX to the game. DirectX 12, so D3DMetal. Confirmed by the reporter on an M5 with Highball 0.9.19 (Epic copy)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "\"Death Stranding requires a CPU with AVX support\" at launch (reported on an M5)", "cause": "Rosetta hides AVX unless asked", "fix": "the recipe advertises AVX to the game (ROSETTA_ADVERTISE_AVX=1), or the Compatibility switch in Environment settings"}, {"symptom": "\"failed to load d3d12.dll\" with exception C06D007F right after the AVX check (reported on an M5, Epic copy, Highball 0.9.15)", "cause": "measured on Path of Exile 2 and Hogwarts Legacy the same day: the DirectX 12 timestamp shim numbered its exports from 1 and the game binds D3D12CreateDevice by ordinal 101", "fix": "Highball 0.9.19 and its engines r3 and r9. Confirmed by the reporter"}, {"symptom": "\"Death Stranding requires a CPU with AVX support\" at launch (reported on an M5)", "cause": "Rosetta hides AVX unless asked", "fix": "the recipe advertises AVX to the game (ROSETTA_ADVERTISE_AVX=1), or the Compatibility switch in Environment settings"}, {"symptom": "\"failed to load d3d12.dll\" with exception C06D007F right after the AVX check (reported on an M5, Epic copy, Highball 0.9.15)", "cause": "measured on Path of Exile 2 and Hogwarts Legacy the same day: the DirectX 12 timestamp shim numbered its exports from 1 and the game binds D3D12CreateDevice by ordinal 101", "fix": "Highball 0.9.19 and its engines r3 and r9. Confirmed by the reporter"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/death-stranding.json"},
{"id": "death-stranding-directors-cut", "title": "Death Stranding Director's Cut", "steam": 1850570, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-06"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "env", "name": "ROSETTA_ADVERTISE_AVX", "value": "1", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["DirectX 12, so D3DMetal. Like the original, the game refuses to start without AVX, which Rosetta hides unless asked, so the recipe advertises it to the game. Works once that is on, by the reporter's account on an M4 Max. Nothing was measured here. A report on an M5 rates it playable over 33 minutes with D3DMetal and the recipe on the default engine (r28) (highball-db#1024).", "The Director's Cut checks for AVX at launch like the original and stops with \"Death Stranding requires a CPU with AVX support\" when Rosetta hides it. The recipe advertises AVX to the game. DirectX 12, so D3DMetal. Confirmed by a player on an M4 Max, who got it running once AVX was advertised (highball#514)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "\"Death Stranding requires a CPU with AVX support\" at launch", "cause": "Rosetta hides AVX unless asked", "fix": "the recipe advertises AVX (from the next Highball version). By hand now, turn on Advertise AVX in the environment's settings"}, {"symptom": "\"Death Stranding requires a CPU with AVX support\" at launch", "cause": "Rosetta hides AVX unless asked", "fix": "the recipe advertises AVX to the game (ROSETTA_ADVERTISE_AVX=1), or the Compatibility switch in Environment settings"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/death-stranding-directors-cut.json"},
{"id": "deaths-door", "title": "Death's Door", "steam": 894020, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-04"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on DXVK after a three-minute session on an M5, Epic copy, so this covers launch and the opening. The Steam id here is the same game on Steam. No measurement here yet. The invisible player and enemies of the DXVK mode (two reports, M1 Max and M2 Max) are gone on DXMT, confirmed by the M1 Max reporter on 0.10.4, so the row's mode is DXMT."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The player and enemies are invisible while the level draws (reported on an M1 Max and again on an M2 Max, both with DXVK, highball#219)", "cause": "DXVK's Vulkan on MoltenVK has no transform feedback on any Apple GPU, so the 35 stream-output geometry shaders Unity creates to animate characters fail to build (the log says Transform feedback not supported by device, then Metal rejects the pipelines) while the scenery's shaders build fine. Not chip generation, the M2 Max reproduces it", "fix": "Set Mode for this game to DXMT (the mode this row now applies). Confirmed by the M1 Max reporter on Highball 0.10.4 with the default engine r19 (highball#219, highball-db#309): after the update, with no setting changed, the player and enemies draw. Before 0.10.2 the per-game mode did not reach a Steam launch, so the fix only works from there."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/deaths-door.json"},
