{"id": "detroit-become-human", "title": "Detroit: Become Human", "steam": 1222140, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The game draws with Vulkan directly, through MoltenVK, so the graphics mode does not apply. It plays on the Wine 11 engine r30 or r31 with three variables, which the recipe sets (HB_MVK_LENIENT_INTERFACES=1, MVK_CONFIG_SHADER_COMPRESSION_ALGORITHM=1, MVK_CONFIG_SHOULD_MAXIMIZE_CONCURRENT_COMPILATION=1). On a base M1 with 16 GB the launcher's shader step took about two minutes and the game ran at about 20 fps with little stutter (udance4ever, 2026-11-07). Its launcher first shows a 'graphics card not officially supported' warning, press OK. Older engines stopped at 98 percent in the shader step or showed only a spinner.", "Asks for the Wine 11 engine r31 or newer, whose MoltenVK carries the changes this game needs. The game draws with Vulkan through MoltenVK, so the graphics mode does not matter. HB_MVK_LENIENT_INTERFACES turns on two MoltenVK workarounds made for Detroit (vertex input and render targets, ported from DiAvisoo's MoltenVK changes), the second variable compresses the shader source MoltenVK keeps in memory (LZFSE) and the third compiles shaders on every core. The launcher still warns that the graphics card is not supported, press OK. Confirmed by udance4ever on a base M1 with 16 GB (highball#125, 2026-11-07). The shader step took about two minutes and the game played at about 20 fps with little stutter. Without the compression variable the shader step took about 22 minutes and the game stuttered badly."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Launcher's shader compile stops at 98 percent, or shows only a spinner (engine r10, highball#125).", "cause": "MoltenVK lacked workarounds the game needs. Which of the ported changes cures the stop is not isolated.", "fix": "Wine 11 engine r30 or r31 with HB_MVK_LENIENT_INTERFACES=1, which the recipe sets."}, {"symptom": "Shader step takes about 22 minutes and the game stutters badly (base M1 16 GB, r30 or r31).", "cause": "not isolated. The variable compresses the shader source MoltenVK keeps in memory, and the difference was measured by the reporter.", "fix": "MVK_CONFIG_SHADER_COMPRESSION_ALGORITHM=1, which the recipe sets."}, {"symptom": "A blur over parts of the picture every so often.", "cause": "the game's post processing under MoltenVK, a community patch to the exe removes it.", "fix": "none in Highball, which does not change game files."}, {"symptom": "A blur over parts of the picture every so often", "cause": "the game's own post processing under MoltenVK, a community patch to the game's exe removes it", "fix": "none in Highball, which does not change game files"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/detroit-become-human.json"},
{"id": "detroit-become-human-demo", "title": "Detroit: Become Human Demo", "steam": 1224230, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-14"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The free demo of Detroit: Become Human (1222140), which has its own page. Like the full game it draws with Vulkan through MoltenVK, so the graphics mode doesn't apply. Reported playable on an M3 Max on the Wine 11 engine r31 over 18 minutes, with the three MoltenVK variables of the full game's recipe in the environment. The demo has the same recipe as the full game now, which reaches players with the next Highball release. The player saw the frame rate drop after 30 minutes with DEPTH_OF_FIELD at 1.", "The full game's settings, for its free demo. Asks for the Wine 11 engine r31 or newer, whose MoltenVK carries the changes this game needs. The game draws with Vulkan through MoltenVK, so the graphics mode does not matter. HB_MVK_LENIENT_INTERFACES turns on two MoltenVK workarounds made for Detroit, the second variable compresses the shader source MoltenVK keeps in memory and the third compiles shaders on every core. The launcher still warns that the graphics card is not supported, press OK. The demo played with these three variables on r31 for ajukraine (M3 Max, highball-db#1211)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The frame rate drops after 30 minutes with DEPTH_OF_FIELD at 1, in the player's words (M3 Max, Wine 11 r31, highball-db#1211)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "A blur over parts of the picture every so often", "cause": "the game's own post processing under MoltenVK, a community patch to the game's exe removes it", "fix": "none in Highball, which does not change game files"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/detroit-become-human-demo.json"},
