{"id": "devil-may-cry-hd-collection", "title": "Devil May Cry HD Collection", "steam": 631510, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-05"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Devil May Cry 3 from the collection is reported on a MacBook with an A18 Pro with DXMT on the default engine (r28), in two short sessions of about a minute. It starts and plays smoothly, videos and cutscenes included, but a Bluetooth controller isn't recognized in game."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "A Bluetooth controller isn't recognized in game (A18 Pro, DXMT, Wine 10 r28)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/devil-may-cry-hd-collection.json"},
{"id": "diablo-ii-resurrected", "title": "Diablo II: Resurrected", "steam": 2536520, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "env", "name": "ROSETTA_ADVERTISE_AVX", "value": "1", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Direct3D 12, so D3DMetal. The Steam copy plays on the Wine 11 engine r35 with the game's recipe, which comes with the next Highball release after 0.10.28: it turns off Wine's fiber copy for this game and has Wine load D3DMetal's libd3dshared.dylib (highball#371). Every Wine 11 engine before r35 stops it a few seconds after start, and the default Wine 10 engine opens no window. The Battle.net copy hasn't been tried with the recipe.", "Asks for the Wine 11 engine r35 or newer. Direct3D 12, so D3DMetal. HB_FIBER_MIRROR=0 stops Wine copying the game's fiber into the slot where macOS keeps the thread's priority class. D3DMetal calls macOS code from the game's own threads, and with the copy on the game exited a few seconds after start, before any window. CX_APPLEGPTK_LIBD3DSHARED_PATH has Wine load D3DMetal's libd3dshared.dylib from the engine, without which the game ran with no window. AVX is advertised as in the player's runs, not shown to be needed. Confirmed by AlexPako on an M5 Pro, macOS 27.2.1 (highball#371): 35 minutes with sync off and again with MSync, switching away and back worked."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Never opens a window on the default engine, the game process idle (M5, macOS 27.0.1, the Battle.net copy; the Steam copy on an M5 Pro the same, highball#371)", "cause": "not diagnosed. Blizzard games hit a Rosetta 2 deadlock from January 2026, and CodeWeavers reports Diablo IV and Overwatch running again with macOS 26.5 on CrossOver 26.1 and later", "fix": "none confirmed. The Wine 11 engines r30 and r31 don't start it either, see the next issue"}, {"symptom": "On the Wine 11 engines before r35 the Steam copy exits a few seconds after start, before any window (M5 Pro, highball#371). On the Wine 11 engine the Battle.net copy doesn't get that far, Battle.net crashed after login or never drew its window", "cause": "measured by AlexPako with test builds (highball#371): Wine's fiber copy (engine patches 0008 and 0009) put the game's fiber pointer where macOS keeps the thread's priority class, and D3DMetal calls macOS code from the game's own threads. A Wine without the copy played, the same Wine with it exited after about four seconds. Why macOS stops the process on it (SIGILL) is a reading, not measured", "fix": "the Wine 11 engine r35 with the game's recipe, in the next Highball release after 0.10.28. It sets HB_FIBER_MIRROR=0 and CX_APPLEGPTK_LIBD3DSHARED_PATH to the engine's libd3dshared.dylib. Without the second the game ran with no window. Battle.net's own crash is a separate problem"}, {"symptom": "The cursor keeps switching between the game's cursor and the Mac pointer (M5 Pro, highball-db#1194)", "cause": "seen with the Metal performance HUD on", "fix": "turn the Metal performance HUD off in the environment's graphics settings and remove MTL_HUD_LOG_ENABLED if it was added, as the reporter did"}, {"symptom": "The cursor keeps switching between the game's cursor and the Mac pointer", "cause": "seen with the Metal performance HUD on", "fix": "turn the Metal performance HUD off in the environment's graphics settings"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/diablo-ii-resurrected.json"},
