{"id": "djmax-respect-v", "title": "DJMAX RESPECT V", "steam": 960170, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxvk"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 3, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-12"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["A rhythm game, so timing is the thing to watch. The reporter tried both modes on an M4 Pro with macOS 27 and found DXVK much better than DXMT, with input delay as the remaining complaint; DXMT was rated playable with unspecified minor issues after ten minutes. Use DXVK. No frame rate recorded, and nobody has measured the actual input latency. Another perfect report on DXVK, 32 minutes on an M2 Pro with the default engine (r28), no issues named (highball-db#1177)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Input delay, noticeable in a rhythm game", "cause": "reported on both graphics modes, worse on DXMT; not measured here", "fix": "Use DXVK, which the reporter found much better. No fix for the remaining delay yet."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/djmax-respect-v.json"},
