{"id": "dokapon-kingdom-connect", "title": "Dokapon Kingdom: Connect", "steam": 2338140, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "wine"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-09-16"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["An OpenGL game. On the stock engine it crashes at startup through a null OpenGL function pointer (GLEW's glClearDepthf, a function macOS's own OpenGL does not provide). The reporter got it running by placing Mesa's Windows OpenGL build (opengl32.dll and libgallium_wgl.dll from mesa-dist-win 26.2.0) beside the game's exe with a per-exe native override for opengl32, launched through Steam with sync off. That is a hand edit Highball does not ship; it points at the same OpenGL gap as Mewgenics and at Mesa as the way to close it. Measured here on 2026-09-16: Mesa's zink driver refuses MoltenVK (no nullDescriptor), so the workaround runs on llvmpipe, software rendering on the CPU. Fine for this board game, not for anything heavier. Performance was not measured."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crashes at startup with a page fault at address zero on every graphics mode (reported on an M3, macOS 27)", "cause": "reported from the disassembly: the game calls glClearDepthf through GLEW and Wine's macOS OpenGL has no such function, so the pointer is null", "fix": "workaround by hand: Mesa's Windows opengl32.dll and libgallium_wgl.dll next to DkkStm.exe with a native,builtin override for opengl32 on that exe. Software rendering (llvmpipe), measured. Not shipped by Highball yet"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/dokapon-kingdom-connect.json"},
{"id": "dokimon-quest", "title": "Dokimon Quest", "steam": 2019300, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-05"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable on D3DMetal. Four error boxes come up before the game starts, and pressing OK on each lets it start and play normally. No measurement here yet."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Four boxes saying 'Win32 function failed: HRESULT 0x80070057' from GR_D3D_Device->CheckMultisampleQualityLevels before the game starts", "cause": "The game is made with GameMaker, whose runner shows every failed graphics query in a box. Asked for 8 or more samples, D3DMetal answers Direct3D 11's multisample quality query with E_INVALIDARG, where Windows, DXMT and DXVK answer success with zero quality levels (measured on an M4 with engine r21, 2026-10-05)", "fix": "Press OK on each box and the game starts and plays. Setting the game to DXMT should skip the boxes, since DXMT answers the query the Windows way; not yet tried with this game (highball-db#344)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/dokimon-quest.json"},
