{"id": "elden-ring", "title": "Elden Ring", "steam": 1245620, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["Easy Anti-Cheat"], "verdict": "warning"}, "reports": {"count": 8, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["EAC is userspace under Wine — runs; use d3dmetal (D3D12) A reporter played 231 minutes on D3DMetal on an M1 with macOS 26.6.2 and rated it perfect, which is the longest session recorded for it here; frame rate not measured. A second perfect report on an M3 with macOS 27.0 and engine r10, D3DMetal with frame generation 2x. That reporter's controller was not recognised until they switched Wine's controller driver in the registry (HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\WineBus, DisableHidraw=1 and Enable SDL=1), after which it worked. A third report, five minutes on an M4 Pro with the environment in DXMT mode, also perfect; too short to say more than that it starts and plays there. A fourth, 11 minutes on an M4 Max with D3DMetal and AVX advertised on engine r28, also perfect. Another perfect rating over 91 minutes on an M1 Pro on the default engine's r19, D3DMetal by the report (highball-db#1224). One player (highball-db#1252, M3 Pro, Wine 11 r30, DXMT) said the anticheat didn't work for them and replaced start_protected_game.exe with a renamed copy of the game's eldenring.exe to play offline. They did that themselves. Highball never changes game files and doesn't do this for anyone, and online play needs the anticheat. The other reports here start the game the normal way, mostly on D3DMetal."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Controller not recognised (reported on an M3, macOS 27.0, engine r10).", "cause": "not measured. The reporter fixed it by switching Wine's controller driver from the system HID path to SDL.", "fix": "The dependency \"Controllers through SDL\" (recipe controller-sdl) sets Wine's controller driver to SDL only, the same two registry values the reporter set by hand. Restart the environment after applying. Reported working, not verified here."}, {"symptom": "Alt+Tab doesn't switch away from the game until the game's resolution is changed (M3 Pro, Wine 11 r30, DXMT, highball-db#1252). Another player couldn't minimize the game or move the mouse and keyboard to another display while it ran (M4 Pro, Wine 10 r28, highball-db#906)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/elden-ring.json"},
{"id": "elden-ring-nightreign", "title": "ELDEN RING NIGHTREIGN", "steam": 2622380, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["Easy Anti-Cheat"], "verdict": "warning"}, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-10-08"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable offline over a 14-minute session. The reporter could only start it without its anti-cheat, Easy Anti-Cheat, which keeps the game out of online play, and the resolution behaved oddly. It's a Direct3D 12 game, so the page asks for D3DMetal like Elden Ring's. No measurement here yet."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The game only starts without its anti-cheat, so online play is unavailable", "cause": "Easy Anti-Cheat. Its support for Proton on Linux doesn't extend to Wine on a Mac.", "fix": "none for online play"}, {"symptom": "The resolution behaves oddly", "cause": "not measured", "fix": ""}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/elden-ring-nightreign.json"},
