{"id": "escape-the-backrooms", "title": "Escape the Backrooms", "steam": 1943950, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 5, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-03"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["An Unreal Engine game, Direct3D 11 or 12 by its store page. Reported perfect three times on D3DMetal, the longest a four and a half hour session on an M4 Pro on the default engine r11, and a two-minute look on an M4 Max on macOS 15.8 with engine r17. Which of the game's two Direct3D paths ran under D3DMetal is not known and nobody tried DXMT, so the mode here is the one that worked rather than a comparison. The first reporter's winhttp override and the third reporter's AVX and D3DM_SUPPORT_DXR settings were in place in the working runs, whether any of them is needed is not known, and the hogwarts-legacy recipe in that environment belongs to another game. No frame rate was given and nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/escape-the-backrooms.json"},
{"id": "esoteric-ebb", "title": "Esoteric Ebb", "steam": 2057760, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-23"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on the Wine 11 engine with DXMT on an M1 Max: about 3.5 hours over two sessions through several areas, clean exits and working autosaves, no settings changed. Player.log shows only two warnings with nothing visible on screen (DBufferClear shader not supported, ID3D11Fence not created). Played through Proton-ish rather than the Highball app. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/esoteric-ebb.json"},
{"id": "euro-truck-simulator-2", "title": "Euro Truck Simulator 2", "steam": 227300, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-14"}, "nativeMac": true, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on DXMT on the Wine 11 engine r16 on an M1, with maps loading faster than on the default engine, where the same reporter saw mouse and camera delays. On the Wine 11 engine r15 it did not start, the DXMT start-up crash that r16 removes. Nothing was measured here. The game has a native Mac version on Steam as well. One player on an M4 Pro with the Wine 11 engine r31 rates it playable twice, 26 minutes on DXVK and 93 minutes on DXMT with rare stutters at high settings (highball-db#1183, highball-db#1201)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "On the Wine 11 engine r15 in DXMT mode the game does not start, while the default engine starts it on the same Mac (reported on an M1, macOS 27.0.1, highball-db#288).", "cause": "The DXMT build the Wine 11 engine carried from r11 to r15 built its clear pipelines before the Metal device they read was set up and could crash at start-up. The Wine 11 engine lost it in r16. Confirmed by the reporter's r16 run rather than measured here.", "fix": "Pick the Wine 11 engine r16 or newer on the game's Full page under Advanced, Engine (0.10.4 beta or later), or stay on the default engine, which the reporter found slower with mouse and camera delays."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/euro-truck-simulator-2.json"},
