{"id": "f1-manager-2024", "title": "F1 Manager 2024", "steam": 2591280, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Installed through Highball's Epic support with the Visual C++ runtimes, then crashed at the copyright screen, where the game starts its intro video, without writing a log of its own. Just before the crash the graphics layer printed 'Invalid device handle' for a shared texture, the failure engines before r13 had when a game and its video player share a texture. Engines since r13 no longer fail that texture. Whether that was the whole crash was not measured, and the reporter did not test again."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crash at the copyright screen (reported on an M1, macOS 26.6.2, engine of Highball 0.9.35)", "cause": "likely the shared texture between the game and its intro video, which engines before r13 failed to open", "fix": "update Highball, engines r13 and later open that texture. Not confirmed on this game"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/f1-manager-2024.json"},
{"id": "factorio", "title": "Factorio", "steam": 427520, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-24"}, "nativeMac": true, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["native mac build exists — prefer it The Windows build also runs through Highball on D3DMetal, rated perfect from a two-minute session on an M1 (highball-db#653). The reporter's tip for shader errors there is to add d3dcompiler_47.dll and use D3DMetal. The Mac build stays the better way to play."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/factorio.json"},
{"id": "fahrenheit-indigo-prophecy-remastered", "title": "Fahrenheit: Indigo Prophecy Remastered", "steam": 312840, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 1, "last": "2026-10-26"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Playable with workarounds for the one report so far (M1). On the Wine 11 engine r30 or r31 it starts as it is, since those engines read the Fahrenheit.exe.local folder. On other engines link the DLLs from Fahrenheit.exe.local next to Fahrenheit.exe first (Wine's loader there does not search that folder). Choose In a Window in the pre-launch settings: fullscreen breaks on the first menu click. On the splash screen click the window's title bar and press Enter rather than clicking the picture, which zooms it in. On r30 the mouse works from the profile screen on; on the default engine it stays stuck at the screen's edge, so play there with the keyboard and a gamepad (enable it in Options, Controls). A DualSense needs Steam Input on, or the right stick does nothing. Steam's Mac version is 32-bit and no longer runs on macOS, so Highball installs the Windows one. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The game stops before opening a window in every graphics mode, its own DLLs not found", "cause": "the DLLs sit in Fahrenheit.exe.local, Windows' DLL redirection folder, which Wine's loader does not search (also missing upstream, checked 2026-10-26)", "fix": "the Wine 11 engines r30 and r31 (Highball 0.10.26) look in a program's .local folder, confirmed with this game on r30 (highball-db#700, 2026-11-07, credit udance4ever). On other engines link each DLL from Fahrenheit.exe.local next to Fahrenheit.exe by hand (for x in Fahrenheit.exe.local/*.dll; do ln -s \"$x\" .; done in the game folder)"}, {"symptom": "The first menu click switches the game to 1024x768 and then it fails with 'A DirectX 9.0c or higher compliant video card is needed' or 'D3D ERROR! Fail to create texture surface' (an M1, DXVK's Direct3D 9, highball-db#700)", "cause": "not diagnosed: opening a menu makes the game rebuild its Direct3D 9 device for its own fullscreen mode, and the device or its textures fail to create. In a window instead, the mouse sticks to the screen's right edge", "fix": "none confirmed. Emulate display mode changes got the reporter in once, not reliably"}, {"symptom": "A DirectX 9 warning dialog at start", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "dismiss it, the game goes on"}, {"symptom": "In a window the mouse cursor sticks to the screen's edge and the mouse cannot be used (the default Wine 10 engine)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "on the Wine 11 engine r30 the mouse works from the profile screen on (highball-db#700, 2026-11-07). On the default engine play with the keyboard and a gamepad: enable the gamepad in Options, Controls with the arrow keys"}, {"symptom": "A DualSense's right stick does nothing", "cause": "the game reads the pad through XInput", "fix": "turn Steam Input on for the game. The XInputPlus route on PCGamingWiki did not help the reporter"}, {"symptom": "In a window, a click in the picture on the splash screen zooms it in (M1, Wine 11 r30)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "click only the window's title bar, then press Enter to go on (highball-db#700, credit udance4ever)"}, {"symptom": "The picture is slightly cropped on the right (M1, Wine 11 r30, in a window)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known, it didn't get in the way in the tutorial"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/fahrenheit-indigo-prophecy-remastered.json"},
{"id": "fallout", "title": "Fallout", "steam": 38400, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 2, "last": "2026-11-01"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Out of the box the opening logo and the talking heads slow to a crawl in every graphics mode on an M1, the GOG copy, with the Overseer's voice garbled. The cause, by emrikol's write-up for Fallout 2 (gist.github.com/emrikol/313701a61d0e692798fe938cf6ac24b0), is the Interplay movie decoder, which rewrites its own x86 code for almost every 8x8 block of a frame. Under Rosetta each rewrite throws the translated code away, so frames take hundreds of milliseconds and the streamed sound repeats. The player replaced the decoder in falloutwHR.exe with one that doesn't rewrite itself, their port of emrikol's Fallout 2 patch, and the game then plays from Highball on the Wine 11 engine r30 (highball-db#862). That is a change to the game's own program that the player made. Highball never changes game files, and the patch hasn't been reviewed by Highball. The GOG copy's high resolution patch draws through Direct3D 9. Fallout Community Edition (github.com/alexbatalov/fallout1-ce), an open source rebuild of the engine, has a native Mac app that uses the game's own data files, and it runs the reporter's copy. It's a 32-bit game."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Slows to a crawl a moment into the opening logo, with every graphics mode (M1, Wine 10 r28 and Wine 11 r28). On Wine 11 r30 with the x87 sidecar the logo starts at full speed and the game can be reached, but it crawls again later, at the Overseer's talking head, whose voice is garbled", "cause": "the game's Interplay movie decoder rewrites its own code for almost every 8x8 block, and under Rosetta each rewrite throws the translated code away (emrikol's write-up for the same decoder in Fallout 2, gist.github.com/emrikol/313701a61d0e692798fe938cf6ac24b0). The player's patched falloutwHR.exe bears it out (highball-db#862)", "fix": "the player's own patch to falloutwHR.exe, which replaces the decoder with one that doesn't rewrite itself (their port of emrikol's Fallout 2 patch, gist.github.com/udance4ever/b58fc6a44a571b07598be6999e7d6689, for the GOG 1.2 falloutwHR.exe), plays without the crawl on Wine 11 r30 (highball-db#862, 2026-11-14). It changes the game's own program, which Highball never does, and it hasn't been reviewed by Highball. Otherwise Fallout Community Edition runs the game's data natively on a Mac. The x87 sidecar didn't help, and with DirectSound disabled the game stops before opening a window (highball-db#862)"}, {"symptom": "DXVK mode draws the picture zoomed in (M1, Wine 11 r30, the GOG copy with its high resolution patch)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "WineD3D mode gets the resolution right"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/fallout.json"},
{"id": "fallout-2", "title": "Fallout 2", "steam": 38410, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 2, "last": "2026-11-01"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays with two workarounds in one report on an M1, the GOG copy. Without the High Resolution Patch it stops with 'Error initializing video mode 640x480'. With the patch enabled in HiRes Config it starts, then runs in slow motion like Fallout. The cause, by emrikol's write-up for Fallout 2 (gist.github.com/emrikol/313701a61d0e692798fe938cf6ac24b0), is the Interplay movie decoder, which rewrites its own x86 code for almost every 8x8 block of a frame. Under Rosetta each rewrite throws the translated code away, so frames take hundreds of milliseconds and the streamed sound repeats. emrikol's patch to fallout2.exe replaces that decoder with one that doesn't rewrite itself, and with it the game plays from Highball on the Wine 11 engine r30 in WineD3D mode (highball-db#869). That is a change to the game's own program that the player made. Highball never changes game files, and the patch hasn't been reviewed by Highball. It's a 32-bit game. Outside Highball, the reporter says Fallout 2 Community Edition (github.com/alexbatalov/fallout2-ce), an open source rebuild of the game's engine that runs natively and uses the game's own data files, works on macOS (highball-db#869)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "'Error initializing video mode 640x480' at start", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "enable the High Resolution Patch in the game's HiRes Config, as the reporter did. Emulate display mode changes on the game's page got Red Alert 2 past a similar error, not tried with this game"}, {"symptom": "Runs in slow motion once started, as Fallout does (M1, Wine 10 r28)", "cause": "the game's Interplay movie decoder rewrites its own code for almost every 8x8 block, and under Rosetta each rewrite throws the translated code away (emrikol's write-up, gist.github.com/emrikol/313701a61d0e692798fe938cf6ac24b0)", "fix": "the player applied emrikol's patch to fallout2.exe (made for the US 1.02 exe), which replaces the decoder, and the game played on Wine 11 r30 in WineD3D mode (highball-db#869). It changes the game's own program, which Highball never does, and it hasn't been reviewed by Highball. Fallout 2 Community Edition is the other way, outside Highball"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/fallout-2.json"},
