{"id": "fort-solis", "title": "Fort Solis", "steam": 1931730, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 1, "last": "2026-11-01"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Gets in game in one report on an M1. On the default engine r29 with D3DMetal it needs Media Foundation disabled for Sycamore-Win64-Shipping.exe, and runs at about 20 fps, 30 at Low settings (highball-db#868). On the Wine 11 engine r30 with D3DMetal and DLSS at Performance (Enable DLSS (MetalFX) on in the environment) it runs at 15 to 20 fps with the GPU as the limit, and the reporter finds it smoother. An Unreal Engine 5 game on Direct3D 12."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Hangs on the loading screen at launch (M1, D3DMetal, Wine 10 r28)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "engine r29 got past it for the reporter (highball-db#868), who then hit the freeze below"}, {"symptom": "On engine r29 a white rectangle shows over a picture of Mars after the loading screen, and the game freezes about 30 seconds later without crashing (M1, D3DMetal from GPTK 4.0b2)", "cause": "a video. The log ends with Metal's 'MTLTextureDescriptor has invalid pixelFormat (0)' assertion, the error The Last Caretaker hit when its menu video went through Windows Media Foundation into D3DMetal, and disabling Media Foundation for the game's exe gets past it", "fix": "disable Media Foundation for the game's Unreal exe, Sycamore-Win64-Shipping.exe in Sycamore\\Binaries\\Win64, not fortsolis.exe: in winecfg add that exe on the Applications tab, then on the Libraries tab add mfplat and set it to Disabled. That got the reporter in game (highball-db#868, 2026-11-06, credit udance4ever). Setting it on fortsolis.exe alone left a black screen with the title music. On the Wine 11 engine r30 the game got past the video without the override (highball-db#868, 2026-11-07), but ran at about 8 fps there. On r30 the white box shows on the title screen without the override but the game goes on, and the box goes away with the override (highball-db#868, 2026-11-08)"}, {"symptom": "A launch right after a working one ended after about a minute and a half without reaching the game (M1, D3DMetal, Wine 10 r29)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "not known. It didn't happen again on a later launch (highball-db#868, 2026-11-07)"}, {"symptom": "On the Wine 11 engine r30 with D3DMetal it ran as a slideshow at about 8 fps (M1)", "cause": "not diagnosed. That environment had Enable DLSS (MetalFX) on, and the game keeps its graphics settings per environment, so the Low preset set in the Wine 10 one didn't apply there. Either may explain it, neither is checked (highball-db#868)", "fix": "turn on Enable DLSS (MetalFX) in the environment and DLSS at Performance in the game: 15 to 20 fps on an M1, about 60 ms of GPU time a frame with MetalFX scaling 960x540 up to 1920x1080 (highball-db#868, 2026-11-08, credit udance4ever)"}, {"symptom": "Resolutions below 1920x1080 shrink the picture and change the Mac's display mode (M1, Wine 11 r30)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "keep 1920x1080. With DLSS at Performance the game already draws at 960x540 and MetalFX scales it up"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/fort-solis.json"},
