{"id": "forza-horizon-4", "title": "Forza Horizon 4", "steam": 1293830, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Does not start. Steam starts the game and it hangs inside its own startup with no window. Two walls were found in turn. The first, Wine answering the game's lookup of the Visual C++ libraries package with nothing (Wine bug 55397), is fixed in the Wine 11 engines r24 and r25 (Highball 0.10.16), which register that package the way Proton does. Behind it a second one remains: inside the game a thread loads Steam's own client library (steamclient64.dll) and never releases Wine's loader lock, so the other threads wait until the game gives up; Steam's overlay off changes nothing (traced 2026-10-15). Proton on Linux does not load that library, it ships its own, which is one reason the game runs there. No Mac Wine setup is known to run it (AppleGamingWiki: does not start on CrossOver and Wine). Microsoft delisted the game from Steam in December 2024, and Highball's own test account does not own it, so the maintainer cannot reproduce it and the work goes through a player's traces (highball#268). Among Us, which works, loads the same Steam library on its main thread and is done in about three seconds; Forza loads it from a worker thread and that load never returns."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Steam shows the game running, no window ever opens, the game quits after a few minutes", "cause": "a startup deadlock on Wine's loader lock while the game loads Steam's steamclient64.dll (after the VCLibs package lookup, fixed in engine r24), traced in highball#268", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/forza-horizon-4.json"},
{"id": "forza-horizon-5", "title": "Forza Horizon 5", "steam": 1551360, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 2, "last": "2026-11-13"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Direct3D 12, so D3DMetal. A detailed report on an M4 gets past startup, the Xbox sign-in and into free roam and the benchmark on both Wine 11 engines, but the game is not playable: every piece of scenery draws tilted and a Fatal Error ends it within minutes. Getting that far took a graphics card disguise and a hand-made way around the black sign-in window, see the known issues. Not measured by the maintainer. A later report rates it playable with minor issues not described after 57 minutes on an M1 Pro, on an engine Highball doesn't ship (x64-crossover26.3-r30-fh5) with the Forza Horizon 6 recipe and an RTX 4070 disguise (highball-db#1198). Whether the scenery still drew tilted isn't stated."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The game crashes at startup during graphics setup (a read of address 0x10 in ForzaHorizon5.exe)", "cause": "the default graphics card D3DMetal reports (AMD), the same as Forza Horizon 6", "fix": "report another card with the variables D3DM_VENDOR_ID, D3DM_DEVICE_ID and D3DM_DEVICE_DESCRIPTION (the reporter used an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060, 0x10de and 0x2503, or an Intel Arc A750, 0x8086 and 0x56a1)"}, {"symptom": "The Xbox sign-in window is black", "cause": "the game's own WebView2 (a fixed runtime, 91.0.864.67) does not draw under D3DMetal, like Steam's window", "fix": "none built in. The reporter replaced msedgewebview2.exe with a stand-in that drops the D3DMetal folders from WINEDLLPATH_PREPEND and opens a remote debugging port, then signed in from a Mac browser with a password (passkeys cannot work under Wine)"}, {"symptom": "All scenery (trees, poles, buildings) draws tilted, only the car and the road look right (highball-db#386)", "cause": "not known. The same on D3DMetal 3 and 4, with either graphics card disguise and on the Low preset", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "A Fatal Error with code 0x800705aa (not enough system resources) after 37 seconds to 6 minutes of driving (highball-db#386)", "cause": "not known. Graphics memory in use was only 200 MB to 1.5 GB, and one crash followed a critical section wait that timed out after 60 seconds", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "On DXMT the game crashes at DXGI, asking for an interface DXMT does not know ({f0db4c7f-fe5a-42a2-bd62-f2a6cf6fc83e})", "cause": "a Direct3D 12 game, which DXMT does not cover", "fix": "use D3DMetal"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/forza-horizon-5.json"},
{"id": "forza-horizon-6", "title": "Forza Horizon 6", "steam": 2483190, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 9, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-09"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "env", "name": "D3DM_VENDOR_ID", "value": "0x10de", "platforms": ["mac"]}, {"type": "env", "name": "D3DM_DEVICE_ID", "value": "0x2786", "platforms": ["mac"]}, {"type": "env", "name": "D3DM_DEVICE_DESCRIPTION", "value": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Plays from the intro through races and free roam on the Wine 11 engine r18 (D3DMetal 4), macOS 27 only. Base M4 at 1080p: 28 fps on High, 38 on Medium with FSR Balanced, 50 on Very Low; 39 to 48 in a race at Medium. The recipe sets the engine and the graphics card D3DMetal reports (the AMD default crashes the game). Xbox sign-in once, by code at microsoft.com/link. Built-in Benchmark Mode shows a black screen. Liveries, factory paint reflections and trees draw right from engine r28 (Highball 0.10.23), which works around a D3DMetal vertex layout bug; the same release lets the game offer DLSS Super Resolution (on MetalFX) with Enable DLSS (MetalFX) on, since the recipe now has D3DMetal report an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070. Online play and controllers not tested. A player on an M5 Max played 25 minutes on 0.10.12 and rated it playable with workarounds, without naming them. A player on an M2 Pro played 22 minutes on 0.10.10 and rated it playable, with frame drops and the micro freezes the copy protection causes. Voices and most of the engine sound were missing on every Mac until Highball 0.10.16 (beta), whose Wine 11 engine r24 plays the game's whole surround mix through Apple's spatial mixer. Pick r24 under Advanced, Engine in the game's environment. Since Highball 0.10.24 Play also offers a native arm64 engine, once, for those who prefer steady to fast: Wine 11.18 with FEX, vkd3d-proton and KosmicKrisp in an environment of its own, the game carried along as a clone. On a base M4 with 32 GB it holds an even 30 fps at 1080p, Very Low and FSR Quality with no hitch from the copy protection, where D3DMetal reaches 50 with it. It starts on those settings, and the first start takes about 10 minutes. The Game page's Other route asks again later. Only that M4 has been measured.", "Forza Horizon 6 needs macOS 27 and the Wine 11 engine r18, which carries Apple's D3DMetal 4. Its copy protection opens files in a way the Wine 10 engine does not handle, and it refuses D3DMetal 3 as an unsupported graphics card (FH205). D3DMetal presents itself as an AMD card by default, and the game then crashes in its AMD-only code (its FHE21 dialog), so this recipe has D3DMetal report an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 instead. The game then offers NVIDIA Reflex, and DLSS Super Resolution when Enable DLSS (MetalFX) is on in the environment's Graphics settings (Highball 0.10.23 or later): D3DMetal runs it on MetalFX. DLSS Frame Generation stays unavailable. The first start spends about three minutes at 'Optimizing for your PC'. The game asks you to sign in to Xbox once with a code at microsoft.com/link, and remembers it from then on. On a base M4 at 1080p expect about 28 fps on the High preset the game picks, 38 on Medium with FSR Balanced (Video settings), 50 on Very Low."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "A hitch of about a tenth of a second roughly once a second, in menus, the garage and while driving", "cause": "the game's copy protection runs a periodic check of about 2,000 deliberate traps while holding a lock the frame needs. Under Rosetta each trap costs about 50 microseconds against 1 to 2 on a PC, so a check of a few milliseconds takes about 100 (measured on an M4)", "fix": "none on D3DMetal: priorities, Game Mode and fewer processors were measured and shorten it by a fifth at best. The native arm64 engine Play offers does not have it, since Highball 0.10.24"}, {"symptom": "Liveries look washed out or missing (the car shows mostly its base paint), factory paint has blotchy, faceted reflections, and trees sway oddly (an M5 in highball#290, an M5 Pro in highball-db#449, an M4 Max)", "cause": "D3DMetal 4.0 beta 2 and beta 3 place vertex attributes that the game's input layouts give as D3D12_APPEND_ALIGNED_ELEMENT at the wrong offsets, so its shaders read other attributes' bytes: the livery vinyls' coverage came from texcoord data, normals and tangents were shifted, and so was the trees' wind data. Found and measured on an M4 Max, macOS 27.0.1, 2026-10-20", "fix": "engine r28 (Highball 0.10.23): its D3DMetal shim writes those offsets out. Accept the engine Play offers, or pick r28 under Advanced, Engine"}, {"symptom": "Snow and patches of ground can turn black (an M5 Pro in highball-db#449)", "cause": "not investigated. D3DMetal 4.0 beta 3 cannot build the game's screen-space shadow mask pipelines (their pixel shaders read SV_ShadingRate, which Metal's shader converter turns into an input the vertex shader never writes) and draws nothing with them, which may be related", "fix": "none yet"}, {"symptom": "Dialogue, the navigator's voice and most of the engine sound are missing, on any Mac with a two-channel output such as its speakers or headphones (an M5 Max, an M5 Pro, an M5, an M2 Pro)", "cause": "the game mixes through Windows spatial audio as a 7.1.4 bed of twelve channels, Wine cannot set that layout on a two-channel output, and only the front left and right channels are heard. Found by @TxCsOffc (highball#313)", "fix": "Highball 0.10.16 (beta), engine x64-crossover26.3-r24: Tx's patches (highball#313) render the 12-channel bed with Apple's AUSpatialMixer for the Mac's speakers or headphones, so every channel is heard. Measured on an M4: the game's 12-channel bed and an 8-channel stream go through the mixer, and a 7.1.4 test bed reaches the speakers on every channel. Existing environments keep their engine, so pick r24 under Advanced, Engine. New environments made from the game's recipe get it by themselves."}, {"symptom": "FHE21 right after the splash, or a Wine crash, when forzahorizon6.exe is added to Highball and started by itself (highball#319, #486, #550)", "cause": "the game needs Steam running in the same environment and has to be started through it", "fix": "install it through Steam in the environment. To keep it on an external drive, add the drive in Steam's Settings, Storage, move the game folder into SteamLibrary/steamapps/common on that drive named ForzaHorizon6, install to that library so Steam checks the files, then press Play on the game's page"}, {"symptom": "A freeze of several seconds in all, in one burst, about half a minute into the first drive after starting the game (native arm64 engine)", "cause": "not known yet. It is not shaders compiling on first use, which were measured at zero there, and not the min/max sampler emulation. It only comes when the shader cache is already filled. Measured on an M4: 6.2 and 7.9 s in two runs", "fix": "none yet, it passes and the rest of the drive stays even"}, {"symptom": "On the native arm64 route, the game crashes the moment a controller is used (M5 Max, highball#618)", "cause": "FEX patched an unaligned atomic in its code buffer without the write permission the engine turns on", "fix": "fixed in the native engine r3 (FEX patch 0034 by ineshd), which Play offers once"}, {"symptom": "Since the game's update of November 3, 2026, it closes within a minute of starting with Wine's Program Error dialog (forzahorizon6.exe, a write to address 0x9 or 0x29)", "cause": "the game now fills a Concurrency::concurrent_vector from several threads at once, and the concrt140 built into Highball's Wine 11 engines up to r29 can hand out an address before the memory behind it exists (fixed in upstream Wine in May 2026)", "fix": "Highball 0.10.26 or later loads Microsoft's concrt140 for this game by itself. Before that, in the environment's Settings, Advanced, DLL overrides, add concrt140=n,b, then stop the environment and start the game again"}, {"symptom": "The built-in Benchmark Mode shows a black screen", "cause": "not investigated", "fix": "none yet, read the frame rate from Highball's HUD instead"}, {"symptom": "'Your graphics card is not supported (Code: FH205)' or a crash with Code FHE21 right after the splash", "cause": "the environment is not on a D3DMetal 4 engine (r18 or later), or the recipe's graphics card setting is missing", "fix": "apply this recipe and accept the engine Play offers"}, {"symptom": "Asked to sign in to Xbox again on every start", "cause": "engines before r18 and r19 lose the saved Xbox login on macOS", "fix": "the r18 engine this recipe asks for keeps it"}, {"symptom": "DLSS is not in the game's Video settings", "cause": "Enable DLSS (MetalFX) is off in the environment's Graphics settings, or Highball is older than 0.10.23, which left NVIDIA's DLSS loader without a signed core to load", "fix": "update Highball, turn on Enable DLSS (MetalFX), stop the environment and start the game again"}], "verified": {"date": "2026-10-05", "engine": "x64-crossover26.3-r18 (Wine 11 with patches 0017 to 0019, D3DMetal 4.0b2, the 2026-10-05 shim)", "chip": "Apple M4"}, "source": "db/games/forza-horizon-6.json"},
