{"id": "geometry-dash", "title": "Geometry Dash", "steam": 322170, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-13"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["This game has a native macOS version on Steam, so the Mac Steam app runs it directly without Highball. That is the better way to play it. The Windows build was reported working through Highball over a 2-minute session, with a low frame rate. It draws with OpenGL, which Highball's graphics modes don't change, so the page sets no mode. A second player rates it perfect after two hours on an M2."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Low frame rate (reported on an M2)", "cause": "not measured", "fix": "Play the native Mac version from the Mac Steam app."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/geometry-dash.json"},
{"id": "gethigh-exe", "title": "GetHigh.EXE", "steam": null, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 2, "last": "2026-10-29"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays on an M1 (Epic) at 60 fps. It opens on its settings screen, and Esc starts the game. The sound stuttered badly on the default engine and was smooth on the Wine 11 engine."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Opens on its settings screen with no title menu", "cause": "the game's design", "fix": "press Esc to start playing"}, {"symptom": "The sound stutters badly (M1, default engine)", "cause": "not diagnosed, the default engine (Wine 10) only", "fix": "Play it in an environment on the Wine 11 engine, where the same player found it smooth (highball-db#799)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/gethigh-exe.json"},
{"id": "ghost-of-tsushima-directors-cut", "title": "Ghost of Tsushima DIRECTOR'S CUT", "steam": 2215430, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["PlayStation Overlay"], "verdict": "warning"}, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-10"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays on an M5 Pro on the Wine 11 engine r30 with D3DMetal at a steady 60 fps (capped) with FSR 3.1.4 and the High preset (highball-db#1141). Turn on Advertise AVX, or the game refuses to start with an F16C CPU error. Use FSR, not DLSS: with DLSS (MetalFX) the GPU times out and the game freezes. Single player only so far, the Legends online mode is untested."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Refuses to start with an F16C CPU error (M5 Pro, Wine 11 r30)", "cause": "not measured here. Rosetta shows AVX and the newer CPU features to games only when asked, and asking fixed it", "fix": "turn on Advertise AVX to games in the environment's settings (highball-db#1141, credit Clemens00505)"}, {"symptom": "Stutters, then freezes in game with Upscale Method set to DLSS (MetalFX) (M5 Pro, Wine 11 r30, D3DMetal)", "cause": "the log shows GPU timeout errors right after MetalFX starts, then the GPU ignoring the game's work. Not measured here", "fix": "use FSR 3.1.4 instead, which gives no GPU errors (highball-db#1141)"}, {"symptom": "A No installed graphics card detected box at launch (M5 Pro, Wine 11 r30)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "click OK, the game runs fine after it"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/ghost-of-tsushima-directors-cut.json"},
