{"id": "god-of-war-ragnarok", "title": "God of War Ragnarök", "steam": 2322010, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 3, "last": "2026-11-04"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported running on the Wine 11 engine (x64-crossover26.3-r27) with the environment on D3DMetal and AVX advertised, which the game needs: without it the game stops at launch asking for AVX2, F16C and FMA. On the default engine (x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r28) with D3DMetal it showed a black screen for about two minutes and crashed, after CheckFeatureSupport queries that D3DMetal did not handle (0xc06d007e). The reporter also set D3DM_ENABLE_METALFX=1 and DXMT_ENABLE_NVEXT=1, which were not shown to matter, and installed the engine with the command-line tool, while the environment's Advanced, Engine picker offers the same Wine 11 engine. The game is DirectX 12 only. No session length or frame rate was given and nothing was measured here. A later report rates it perfect over 51 minutes on an M4 Pro on the default engine r29 with D3DMetal and AVX advertised (highball-db#989)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "A black screen for about two minutes, then a crash, on the default engine with D3DMetal (reported on an M5 Pro, macOS 26.6.2)", "cause": "by the reporter's log, the default engine's D3DMetal does not answer some of the game's CheckFeatureSupport queries (0xc06d007e)", "fix": "move the environment to the Wine 11 engine (Advanced, Engine, x64-crossover26.3, r27 or later), keep D3DMetal and turn on Advertise AVX. A player on an M4 Pro played 51 minutes on the default engine's r29, whose D3DMetal is newer, with D3DMetal and AVX advertised and rated it perfect (highball-db#989), so r29 is likely past this too"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/god-of-war-ragnarok.json"},
{"id": "gold-mining-simulator-2-demo", "title": "Gold Mining Simulator 2 Demo", "steam": 3626940, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Unreal Engine. The free singleplayer demo of Gold Mining Simulator 2 (full game Steam 2885380). Runs on D3DMetal with -dx12, which the game needs: without it it falls back to Direct3D 11 and crashes. Reported about 135 fps in the menu and about 30 fps in game at 1920x1080 windowed, all Low, 3D resolution 50%, 18 to 20 fps at 3440x1440. The game uses 11 to 13 GB of memory, so close other apps on a 16 GB Mac. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crashes at start on DXMT and DXVK with an Unreal fatal error (CreateTexture2D failed with E_FAIL on a shared render target, MiscFlags 0x2), reported on an M2 Pro, engine r7.", "cause": "the shared-texture failure ContractVille also hits on the default engine up to r11: DXMT's D3DKMT adapter lookup fails on that Wine, so a shared render target could not be created and Unreal treats that as fatal.", "fix": "launch with -dx12 on D3DMetal, which Highball does from this entry. From engine r13 (Highball 0.10 beta) the Direct3D 11 path no longer crashes on this either, not yet tried with this game."}, {"symptom": "\"DirectX 12 is not supported on your system\" (reported).", "cause": "processes left running from an earlier launch in another mode, per the reporter.", "fix": "stop the environment (or restart the Mac) and launch again."}, {"symptom": "Frame rate falls to about 3 fps with other apps open (reported on 16 GB).", "cause": "the game uses 11 to 13 GB and the Mac swaps.", "fix": "close the browser and other apps before playing."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/gold-mining-simulator-2-demo.json"},
