{"id": "grim-dawn", "title": "Grim Dawn", "steam": 219990, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-12"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable for about two hours on an M5 Ultra with the environment on D3DMetal. The game's resolution did not scale until Emulate display mode changes was turned on in the game's settings in Highball."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The game's resolution does not scale to the screen", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "turn on Emulate display mode changes for the game in Highball"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/grim-dawn.json"},
{"id": "grounded", "title": "Grounded", "steam": 962130, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-02"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable on an M3 Pro with DXMT, multiplayer included, after two changes to the game's own DLLs."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Endless loading spinner at start", "cause": "SpeechSynthWrapper.SetPreferredVoice throws because Wine's speech API returns no voices", "fix": "rename SpeechSynthWrapper.dll in Maine/Binaries/Win64 to SpeechSynthWrapper.dll.bak"}, {"symptom": "Multiplayer fails with ConnectToNetwork: Failed: 3: 63", "cause": "under Windows 10 the game loads PlayFab Party's PartyWin.dll, which fails under Wine", "fix": "in Maine/Binaries/Win64, rename PartyWin.dll to PartyWin.dll.bak and put a copy of PartyWin7.dll in its place named PartyWin.dll"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/grounded.json"},
{"id": "gu-long-feng-yun-lu", "title": "古龙风云录", "steam": 2340650, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-08"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on DXMT, the default mode, over about 6 minutes on an M4 at 1920x1080: 48 fps on the world map and 38 in a hex battle at the game's higher preset, steady, and about 70 at its lowest preset with shadows still on. Unity 2020.1, 64-bit, Direct3D 11. The store has no English title. No measurement here yet."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/gu-long-feng-yun-lu.json"},
{"id": "guild-wars-2", "title": "Guild Wars 2", "steam": 1284210, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-08"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Free to play on Steam, about 90 GB. Its launcher opens on Highball's default setup and, on a first start, asks for an ArenaNet display name to link to your Steam account before the game starts. Only the launcher was exercised here, so no frame rate was measured. AppleGamingWiki's Wine entry says to turn esync off. Highball uses msync, a different mechanism. If the game hangs, set the environment's Synchronization to None. Checked here on 2026-10-05 on an M4 with engine r21 in DXMT mode: the launcher reaches Ready and asks for a display name at 120 s; the game itself was not entered. A player on an M5 with 16 GB plays it on DXMT with the game's balanced preset, with occasional frame drops (highball-db#480)."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/guild-wars-2.json"},
{"id": "gunslugs", "title": "Gunslugs", "steam": 371890, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 2, "last": "2026-11-01"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays in one report on an M1 with D3DMetal. With a controller it needs libusb-1.0.dll next to the game's exe, see the known issue."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "With a controller connected, closes as soon as A is pressed at the title screen to play (M1, DualSense, D3DMetal, Wine 10 r28)", "cause": "when the game finds a controller it loads a native library of its own that needs libusb-1.0.dll, which isn't part of Windows, Wine or the game's files, so the load fails ('Failed loading libusb-1.0.dll: Module not found') and the game exits", "fix": "put libusb-1.0.dll next to gunslugs.exe, from the MinGW64/dll folder of libusb's Windows release (1.0.30, github.com/libusb/libusb/releases), which made the DualSense work for the reporter (highball-db#856). Without it, start with the controller unplugged and play with the keyboard"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/gunslugs.json"},
{"id": "gunsmith-simulator", "title": "Gunsmith Simulator", "steam": 1101120, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-09-26"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable on D3DMetal on an M3 once the resolution is set to 1280 wide and every graphics setting to its lowest, at 60 fps by the reporter's counter. Higher settings were not playable for them. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Needs 1280 wide and the lowest graphics settings for 60 fps on an M3 (reported, highball-db#221).", "cause": "GPU load at the game's defaults, not measured here.", "fix": "lower the resolution and settings as the reporter did."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/gunsmith-simulator.json"},
