{"id": "hogwarts-legacy", "title": "Hogwarts Legacy", "steam": 990080, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 8, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-10"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "env", "name": "ROSETTA_ADVERTISE_AVX", "value": "1", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["DirectX 12 only, so D3DMetal. Before Highball 0.9.19 it stopped at \"Failed to initialize DirectX 12\" on every Mac: the timestamp shim in front of D3DMetal's d3d12.dll numbered its exports from 1 and the game asks for D3D12CreateDevice by ordinal 101, so it never got a device (highball-db#48, the same bug as Path of Exile 2). Fixed in the engines shipped with 0.9.19 (r3 and r9). Do not add -dx11, the game refuses two graphics API flags and crashes at start. The recipe still advertises AVX to the game, it was on in the working run and whether it is needed is not known. A second report on an M5 with macOS 26 rates it perfect on D3DMetal, Epic copy. A third report on an M3 Pro, macOS 27.0, engine r5, rated it playable with minor issues after installing the Visual C++ runtimes; the unspecified minor issues are not recorded here. The same reporter noted the first launch failed and the second launched fine, and that the minor issues were the game's own default graphics choices and a game dialog you click OK on, not Highball. A player on an M5 recommends the Ascendio III performance mod from Nexus Mods, with every option on but ray tracing, after which doors open almost at once (highball-db#1087). Untested here.", "DirectX 12 only, so D3DMetal, on Highball 0.9.19 or later (its engines carry the corrected DirectX 12 shim, without it the game reports \"Failed to initialize DirectX 12\", highball-db#48). Never add -dx11, the game crashes at start with two graphics API flags. AVX is advertised to the game because it was on in the working run; whether it is needed is not known."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "\"Failed to initialize DirectX 12\" a few seconds after launch on D3DMetal, no crash, no log (reported on an M4 Max, macOS 15.7.7)", "cause": "measured: the DirectX 12 timestamp shim exported its functions numbered from 1 and the game binds D3D12CreateDevice by ordinal 101", "fix": "Highball 0.9.19 and its engines r3 and r9. Confirmed by the reporter"}, {"symptom": "Crashes at second zero at fixed addresses when -dx11 is among the Steam launch options", "cause": "measured from the crash context: the game adds its own DirectX 12 flag and Unreal refuses two graphics API flags", "fix": "never use -dx11 with this game"}, {"symptom": "Start fails until the Microsoft Visual C++ runtimes are installed (reported on an M3 Pro, macOS 27.0)", "cause": "not measured here; the game's prerequisite runtimes were missing from the prefix", "fix": "Install the Visual C++ runtimes into the environment, then launch (the reporter's step)"}, {"symptom": "\"Failed to initialize DirectX 12\" a few seconds after launch on D3DMetal, no crash, no log (reported on an M4 Max, macOS 15.7.7)", "cause": "measured: the DirectX 12 timestamp shim exported its functions numbered from 1 and the game binds D3D12CreateDevice by ordinal 101", "fix": "Highball 0.9.19 and its engines r3 and r9. Confirmed by the reporter"}, {"symptom": "Crashes at second zero at fixed addresses when -dx11 is among the Steam launch options", "cause": "measured from the crash context: the game adds its own DirectX 12 flag and Unreal refuses two graphics API flags", "fix": "never use -dx11 with this game"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/hogwarts-legacy.json"},
{"id": "hollow-knight", "title": "Hollow Knight", "steam": 367520, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-09-20"}, "nativeMac": true, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["This game has a native macOS version on Steam, so the Mac Steam app runs it directly without Highball. The Windows build was reported playable through Highball at 1080p and 75 Hz, mode not stated, with an occasional keyboard issue. No measurement here yet."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Keyboard input drops once in a while (reported, Windows build through Highball)", "cause": "", "fix": "Not investigated. The native macOS version avoids Wine altogether."}, {"symptom": "Some cutscenes (the Nailsmith's, the Black Egg's) stay on a black screen with the ambience playing (reported on an M4, DXMT, default engine r5 and r6, then Wine 11 engine r5, highball#214).", "cause": "not measured on this game. Hollow Knight plays its cutscenes as video files through Wine's media layer into the graphics layer, and the reporter's log shows those frames failing on the way in (DeviceTexture: Invalid device handle). Both engines tested predate the fixes for that path: the default line got it in r13, the Wine 11 line in r11.", "fix": "Untested on this game. Highball 0.10.3 with the Wine 11 engine r15 (or the default engine r13 or later) carries the fixes, measured on another Unity game's menu video. The native Mac build on Steam plays them without Wine."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/hollow-knight.json"},
