{"id": "kunitsu-gami-path-of-the-goddess-demo", "title": "Kunitsu-Gami: Path of the Goddess Demo", "steam": 2842890, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 2, "last": "2026-09-16"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Capcom's RE Engine, DirectX 12. On an M1 it stops at start with an unsupported graphics card error, because D3DMetal answers no to the game's check for 64-bit atomics on descriptor heap resources (D3D12 OPTIONS11), the same check as the Onimusha: Way of the Sword demo and PRAGMATA Sketchbook. On an M4 D3DMetal 3 already answers yes (measured here 2026-10-14 with a probe). On Highball's Wine 11 engines (r25 or later) the variable HB_TSSHIM_ATOMIC64=1 makes Highball's DirectX 12 layer answer yes, and with it a player reached gameplay on an M1, but the scene draws wrongly, black silhouettes over a flat pale ground (highball-db#69, r32 with D3DMetal 4.0 beta 3). Whether that comes from D3DMetal 4's beta, from the game now using a feature D3DMetal says the M1 doesn't have, or from something else isn't known. D3DMetal 3 (Wine 11 r33) hasn't been tried with it. No recipe sets the variable for this demo, so a player adds it to the environment's variables by hand, where it reaches every game in that environment."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Unsupported graphics card error at start, naming AtomicInt64OnDescriptorHeapResourceSupported, then the game quits (M1, the same in D3DMetal, DXMT and DXVK mode)", "cause": "D3DMetal reports AtomicInt64OnDescriptorHeapResourceSupported as false on M1 chips, and RE Engine requires it", "fix": "the player's way past it: a Wine 11 engine (r25 or later) with HB_TSSHIM_ATOMIC64=1 in the environment's variables, which has Highball's layer in front of D3DMetal answer yes (highball-db#69). The game then draws wrongly, see below. No recipe sets it for this demo"}, {"symptom": "In gameplay the scene draws as black silhouettes over a flat pale grey ground and sky (M1, Wine 11 r32 with D3DMetal 4.0 beta 3, HB_TSSHIM_ATOMIC64=1)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known. D3DMetal 3 (Wine 11 r33) not tried"}, {"symptom": "A DualSense isn't recognised in the game, with Steam Input on or off (M1)", "cause": "not diagnosed. The same controller worked in the Onimusha: Way of the Sword demo, also RE Engine", "fix": "an XInput controller worked (highball-db#69)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/kunitsu-gami-path-of-the-goddess-demo.json"},
