{"id": "left-4-dead", "title": "Left 4 Dead", "steam": 500, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "wine"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Fullscreen fails: the game asks macOS for its display mode, Wine's Mac driver refuses, and the Source engine then cannot create its Direct3D device (\"Failed to create D3D device!\") whatever the graphics mode. Windowed and borderless works, and the row adds -windowed -noborder to the launch. Reported playable only on Wine's Direct3D, 15 to 20 fps on low settings on an M5; the other modes ran at 3 to 5 fps for the reporter, cause not investigated. A per-game EmulateModeset registry value, as in the Five Nights at Freddy's recipe, should let fullscreen work too, untested here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "\"Failed to create D3D device!\" at launch in every graphics mode (reported on an M5, macOS 26.6.2)", "cause": "measured from the log: the display mode change for fullscreen is refused (NtUserChangeDisplaySettings returns -2), so the Direct3D device cannot be created fullscreen", "fix": "run windowed, the row adds -windowed -noborder. Confirmed by the reporter with -w 1280 -h 720 -windowed -borderless"}, {"symptom": "3 to 5 fps on DXMT, DXVK and D3DMetal, 15 to 20 fps on Wine's Direct3D on low settings (reported on an M5)", "cause": "not investigated", "fix": "none known, use Wine's Direct3D"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/left-4-dead.json"},
{"id": "left-4-dead-2", "title": "Left 4 Dead 2", "steam": 550, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-07"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Runs well on an M2 Air once workshop add-ons are not loaded automatically; with them the campaign froze at load on DXVK and crawled on Wine's Direct3D. The mode of the clean run is not recorded yet. A Source game, so DXVK is the expected mode. On an M1 with the Wine 11 engine and DXMT it played 49 minutes without trouble, with small dips when big hordes come."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Campaign freezes as it loads on DXVK, or runs at very low fps on Wine's Direct3D", "cause": "reported: many workshop add-ons loading at start (M2 Air, 8 GB)", "fix": "Disable the add-ons from loading automatically, then play"}, {"symptom": "Freezes during a match, the log shows 'out of realized font handles' (M5, default engine r28, highball#525)", "cause": "the default Wine 10 engine allows 256 realized fonts and the game runs past that, as Portal 2 and Counter-Strike Source do. Started from the Steam window it also inherits sync off", "fix": "start it with Play in Highball, and if it still freezes move the environment to a Wine 11 engine (limit 5000)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/left-4-dead-2.json"},
