{"id": "marvels-guardians-of-the-galaxy", "title": "Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy", "steam": 1088850, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-22"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "dlloverride", "value": "amd_ags_x64=", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Playable on the r5 engine, which carries the fix. DirectX 12 only: on DXMT it stops at \"No suitable D3D12 adapter found\" before the splash, so D3DMetal is the only mode that reaches the game, and Highball asks for Apple's licence at the first launch. Reached gameplay twice from a clean start on 2026-09-09: 27.5 fps at 1280x720 in the opening scene, 17-32 fps in play, and about 10 fps for the first minute while shaders compile. The Metal HUD reports GPU time of 12.9 ms against a 36.4 ms frame interval, so it is CPU-bound rather than GPU-bound, which is what Rosetta plus 3080 draws and 3049 ExecuteIndirect calls per frame costs. A dialog saying \"Your graphics card driver is older than supported\" appears before the game starts; answer Yes. CodeWeavers' own testers report the same prompt, so it is expected here and not a sign of a broken install.\n\nOn engines before r5 the game renders its splash and menu and then crashes on Play Game. That crash was an unhandled page fault reading 0x907 inside SwitchToFiber, which was handed 0x8ff instead of a fiber pointer. The cause was in Wine, not the game: on macOS the %gs base is the host thread block rather than the TEB, and Wine mirrors only some TEB fields into it. Tib.FiberData was not mirrored, so GetCurrentFiber(), a compiler intrinsic that reads that slot directly and cannot be intercepted, returned the host value 0x8ff, which the game's job system passed straight back to SwitchToFiber. Highball's engine patch 0008 keeps the mirror in step at the three places kernelbase changes the field. An earlier version of this entry blamed D3DMetal's missing DirectX 12 timestamp queries and named Highball's timestamp shim as the fix; that was wrong and is retracted. The shim was loaded and active during a reproduction of the crash and changed nothing. Re-verified on engine x64-crossover26.3-r8 on 2026-09-13 (M1 Pro, macOS 26.6.2, Highball 0.9.9, D3DMetal): launcher, Play Game, the opening bedroom scene under keyboard control at 41 to 42 fps, 1280x720 windowed, GPU 10.7 ms, no fault. r8 replaces the r5 fiber mirror with a slot swap (the mirror hung Metaphor: ReFantazio), and this game still plays on it. The recipe keeps asking for r5, the engine it was first verified on; any later CrossOver-tree engine works too.\n\nA player on a base M5 with the Wine 11 engine r27 and D3DMetal rates it perfect after 9 minutes, around 50 fps with the low preset, anisotropic filtering at 2x and textures on high (highball-db#624).", "Needs engine x64-crossover26.3-r5 or later: earlier engines render the menu and then crash on Play Game, because Wine did not tell the game which task it was running on.", "DirectX 12 only, so it needs Apple's DirectX 12 support. DXMT stops at \"No suitable D3D12 adapter found\" before the splash. Needs engine x64-crossover26.3-r5 or later: earlier engines crash on Play Game."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crashes on \"Play Game\" from the splash screen, with Wine's \"has encountered a serious problem\" dialog, on D3DMetal.", "cause": "Wine did not mirror TEB->Tib.FiberData into the macOS %gs block, so GetCurrentFiber() returned a host value (0x8ff, which is the thread's pthread QoS class) and SwitchToFiber dereferenced it, faulting at 0x907. Measured on engine x64-crossover26.3-r4 and reproduced without the game by a 20-line test program that crashes at the same address, with the same register, on the same instruction.", "fix": "Use engine x64-crossover26.3-r5 or later, which carries patch 0008. On r4 and earlier there is no workaround."}, {"symptom": "About 10 fps for roughly the first minute of play, improving afterwards.", "cause": "shader compilation on first run.", "fix": "none needed, it settles on its own. Later runs start faster."}, {"symptom": "A dialog before launch says the graphics card driver is older than supported.", "cause": "the game's driver version check does not recognise D3DMetal. CodeWeavers' testers report the same prompt.", "fix": "answer Yes. The game runs normally."}, {"symptom": "A dialog before launch says the graphics card driver is older than supported.", "cause": "the game calls agsCheckDriverVersion from AMD's AGS library. D3DMetal presents the Apple GPU as an AMD card, so the game takes AMD's vendor path and looks for a Radeon driver that is not there.", "fix": "the recipe disables amd_ags_x64.dll, which is the library's own absence rather than a trick: there is no AMD GPU here, so its extensions cannot work anyway. Verified 2026-09-09: with the override the prompt does not appear and the game runs. Without it, answering Yes also works."}, {"symptom": "About 10 fps for the first minute, then 17-32 fps.", "cause": "shader compilation first, then a CPU limit. The Metal HUD shows GPU time of 12.9 ms inside a 36.4 ms frame, with 3080 draws and 3049 ExecuteIndirect calls per frame.", "fix": "settings that cut draw calls (shadows, level of detail, object density) are what gain frames. Resolution is nearly free here, so lowering it does not help and raising it costs little."}], "verified": {"date": "2026-09-09", "engine": "x64-crossover26.3-r5", "chip": "Apple M1 Pro"}, "source": "db/games/marvels-guardians-of-the-galaxy.json"},
{"id": "marvels-spider-man-2", "title": "Marvel's Spider-Man 2", "steam": 2651280, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-10"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable on an M4 Pro with D3DMetal over two hours, with AVX advertised, D3DM_MTL4=1 and D3DM_SUPPORT_DXR=1 set by the player. A player on an M4 Pro rates it playable with the sound glitching at times, and uses MacGameFix for characters stuck in a T-pose (highball-db#1133)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Characters stuck in a T-pose (reported on an M4 Pro, D3DMetal, Wine 10 r29)", "cause": "not diagnosed here. MacGameFix's readme lists this game with a T-pose, a broken symbiote and black blocks in the sandstorm on D3DMetal, and says its fix rebuilds four of the game's shaders", "fix": "the reporter uses MacGameFix (github.com/MathiasKowoll/MacGameFix), a third party app that installs fixes into a game's folder (highball-db#1133). Its readme names CrossOver and Steam Play tools, not Highball. Untested here"}, {"symptom": "The sound glitches at times (reported on an M4 Pro, D3DMetal, Wine 10 r29)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/marvels-spider-man-2.json"},
