{"id": "meccha-chameleon", "title": "MECCHA CHAMELEON", "steam": 4704690, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-09-17"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable with workarounds on D3DMetal (Unreal Engine, Direct3D 12). The game's bundled launcher PenguinHotel.exe refuses to start with a 'Visual C++ 2015-2022 Redistributable is required' dialog although the runtime is installed, then hangs at sign-in with a missing authentication token. The reporter got past both by setting native,builtin overrides for msvcp140, msvcp140_1, msvcp140_2, vcruntime140 and vcruntime140_1 (the same overrides Highball's Visual C++ component sets when it installs the runtime itself) and by pointing Steam's launch options straight at Chameleon/Binaries/Win64/PenguinHotel-Win64-Shipping.exe with %command% -windowed, which skips the launcher. Only one minute played, so the game starting and rendering is all this says. No measurement here yet."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Launcher says the Visual C++ 2015-2022 runtime is missing although it is installed, then hangs at sign-in", "cause": "The launcher checks the runtime DLLs and finds Wine's built-in copies when the runtime was installed by Steam's redist step rather than by Highball's component, which sets native overrides", "fix": "Install the Visual C++ runtimes from Environment settings, Windows components (sets the overrides), and in Steam's launch options for the game put the full path to Chameleon\\Binaries\\Win64\\PenguinHotel-Win64-Shipping.exe followed by %command% -windowed to skip the launcher (reported by the community)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/meccha-chameleon.json"},
