{"id": "microsoft-flight-simulator-2024", "title": "Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024", "steam": 2537590, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 3, "last": "2026-10-24"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "env", "name": "VKD3D_FEATURE_LEVEL", "value": "12_1", "platforms": ["mac"]}, {"type": "env", "name": "VKD3D_SHADER_MODEL", "value": "6_7", "platforms": ["mac"]}, {"type": "env", "name": "VKD3D_CONFIG", "value": "force_native_fp16,no_staggered_submit", "platforms": ["mac"]}, {"type": "env", "name": "DXVK_CONFIG", "value": "dxgi.maxVideoMemoryBudget=${memoryMB*0.375}", "platforms": ["mac"]}, {"type": "dlloverride", "value": "gameoverlayrenderer64,gameoverlayrenderer=d", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Runs on Highball's native arm64 preview engine (arm64-wine11.18-r5), which Play offers for this game in one click, through vkd3d-proton on MoltenVK. The game's recipe asks for that engine and sets the feature level, shader model and other variables it needs, including emulator switches that cut most of the stutter (frames over 100 ms per 2-minute park from 59 to 5 on a base M4 in daylight, highball-engine#16). On a base M4 with 32 GB it flies at 22 to 25 fps parked and 19 to 21 on the take-off roll at the Medium preset with FSR Balanced, takes about seven minutes to the start screen and four more to the cockpit, and crashes during the world load about one start in sixteen to forty. The engine needs macOS 26.5 or later. On the Intel engines the game does not run: D3DMetal 3 and the first D3DMetal 4 betas report Shader Model 6.6 and the game refuses to start, and past that check it stops during its first load. How it was made to run: gethighball.com/docs/flight-simulator-2024-apple-silicon/. The first teardown, probes and DXVK patches are Michael-Liendo's, in highball-db#6 and github.com/Michael-Liendo/msfs2024-apple-silicon. An M5 Max player got the plane up on r6 and rated it 4 of 5, with motion blur turned off in the graphics settings (highball-db#665).", "Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024 runs on Highball's native arm64 preview engine, which this recipe asks for, and the Intel engines cannot start it. The engine needs macOS 26.5 or later. It was tested on a Mac with 32 GB of memory, where the game used 25 to 27 GB. The first start takes about seven minutes to the start screen and four more from Start to the cockpit, and later starts reuse the shader and code caches. On a base M4 in daylight, expect 22 to 25 fps parked and 19 to 21 on the take-off roll at the Medium preset with FSR Balanced. Turn Motion Blur off in the graphics settings."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Joysticks, yokes, throttles and pedals do not show up in the game's controls, only mouse and keyboard", "cause": "the preview engines before r6 never started Wine's controller support (a missing SDL3 library name)", "fix": "this recipe's engine r6 starts it, and Highball offers the move when you press Play"}, {"symptom": "A Honeycomb Bravo throttle quadrant shows up as a gamepad (Controller_1) and its levers move the menus, or the Alpha yoke does not show up at all", "cause": "Wine's controller driver counted the Bravo, six levers and dozens of switches, as a gamepad when it read it through SDL, and Apple's game controller layer hid the Alpha", "fix": "this recipe's Flight controls as on Windows tweak reads Honeycomb devices directly, as Windows does; from Highball 0.10.23, Play applies it to environments set up before"}, {"symptom": "On the Intel engines the game refuses to start with 'Your graphics card does not support Shader Model 6.7', or quits during its first loading screen", "cause": "D3DMetal 3 and the first D3DMetal 4 betas report Shader Model 6.6, and past that check the game stops during its first load under Rosetta", "fix": "this recipe asks for the native arm64 preview engine, which Play offers for this game"}, {"symptom": "A short freeze of one to two seconds a few times a flight, more in daylight", "cause": "Metal stopping on lossless-compressed images the game copies every frame", "fix": "this recipe sets HB_MVK_NO_LOSSLESS=1 on the environment, which removes most of them, and one flight in four still shows two in daylight"}, {"symptom": "About one start in sixteen to forty ends in a crash during the world load", "cause": "under study (memory corruption during the load)", "fix": "none yet, start again"}, {"symptom": "About seven minutes to the start screen and four more from Start to the cockpit", "cause": "the emulator translating the game's code, the shader preparation and the game unpacking its packages on one thread", "fix": "none, later starts reuse the shader and code caches"}, {"symptom": "Short hitches remain, most on the first take-off after loading and when one of the game's pop-ups opens", "cause": "under study", "fix": "none yet"}, {"symptom": "Menus can freeze for three to four seconds", "cause": "under study", "fix": "switching to another app and back with Cmd+Tab ends the freeze, as a tester found"}, {"symptom": "Far map tiles stay coarse on the Free Flight page away from the departure airport, and the main menu's globe shows pale wedges over the oceans", "cause": "under study", "fix": "none yet"}, {"symptom": "Some lights and line effects are missing", "cause": "geometry-shader pipelines Metal cannot run", "fix": "none yet"}, {"symptom": "Smeared picture when the view turns", "cause": "the game's motion blur at these frame rates", "fix": "turn Motion Blur off in the game's graphics settings"}], "verified": {"date": "2026-10-20", "engine": "arm64-wine11.18-r6 (r5 with the SDL3 library name Wine's controller support needs: Wine 11.18 with Highball's 25 arm64 patches, FEX 2610 with fex/patches 0001 to 0023 and this recipe's FEX switches, MoltenVK 1.4.2 with patches 0001 to 0016, vkd3d-proton 3.0.1)", "chip": "Apple M4"}, "source": "db/games/microsoft-flight-simulator-2024.json"},
{"id": "middle-earth-shadow-of-war", "title": "Middle-earth: Shadow of War", "steam": 356190, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-17"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["DXMT's changelog v0.80 lists an infinite hang on launch as fixed. Reported playable on a base M1 with DXMT on the Wine 11 engine r32 over 5 minutes: the prologue drew with no graphical issues, and the game's benchmark averaged 63 fps on its auto settings, with some texture flickering in the landscape (highball-db#1287). On the Wine 10 engine D3DMetal gave a black screen and controllers didn't work."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Some texture flickering in the landscape during the game's benchmark (M1, DXMT, Wine 11 r32, highball-db#1287)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "A black screen on D3DMetal (M1, Wine 10 r31, highball-db#1287)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "use DXMT, the mode this page sets"}, {"symptom": "DualSense and XInput pads don't work, with Steam Input on or off (M1, Wine 10 r31, highball-db#1287)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "the Wine 11 engine (r32 in the report), where they worked"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/middle-earth-shadow-of-war.json"},
