{"id": "minecraft-dungeons", "title": "Minecraft Dungeons", "steam": 1672970, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 3, "last": "2026-10-26"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Runs well once signed in, on the default engine with DXMT on an M1 Pro. The game signs in with a Microsoft account through Xbox's sign-in, and on the default Wine 10 engine Wine forgets that sign-in at every start: its credential lookup fails on macOS when the Keychain holds no match, so the Xbox sign-in never finds its saved key. Highball's Wine 11 engines carry the fix (engine patch 0019, made for Forza Horizon 6), and the recipe makes Play offer that engine. Confirmed with this game: on the Wine 11 engine r27 the reporter's sign-in stuck and the game rated 5 of 5 (highball-db#710). Nothing was measured here.", "Asks for the Wine 11 engine r19 or newer, the D3DMetal 3 line, which runs on macOS 14 and later. The game signs in with a Microsoft account through Xbox's sign-in, and on the default engine Wine forgets that sign-in at every start (its credential lookup fails on macOS when the Keychain has no match). The Wine 11 engines carry the fix, the same one that keeps Forza Horizon 6 signed in (confirmed by the reporter of highball-db#707 on r27). Everything installed in the environment stays."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The Microsoft account sign-in comes back at every start, and its 'Let's Go' step often does not go through (default engine)", "cause": "Wine's CredEnumerateW fails on macOS when the Keychain has no match, so Xbox's sign-in never finds the key it saved (the same bug as Forza Horizon 6 and Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024)", "fix": "the Wine 11 engine (r18 or newer), which the recipe offers on Play (confirmed on r27, highball-db#710). By hand, the environment's settings, Advanced, Engine. On the sign-in pages, hold a button for about half a second rather than a quick click, and switch apps and back if a page sits"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/minecraft-dungeons.json"},
{"id": "minecraft-dungeons-ii", "title": "Minecraft Dungeons II", "steam": 1912410, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-24"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable on the Wine 11 engine with DXMT on an M1. Signing in with a Microsoft account does not work, so capes cannot be redeemed, and everything else is available. The reporter says the sign-in needs an implementation of xgameruntime.dll, Microsoft's Gaming Runtime, which Wine does not have. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Microsoft account sign-in does not work, so capes cannot be redeemed (reported on an M1, Wine 11 r27, DXMT)", "cause": "the game wants Microsoft's Gaming Runtime (xgameruntime.dll), which Wine does not provide, by the reporter", "fix": "none yet. The rest of the game plays without signing in"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/minecraft-dungeons-ii.json"},
{"id": "minemergematic-demo", "title": "MineMergeMatic Demo", "steam": 5029110, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 5, "last": "2026-09-26"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The free demo of MineMergeMatic (full game Steam 4976010). Reported perfect twice on the default engine line, three hours on an M2 Max (r2) and 36 minutes on an M2 Pro (r3). Neither reporter said which graphics mode. No measurement here yet."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/minemergematic-demo.json"},
