{"id": "moon-mystery", "title": "Moon Mystery", "steam": 1933840, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-18"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Works on DXMT, the default mode, with full graphics. D3DMetal caps the resolution and forces low settings, and DXVK crashes when loading a game. On an M5 Pro with the Wine 11 engine r29 it runs at 60 fps and more at 3200x1800 fullscreen, with occasional lags while shaders load (highball#659)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crash when loading a game on DXVK", "cause": "a render pipeline with a geometry shader fails to compile in MoltenVK (Metal has no geometry shaders)", "fix": "use DXMT, the default mode"}, {"symptom": "Resolution capped at 1440 pixels and low graphics forced on D3DMetal", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "use DXMT"}, {"symptom": "Steam overlay's FPS counter shows a black square", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "Doesn't start, \"CreateProcess() returned 2\" for MoonMystery-Win64-Shipping.exe (after moving the Steam library to another drive)", "cause": "the game's folder was left without most of its files", "fix": "in Steam open the game's Properties, Installed Files, Verify integrity of game files (highball#659, credit Swiss-Mac-User)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/moon-mystery.json"},
{"id": "moon-sweepers", "title": "Moon Sweepers", "steam": 5335510, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 17, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-16"}, "nativeMac": true, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect or nearly so by many players with DXMT on the default engine, on chips from the M1 to the M4 Pro and M3 Max, in sessions up to almost ten hours. The minor issues reported are the Mac running hot with frame drops when turning quickly, occasional crashes (M3, highball-db#1059), and on the Wine 11 engine r31 the game not taking focus back after switching away (highball-db#1060). Nothing was measured here. Rated perfect over 54 minutes on an M5 Pro on the default engine with DXMT (highball-db#1254)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The Mac runs hot and frames drop when moving or turning quickly (M3, M1)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "Crashes now and then (M3, Wine 10 r28, DXVK by the report)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "After switching away from the game once, it doesn't take focus back (M1 Pro, Wine 11 r31, DXMT)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/moon-sweepers.json"},
{"id": "mortal-kombat-11", "title": "Mortal Kombat 11", "steam": 976310, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-25"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Faces are distorted, clothing and stages fine: the skin shows deep creases on the forehead, the cheeks and under the eyes, as if the game's facial wrinkle detail were turned all the way up. Still so on Highball 0.10.21 with engine x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r28 on an M1 with 8 GB (highball#390, 2026-10-19), on DXMT and, tried the next day, on D3DMetal too. The DXMT log shows the game's tessellation factor clamped from 32 to 8 on GPUs before Apple9, but since D3DMetal, which has no such clamp, draws the faces the same way, that clamp is not the cause. Not diagnosed. A second player rated it 4 of 5 on an M4 with DXMT after 33 minutes, and confirmed the same creased faces there, so they are not tied to the M1 or its memory (highball-db#685)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Character faces distorted, with deep creases in the skin, clothing and stages fine (DXMT and D3DMetal on an M1 with 8 GB, Highball 0.10.21, highball#390; DXVK on 0.7.6; DXMT on an M4, Highball 0.10.22, highball-db#685)", "cause": "not diagnosed. The same on DXMT and D3DMetal, so not either translator's limits (DXMT's tessellation clamp ruled out, 2026-10-20)", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/mortal-kombat-11.json"},
{"id": "mortal-kombat-x", "title": "Mortal Kombat X", "steam": 307780, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-16"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on DXMT on the default engine on an M1. A second report, on a base M1 with the Wine 10 engine r29 in D3DMetal mode, played a match at close to 60 fps at 1080p, with two small issues (see the known issues, highball-db#514)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "On the brightness screen the logo stays visible even with the slider at 0 percent (M1, a Dell S2722QC display)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "set it by eye. At 0 percent the game was far too dark, and the player settled on 40 percent (highball-db#514)"}, {"symptom": "With Fullscreen picked by the automatic settings, the game stays in a window (M1)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "toggle Windowed and Fullscreen in the game's settings a few times, as the player did (highball-db#514). Restarting the game may also do it, not tried"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/mortal-kombat-x.json"},
