{"id": "ori-and-the-blind-forest", "title": "Ori and the Blind Forest", "steam": 387290, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 2, "last": "2026-11-06"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Micro freezes made it unplayable on DXVK with async compilation off, where each new shader compiles while playing. The Definitive Edition was reported playable on DXMT on an M4 through Proton-ish, apart from doubled audio. In Highball on an M4 with the Wine 11 engine r31 it crackled and stuttered in every mode, and with athei's x87 sidecar switched on (HB_X87SIDECAR=1) and a 60 fps cap it plays flawlessly at 60 fps on DXMT (highball-db#1032). It's a 32-bit Unity 5 game (PCGamingWiki)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Micro freezes (reported on an M5, macOS 26.6.2, DXVK)", "cause": "likely shaders compiling on first use with DXVK's async compilation off", "fix": "DXMT, or DXVK async shader compilation in the environment's settings, untested here"}, {"symptom": "Audio plays twice, about a second apart (Definitive Edition through Proton-ish, Wine 11 r27, DXMT)", "cause": "not diagnosed, not seen in Highball itself yet", "fix": "none yet"}, {"symptom": "Heavy sound crackling and stutter, the frame counter at 120 with very uneven frame pacing (Definitive Edition, M4, Wine 11 r31, DXMT and D3DMetal)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "add HB_X87SIDECAR=1 to the environment's variables on r30 or r31 and cap the frame rate at 60 in the environment's settings: 60 fps on DXMT with no issues (highball-db#1032, 2026-11-07, credit DonatusBarlas). Which of the two did it isn't known"}, {"symptom": "Stays on the loading screen (Definitive Edition, M4, Wine 11 r31, DXVK)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "Plays in slow motion and stutters (Definitive Edition, M4, Wine 11 r31, WineD3D)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/ori-and-the-blind-forest.json"},
