{"id": "over-the-hill", "title": "over the hill", "steam": 2929250, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 8, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-16"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["A Unity game. Reported playable on DXMT on an M2 Pro and perfect on an M3 Max on D3DMetal 4 with -force-d3d11, with a rare stutter. Rumble works with an Xbox Series controller over Bluetooth once Wine's controller bus is set to SDL in the right registry key (highball#324), and a DualSense then gives no input in Unity games, see that issue. A base M4 played it for an hour with an Xbox controller over Bluetooth and no issues (highball-db#1233). An M5 with 24 GB rated it playable on DXVK in a 4 minute session, saying it takes all the Mac's memory at launch (highball-db#1272)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Takes all of a 24 GB Mac's memory at launch, in the player's words (M5, DXVK, Wine 10 r28, highball-db#1272)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/over-the-hill.json"},
{"id": "overwatch-2", "title": "Overwatch 2", "steam": 2357570, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["Warden"], "verdict": "warning"}, "reports": {"count": 3, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-07"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["A player on an M5 Pro reports it plays flawlessly on the Wine 11 engine (highball#232), and the recipe makes Play offer that engine. On the Wine 11 engine (x64-crossover26.3-r12) the game opens and shows Blizzard's Battle.net account link screen, a QR code and a code to enter at blizzard.com/link, which a Steam player sees on a first start. The account was not linked here, so nothing past that screen was played. On the default engine (x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r17) the same copy runs for two minutes without ever opening a window, which is what players report (highball#232). The hang measured in September on engine r5, a load above 240 that buried the Mac, did not happen on either engine, the load stayed under 7. The DXMT changelog note still stands as an upstream claim (missing hero ability effects fixed, Battle.net required). Re-checked on 2026-10-05 on an M4 with the Wine 11 engine r15 and DXMT: the game opens full screen on its own desktop Space and shows Blizzard's Battle.net link screen (QR code), the first screen for a Steam account that is not linked yet. A second player, on an M4 with the Wine 11 engine r15 and DXMT, played 18 minutes with some frame drops (highball-db#340).", "Asks for the Wine 11 engine r15 or newer. On the default engine the game starts but never opens a window, on every graphics mode (highball#232, reproduced on an M4 on 2026-10-01). On the Wine 11 engine it opens, shows Blizzard's account link screen on a first start, and a player on an M5 Pro reports it plays flawlessly (2026-10-05). Everything installed in the environment stays."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "On the default engine the game starts but never opens a window (highball#232)", "cause": "Not found yet. The same copy opens and reaches the account link screen on the Wine 11 engine. Measured on an M4 with macOS 27.0 on 2026-10-01, engines r17 and r12 with DXMT", "fix": "The recipe offers the Wine 11 engine (x64-crossover26.3-r15 or newer) on Play; switching by hand is the environment's full page, Advanced, Engine. A player confirmed it plays there (highball#232)."}, {"symptom": "On engine r5 (September 2026) the Mac became unresponsive soon after launch, with no game window", "cause": "A repeating assertion failure inside the game, each one a Windows exception that is expensive under Rosetta. Measured 2026-09-09 on x64-crossover26.3-r5, load average above 240, back to 2 when the process was killed", "fix": "Did not happen on r12 or r17 in two minutes each on 2026-10-01. If it does, stop the environment from Highball and the Mac recovers at once"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/overwatch-2.json"},
{"id": "pacific-drive", "title": "Pacific Drive", "steam": 1458140, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-24"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on D3DMetal on an M2 Pro over 137 minutes, at about 50 to 60 fps on medium settings by the reporter, who recommends it. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/pacific-drive.json"},
{"id": "palia", "title": "Palia", "steam": 2707930, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 3, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-11"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on DXMT, the default mode, over a 98-minute session on an M4. No measurement here yet."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Black window with sound and the game's cursor on macOS 14 (M2 Pro, DXMT, highball#584)", "cause": "DXMT's own shaders are built for Metal language 3.2, which macOS 14 refuses (its log says so), so nothing it draws with them appears", "fix": "Update to macOS 15 or later. Not tested here on macOS 14"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/palia.json"},
{"id": "palworld", "title": "Palworld", "steam": 1623730, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-07"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Works on D3DMetal, started from Highball's library. GPU-bound on an M4 at 1920x1080: about 15 fps on the highest preset, 30 fps on medium and 32.5 fps on low with DLSS Performance. DLSS needs two switches: Enable DLSS (MetalFX) in the environment's Graphics settings, and DLSS in the game's video settings. Memory is tight on 16 GB (swap in use). (highball-db#366)"], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The 3D world is black while menus, HUD and text draw", "cause": "seen on DXVK, and when the game is started from Steam's own window, which gives it the environment's mode instead of the one set on its page (highball-db#366)", "fix": "set Mode for this game to D3DMetal on its page and start it from Highball's library"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/palworld.json"},
{"id": "paperback-the-game", "title": "Paperback: The Game", "steam": 710700, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 1, "last": "2026-10-06"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays on the Wine 11 engine r21 or later, which Play offers by itself since Highball 0.10.12. The game is built on the Loom engine (SDL and OpenGL, 2017), so the graphics mode setting does not apply to it. On older engines it crashed a second after start, because macOS's old-style OpenGL 2.1 context lacks a function the game loads (glClearDepthf), and engine patch 0021 in r21 answers it. The game also mixes its music louder than full scale. Windows' audio engine turns such peaks down before the speakers, while Wine on a Mac clipped them, which made loud parts sound like a bad bitrate. The Wine 11 engines r22 and r23 (Highball 0.10.15) add a limiter that does what Windows does. On r23 the reporter still hears the music as too loud (highball-db#349), not yet compared with Windows.", "Paperback runs on the Wine 11 engine r21 and on no engine before it. The game (Loom engine, SDL and OpenGL) loads glClearDepthf in the OpenGL 2.1 context macOS gives it, where older engines hand it nothing, so it crashed at address 0 a second after start on every engine and graphics mode (highball-db#349). r21 answers that call and four like it in old-style contexts (engine patch 0021), and both of the game's builds reach the title menu there. The graphics mode does not apply to an OpenGL game, so this fix only names the engine, nothing in the environment changes."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Wine's Program Error dialog (winedbg) right at launch, page fault on read access at address 0, on every graphics mode", "cause": "the game calls glClearDepthf, which Wine's opengl32 withholds in macOS's OpenGL 2.1 context (needs GL_ARB_ES2_compatibility or OpenGL 4.1); measured with WINEDEBUG=warn+opengl,+wgl on an M4", "fix": "engine x64-crossover26.3-r21 (Wine 11, patch 0021), shipped in Highball 0.10.11; reaches the title menu on an M4; confirmed by the reporter on an M1 (highball-db#349). Highball 0.10.12 and later offer r21 on Play"}, {"symptom": "Loud parts of the music sound harsh, like a bad bitrate", "cause": "The game mixes its music above full scale (the title music goes over in 25 of every 30 seconds, measured on an M4). Windows' audio engine limits such peaks, and Wine on a Mac clipped them", "fix": "The Wine 11 engine r23, or r22 for D3DMetal 4, carries Highball's limiter from Highball 0.10.15. Pick it on the environment's Full page under Advanced, Engine. On r23 the reporter still hears the music as too loud (highball-db#349), not compared with Windows yet"}], "verified": {"date": "2026-10-06", "engine": "x64-crossover26.3-r21", "chip": "Apple M4"}, "source": "db/games/paperback-the-game.json"},
