{"id": "path-of-building-poe2", "title": "Path of Building Community Fork (Path of Exile 2)", "steam": null, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-09-25"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Not a game: the free build planner for Path of Exile 2, an open-source Windows program from github.com/PathOfBuildingCommunity/PathOfBuilding-PoE2 (the official portable release). Listed because PoE2 players run it beside the game and the official release is a verifiable source. The reporter unpacked the portable release in a fresh environment, added the executable to Programs and, on DXMT with msync, reached the build interface and used build import and export, account sign-in, saving and reopening builds, and the built-in updater, all without extra runtimes or DLL changes. Keep game files inside the environment was on. Long sessions were not tested and nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/path-of-building-poe2.json"},
{"id": "path-of-exile-2", "title": "Path of Exile 2", "steam": 2694490, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 3, "median": 3, "last": "2026-10-27"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["DirectX 12 only, so D3DMetal. Before Highball 0.9.19 the normal Play path died at startup with Wine exception 0xc06d007f: the game binds D3D12CreateDevice by ordinal 101 and the timestamp shim in front of d3d12.dll numbered its exports from 1 (highball-db#53). Fixed in the engines shipped with 0.9.19 (r3 and r9), confirmed by the reporter on a fresh install. On DXMT and DXVK the game stops at a GetAdapterInfo dialog, they have no DirectX 12. The white and green rendering artifacts the reporter saw on Apple's D3DMetal 4.0b2 did not show on the shipped 3.0. One crash in three launches after a \"Controller disconnected\" prompt, not reproduced since. A later report on the default engine (r11) on an M5 Max rates it 3, playable with workarounds, after three minutes, without saying which workarounds."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Quits at startup, Wine reports unhandled exception 0xc06d007f (reported on an M5, macOS 26 and 27, before 0.9.19)", "cause": "measured: the game resolves D3D12CreateDevice by ordinal 101 and the timestamp shim's d3d12.dll numbered its exports from 1", "fix": "Highball 0.9.19 and its engines r3 and r9. Confirmed by the reporter"}, {"symptom": "Crashed once after a \"Controller disconnected\" prompt when pressing A (one launch in three, reported on an M5)", "cause": "not isolated", "fix": "none known, not reproduced since"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/path-of-exile-2.json"},
