{"id": "persona-5-royal", "title": "Persona 5 Royal", "steam": 1687950, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-17"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["DirectX 11. Needs the CrossOver-tree engine: the reporter says the Sikarugir (Wine 10) engines do not run it. The recipe asks for x64-crossover26.3-r8, which the reporter found more stable than r7 while the game loads. Mode: D3DMetal is the one rated 5 of 5 (on r7). DXMT: on r7, with DXMT_ALLOW_CROSS_PROCESS_SWAPCHAIN=1 set to get a window, the reporter's Mac kernel-panicked (a watchdog panic, macOS's GPU driver going down); on r8 the reporter says DXMT runs, 26 fps in Shibuya at 1280x800 on a throttling M5, and the panic did not recur. The panic's cause was not measured, and whether r8's fiber slot change is what removed it is the reporter's inference, not a measurement. No measurement here yet. Rated playable with minor issues not described on an M3 with DXMT on the Wine 11 engine r31 over 25 minutes, with no recipes listed in the environment (highball-db#1290).", "Reported playing on the CrossOver-tree engine (highball-db#22, M5, macOS 27.0): D3DMetal rated 5 of 5 on r7, DXMT running on r8 at 26 fps in Shibuya at 1280x800 on a throttling Mac. The reporter says the Sikarugir (Wine 10) engines do not run it and that r8 loads more stably than r7, so the recipe asks for r8. Highball asks for Apple's licence the first time D3DMetal is used.", "On engine r7, DXMT with the cross-process swapchain switch kernel-panicked the reporter's Mac. On r8 the reporter says DXMT works and the panic did not recur. Not measured by the maintainer, so the recipe keeps D3DMetal, the rated mode; switch the game to DXMT in Advanced if you want to try it on r8."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "On engine r7 with DXMT and DXMT_ALLOW_CROSS_PROCESS_SWAPCHAIN=1 the whole Mac kernel-panicked (reported on an M5, macOS 27.0)", "cause": "not measured; the panic log names the watchdog timer, which is what fires when the GPU driver stops responding. The reporter says it did not recur on engine r8 with DXMT", "fix": "the recipe asks for engine r8 and sets D3DMetal, the mode the reporter rated; DXMT on r8 is reported working"}, {"symptom": "Does not run on the Sikarugir (Wine 10) engines", "cause": "not measured (reported)", "fix": "the recipe asks for engine x64-crossover26.3-r8"}, {"symptom": "Drops to about 40 fps in the colour puzzle in Maruki's Palace, the final cutscene and the end credits (M1, DXVK, Wine 11 r27, highball#530)", "cause": "assumed: the movies are decoded on the CPU by the game, under Rosetta, and DXVK is the heavier mode on an M1. Not measured", "fix": "use D3DMetal, the mode the game is rated with. The movie dips may stay"}, {"symptom": "On engine r7 with DXMT and DXMT_ALLOW_CROSS_PROCESS_SWAPCHAIN=1 the whole Mac kernel-panicked (reported on an M5, macOS 27.0)", "cause": "not measured; the panic log names the watchdog timer, which is what fires when the GPU driver stops responding. The reporter says it did not recur on engine r8 with DXMT", "fix": "the recipe asks for engine r8 and sets D3DMetal, the mode the reporter rated; DXMT on r8 is reported working"}, {"symptom": "Does not run on the Sikarugir (Wine 10) engines", "cause": "not measured (reported)", "fix": "the recipe asks for engine x64-crossover26.3-r8"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/persona-5-royal.json"},
