{"id": "pico-park-classic-edition", "title": "PICO PARK:Classic Edition", "steam": 461040, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxvk"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-02"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The 2016 edition, which Steam no longer sells (its store page says it is no longer available; the 2021 PICO PARK is Steam 1509960 and a separate game), so this row is for people who already own it. Reported perfect on DXVK on the default engine after a one-minute session, enough for the menu and a first room. Co-op with other players is the whole game and the report does not say whether a session with others was tried. No frame rate was given and nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/pico-park-classic-edition.json"},
{"id": "planet-coaster-2", "title": "Planet Coaster 2", "steam": 2688950, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 1, "last": "2026-10-06"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Direct3D 12 only (Cobra engine), so D3DMetal, and it needs a Wine 11 engine. On the Wine 10 engines it crashes within seconds: the game reads the current fiber at gs:0x20, where macOS keeps the thread's scheduling priority (0x8ff and 0x20ff in a reporter's minidumps, highball#537), and the Wine 11 engines' patches 0008 and 0009 put the real fiber pointer there. The recipe no longer turns on Metal's validation layer (the Cellar workaround), which froze two Macs. Reported about 55 fps in the menu on an M5 there, with large parks CPU-bound under Rosetta. Denuvo, Steam must be online. Nothing measured here yet. Two reports with the full configuration in place got no window at all: an M3 Pro (Wine 11 r9, D3DMetal 3, a Mac freeze on Stop) and an M5 Pro (r18 with D3DMetal 4 and r19 with D3DMetal 3, the Mac growing unresponsive within minutes without Stop). No report with this recipe has worked yet, so it stays unconfirmed. A third report on an M5 Pro (highball#537, 2026-10-28) gets past the Wine 10 crash on Wine 11 and then hangs: a black window at 0% CPU on r26 (D3DMetal 4 beta 3), an exit after about 100 seconds with an empty dump on r27 (D3DMetal 3).", "Direct3D 12 only, so D3DMetal, and it needs a Wine 11 engine (Wine 10.8 or newer): on the Wine 10 engines it dies at start with the game's own crash dialog even on D3DMetal. Highball offers the engine before applying this. Denuvo, so Steam must be signed in. Not yet run here. Until 2026-10-06 this recipe also turned on Metal's validation layer (MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1 with MTL_DEBUG_LAYER_ERROR_MODE=nslog), the Cellar project's workaround for a D3DMetal startup race, reported playable on an M5 there. With it, two Macs here (an M3 Pro and an M5 Pro) froze and needed a restart, so it was removed. Without it, the expected failure is the game's crash dialog at start, which is the safer one."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crash dialog at launch offering to send diagnostics to the developer", "cause": "DXMT has no Direct3D 12, and on the Wine 10 engines the game reads the Mac's thread scheduling priority where Windows keeps the current fiber (gs:0x20), which our Wine 11 patches 0008 and 0009 fix", "fix": "the planet-coaster-2 recipe, which asks for the Wine 11 engine and D3DMetal (it no longer sets Metal's validation layer)"}, {"symptom": "Nothing visible for five minutes with the full recipe configuration on an M3 Pro, and a forced reboot after stopping it", "cause": "not diagnosed; the working report behind the recipe was on an M5", "fix": "none confirmed; recorded as not working on an M3 Pro, macOS 26.6.2, Wine 11 r9"}, {"symptom": "The game process starts and stays alive, but no window ever appears, and after several minutes the whole Mac becomes unresponsive and needs a restart (highball-db#356, Apple M5 Pro, macOS 27.0.1, Highball 0.10.10, engine r18 with D3DMetal 4 and r19 with D3DMetal 3, the recipe's variables confirmed by 'Metal API Validation Enabled')", "cause": "not diagnosed; the same shape as the M3 Pro report in highball-db#115. Steam's web helpers throw setDisplaySyncEnabled: exceptions under D3DMetal 4 at the same time, which is known from other games and does not stop them", "fix": "none known; avoid running it until there is something new to try"}, {"symptom": "On Wine 11 the game starts and then hangs: a black window at 0% CPU for over four minutes on r26 (D3DMetal 4 beta 3), an exit after about 100 seconds with an empty crash dump on r27 (D3DMetal 3). The Mac stayed responsive (M5 Pro, macOS 27.0, highball#537)", "cause": "not diagnosed, no error lines in the Wine log", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "With the recipe's configuration in place (Wine 11 r9, D3DMetal, Metal's validation layer on, confirmed by 'Metal API Validation Enabled' in the launch log) the game shows nothing for five minutes; stopping the environment then froze the whole Mac and needed a forced reboot (highball-db#115, Apple M3 Pro, macOS 26.6.2, 2026-09-18)", "cause": "not diagnosed; the Cellar profile this recipe carries was reported working on an M5. A first run in the same session went to a Steam client started before the variables were set, which reproduced the original crash dialog once.", "fix": "none confirmed on an M3 Pro. Do not force-stop the environment while the game is up under D3DMetal, quit from the game if it ever shows; close Steam and Play again after changing the environment's variables so the client carries them"}, {"symptom": "On an M5 Pro (macOS 27.0.1, engine r18 with D3DMetal 4 and r19 with D3DMetal 3) the game process stays alive with no window, and the Mac becomes unresponsive within minutes and needs a restart (highball-db#356, 2026-10-06)", "cause": "not diagnosed; same shape as the M3 Pro report above", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "Crash dialog offering to send diagnostics to the developer right at launch (reported highball-db#115, DXMT and D3DMetal, engine x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r2 and r3)", "cause": "two things stack: DXMT has no Direct3D 12 at all, and on the Wine 10 engines the game reads the Mac's thread scheduling priority at gs:0x20, where Windows keeps the current fiber, and crashes within seconds (minidumps in highball#537). The Wine 11 engines' patches 0008 and 0009 put the real fiber pointer there.", "fix": "Apply this recipe on the Wine 11 engine it asks for. The Cellar workaround (MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1 and MTL_DEBUG_LAYER_ERROR_MODE=nslog) is not recommended: on an M3 Pro and an M5 Pro it led to a frozen Mac that needed a restart"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/planet-coaster-2.json"},
