{"id": "poppy-playtime", "title": "Poppy Playtime", "steam": 1721470, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 2, "last": "2026-10-25"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Chapter 1 reported perfect on an Apple A18 Pro with Apple's DirectX 12 support on the default engine. In the same setup Chapter 2 draws only red outlines of its models, and Chapter 3 shows a blank screen with the game's cursor once a new game starts, while its intro sound, menu and settings work. Chapters 4 and 5 not tried. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Chapter 2 draws only red outlines of its models", "cause": "not diagnosed (seen with Apple's DirectX 12 support on the default engine)", "fix": "none known"}, {"symptom": "Chapter 3 shows a blank screen with the game's cursor after starting a new game, while sound and menus work", "cause": "not diagnosed (seen with Apple's DirectX 12 support on the default engine)", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/poppy-playtime.json"},
{"id": "portal-1", "title": "Portal", "steam": 400, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxvk"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-11"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Works under DXVK with HDR on, as on Windows, and the Portal recipe sets it up. Source's HDR used to freeze map loads on Macs (seen on an M1 Pro in August 2026, engine r0), so the recipe turned HDR off with mat_hdr_level 0, at about 96 fps in the first chamber. From Highball 0.10.14 it keeps HDR on and sets mat_tonemapping_occlusion_use_stencil 1, the switch that fixed the same freeze in Portal 2. Checked on an M4 with macOS 27.0 and engine r21: testchmb_a_00 and testchmb_a_08 load with HDR, and the first portals draw. On that Mac Portal's HDR loaded even without the switch, which stays as a precaution for the Macs where the freeze was seen. Players who applied the recipe before get HDR with Re-apply the Portal fix on the game's page. Keep the bottle on DXVK.", "Portal runs with HDR on, with the lighting and bloom it has on Windows. On a Mac, Source's HDR auto-exposure pass used to make map loads freeze or crash, so this recipe turned HDR off. It now sets mat_tonemapping_occlusion_use_stencil 1, Source's own switch that runs that pass on the stencil buffer, the fix that brought HDR back in Portal 2. If loads ever freeze, turn HDR off again by changing mat_hdr_level 2 to 0 in portal/cfg/autoexec.cfg. Keep the game on DXVK."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Freeze or crash at the end of map loads with HDR enabled", "cause": "Source's HDR auto-exposure pass draws occlusion queries into a render pass with no attachments, which the Apple GPU can fail on inside MoltenVK, the same freeze Portal 2 had. Seen on an M1 Pro with engine r0 (2026-08-28). On an M4 with engine r21 Portal's HDR loaded even without the switch below (2026-10-07).", "fix": "mat_tonemapping_occlusion_use_stencil 1 (this recipe writes it into portal/cfg/autoexec.cfg) runs that pass on the stencil buffer. Checked on an M4, macOS 27.0, engine x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r21, DXVK, 2026-10-07: testchmb_a_00 and testchmb_a_08 load with HDR on and the first portals draw. Turning HDR off (mat_hdr_level 0) still works as a fallback."}], "verified": {"date": "2026-10-07", "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r21", "chip": "Apple M4"}, "source": "db/games/portal-1.json"},
{"id": "portal-2", "title": "Portal 2", "steam": 620, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxvk"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 6, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\portal2.exe\\Direct3D", "name": "VideoMemorySize", "valueType": "REG_SZ", "data": "2047", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Works under DXVK with HDR on, as on Windows, and the Portal 2 recipe sets it up. Source's HDR path draws its auto-exposure occlusion queries into a render pass with no attachments, which made the Mac's GPU lose the device, so every map load froze or crashed while menus looked fine. For a month the recipe turned HDR off (mat_hdr_level 0), at the cost of Source's HDR lighting, bloom and haze. From Highball 0.10.14 it sets mat_tonemapping_occlusion_use_stencil 1 instead, Source's own switch that runs that pass on the stencil buffer, and HDR loads and plays. Checked with nine map loads across four maps on an M4 with macOS 27.0, portals included. Players who applied the recipe before get HDR back with Re-apply the Portal 2 fix on the game's page. Keep the bottle on DXVK. With HDR off, the intro map ran at 138-147 fps at 1728x1117 on an M1 Pro (macOS 26.6.2, DXVK, async off).\n\nDynamic shadows (sunlight through the blinds, lamps, the shadows furniture and objects cast) are missing with the defaults. Portal 2's renderer only turns on shadow maps when the graphics card reports an NVIDIA, AMD or Intel vendor ID, and the Direct3D 9 every engine uses reports Apple's. The row passes -force_vendor_id 0x1002 -force_device_id 0x73BF on Play, Portal 2's own switch for its GPU identity, so the game takes its AMD path and draws them. Half-Life 2's renderer has the same check, and with Apple's ID its console shows its flashlight shadows turned off (M4, 2026-10-07), so other Source games probably lose them the same way.\n\nTexture detail: Portal 2 picks its lowest Model / Texture Detail on its first start because Wine reports 0xFFFFFFFF bytes of video memory through WMI and the game reads that as -1. The recipe has Wine report 2047 MB to portal2.exe, and the game then picks High (checked on an M4, 2026-10-06). With HDR on and without the stencil switch, the map loaded to a white screen on the M4 (2026-10-06).", "Portal 2 runs with HDR on, with the lighting, bloom and haze it has on Windows. On a Mac, Source's HDR auto-exposure pass used to make every map load freeze or crash, because it draws into a pass with nothing attached, which the Mac's GPU driver gives up on. This recipe sets mat_tonemapping_occlusion_use_stencil 1, Source's own switch that runs that pass on the stencil buffer instead, and HDR then loads and plays. If loads ever freeze with a white or stuck screen, turn HDR off again by changing mat_hdr_level 2 to 0 in portal2/cfg/autoexec.cfg and in portal2/cfg/video.txt. Keep the game on DXVK.", "Portal 2 sizes video memory from Windows' WMI, where Wine reports 4294967295 bytes on a Mac with a lot of memory. The game reads that as -1 and picks its lowest Model / Texture Detail on its first start. The recipe tells Wine to report 2047 MB to portal2.exe, so the game picks High. A config saved before this keeps its old setting: set Model / Texture Detail to High in Options, Video, Advanced once."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "No dynamic shadows. Furniture, objects and characters cast no shadows from lamps or sunlight (reported on an M3 Pro, Discord 2026-10-05)", "cause": "Portal 2's shaderapidx9.dll sets up shadow depth textures only for vendor IDs 0x10de, 0x1002 and 0x8086 and switches them off for any other. DXVK's Direct3D 9 in the engine reports Apple's vendor ID (0x106b), so the game runs with no shadow maps. Seen on an M4, macOS 27.0, engine r21, DXVK, 2026-10-06.", "fix": "Highball's Play passes -force_vendor_id 0x1002 -force_device_id 0x73BF (from the next version). By hand, put the same in Portal 2's launch options in Steam."}, {"symptom": "Textures softer than the original, Model / Texture Detail on Low (reported on an M3 Pro, Discord 2026-10-06)", "cause": "Wine reports AdapterRAM 0xFFFFFFFF through WMI, Portal 2 reads it as -1 video memory and its first-start autodetect saves the lowest texture level.", "fix": "the portal-2 recipe sets Wine's VideoMemorySize to 2047 for portal2.exe (re-apply it from the game page). For a config saved before, set Model / Texture Detail to High in Options, Video, Advanced."}, {"symptom": "Freeze or crash at the end of every map load (white or stuck screen), menus fine", "cause": "Source's HDR auto-exposure pass draws occlusion queries into a render pass with no attachments, and the Apple GPU loses the device on it inside MoltenVK (VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST, Metal 'Internal Error (0000010d)', and Metal API and shader validation report nothing before it). Engine-level, and it affects other Source titles too.", "fix": "mat_tonemapping_occlusion_use_stencil 1 (this recipe writes it into portal2/cfg/autoexec.cfg) runs that pass on the stencil buffer, so it has an attachment, and HDR works. Measured on an M4 with macOS 27.0, engine x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r21 and DXVK on 2026-10-07, in nine map loads with HDR on across sp_a1_intro1, sp_a1_intro2, sp_a1_intro3 and sp_a2_laser_intro, the last two with this recipe applied by Highball itself. No device loss, and portals drawn correctly. Without the switch every HDR load lost the device. Earlier this recipe turned HDR off (mat_hdr_level 0), which still works as a fallback."}, {"symptom": "Textures look softer than on Windows. Options, Video, Advanced shows Model / Texture Detail on Low after the first start", "cause": "Portal 2's shaderapidx9 sizes video memory through WMI (Win32_VideoController). Wine answers AdapterRAM 4294967295 (0xFFFFFFFF) under DXVK, the game reads it as -1 (mat_info: m_TextureMemorySize -1, Size of Texture Memory 0 kb) and its autodetect saves gpu_mem_level 0. Seen on an M1 Pro (16 GB) and an M4 (32 GB), 2026-10-06.", "fix": "this recipe sets HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\portal2.exe\\Direct3D VideoMemorySize = 2047, then the game reports 2047 MB and saves gpu_mem_level 2 (High). Verified on the M4, macOS 27.0, r21. A config saved before needs Model / Texture Detail set to High once by hand."}], "verified": {"date": "2026-10-07", "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r21", "chip": "Apple M4"}, "source": "db/games/portal-2.json"},
{"id": "portal-first-slice", "title": "Portal: First Slice", "steam": 410, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The free demo of Portal (400), which has its own page. The Portal recipe is for the full game only. Reported playable on a base M1 on the Wine 10 engine r31 in D3DMetal mode over 6 minutes, with an occasional small stutter. A Direct3D 9 game, which on the Wine 10 engine gets DXVK's Direct3D 9 in D3DMetal mode too."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "An occasional small stutter, which the player thinks may be shaders compiling (M1, Wine 10 r31, highball-db#1253)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/portal-first-slice.json"},
