{"id": "pragmata", "title": "PRAGMATA", "steam": 3357650, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-01"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Capcom's RE Engine, DirectX 12 only, so it needs D3DMetal, which this page picks. Reported perfect on an M5 Pro. The reporter's tip is to turn on Enable DLSS (MetalFX) in the environment's settings, which makes the game offer DLSS and raised the frame rate. On an M1 Pro the free demo stopped at its graphics check (see the PRAGMATA SKETCHBOOK demo's page), so older chips may differ. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/pragmata.json"},
{"id": "pragmata-sketchbook-demo", "title": "PRAGMATA Sketchbook (Demo)", "steam": 4003800, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-10-14"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Capcom's RE Engine, DirectX 12 only, so it needs D3DMetal (DXMT translates Direct3D 11 and is rightly refused). On an M1 Pro the game stops at its graphics check because D3DMetal answers no to 64-bit atomics on descriptor heap resources (D3D12 OPTIONS11), the same check as the Onimusha: Way of the Sword demo and Kunitsu-Gami. A player patched that answer inside D3DMetal and reached gameplay and combat at 20 to 60 fps, which says the game does not need the feature to draw. Highball cannot ship a modified D3DMetal. On an M4 D3DMetal 3 already answers yes (measured here 2026-10-14 with a probe), so newer chips may pass the check as they are. On Highball's Wine 11 engine r25 (0.10.16) the variable HB_TSSHIM_ATOMIC64=1 makes Highball's DirectX 12 layer answer yes, and the demo reaches gameplay on the M1 Pro with the original D3DMetal (confirmed by the reporter, highball-db#485). The recipe sets both. An earlier report (M4, macOS 15.7, engine r6) crashed at thread start on D3DMetal; it predates every current engine.", "Capcom's RE Engine asks DirectX 12 for 64-bit atomics on descriptor heap resources and refuses the graphics card without them. On M1 and M2 chips Apple's D3DMetal answers no, so this recipe moves the game to the Wine 11 engine r25 or later, whose DirectX 12 layer in front of D3DMetal answers yes when HB_TSSHIM_ATOMIC64=1 is set, and sets it. Confirmed by a player on an M1 Pro with the unmodified D3DMetal 3 (Highball 0.10.16). On an M4 D3DMetal answers yes by itself and the variable changes nothing."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Unsupported graphics card error at start, then the game quits (M1 Pro)", "cause": "D3DMetal reports AtomicInt64OnDescriptorHeapResourceSupported as false on M1 chips, and RE Engine requires it", "fix": "the recipe: Wine 11 engine r25 or later with HB_TSSHIM_ATOMIC64=1, which has Highball's layer in front of D3DMetal answer yes (confirmed on an M1 Pro, highball-db#485)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/pragmata-sketchbook-demo.json"},
{"id": "prey-2017", "title": "Prey (2017)", "steam": 480490, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["PunkBuster"], "verdict": "warning"}, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["works"], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/prey-2017.json"},
{"id": "prince-of-persia-the-two-thrones", "title": "Prince of Persia: The Two Thrones", "steam": 13530, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The game showed its launch screen, then a black screen, then quit, on every graphics mode. Its log showed Wine refusing the fullscreen mode the game asked for. Since Highball 0.10.11 (0.10.15 for everyone) Emulate display mode changes on the game's page makes Wine list the older display modes, so that switch goes through and the picture is scaled to the screen. The game was not run here and the reporter did not confirm the fix."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Black screen after the launch screen, then the game quits (reported on an M2 Pro, macOS 26.6.1)", "cause": "the game's fullscreen mode switch was refused, the mode was not listed by the Mac", "fix": "Emulate display mode changes on the game's page, Highball 0.10.15 or later, untested on this game"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/prince-of-persia-the-two-thrones.json"},
