{"id": "raceroom-racing-experience", "title": "RaceRoom Racing Experience", "steam": 211500, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxvk"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-09-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": true, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\RRRE64.exe\\DllOverrides", "name": "d3d9", "valueType": "REG_SZ", "data": "n,b", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Direct3D 9 game. On the shipped engine it froze on the pre-race screen after the track loaded with VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST. The reporter replaced the engine's Direct3D 9 DLL (DXVK-Kegworks 1.10.4, frameworks/renderer/d9vk/wine/x86_64-windows/d3d9.dll) with the d3d9.dll from DXVK 3.1.1 and the game then played, practice and races with AI, smooth with minor stutter. That swap is a hand edit of the engine today; shipping a newer Direct3D 9 layer is an engine decision that needs the other Direct3D 9 games rechecked (Portal, Portal 2, Five Nights at Freddy's). Correction 2026-09-18: the reporter's working d3d9.dll prints 'DXVK: v3.1+' with gcc 16.1.0, which is the string of the withdrawn r4 engine's dgVoodoo-free DXVK-macOS 3.1 fork, not of the official DXVK 3.1.1 (which prints 'v3.1.1' and refuses MoltenVK for geometry shaders on every Mac tested). So the layer that renders RaceRoom for him is the fork that froze FNAF and drew RaceRoom in grayscale for another reporter on r4.", "Optional, never applied by Play: puts the DXVK-MacOS 3.1 Direct3D 9 (the engine's d9vk-modern directory) beside RRRE64.exe with a per-program override, so this game alone runs on it while every other game keeps the default layer. It rendered the game, practice and races with AI, for one reporter on an M3 whose sessions froze with VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST on the default layer (highball-db#60); when the withdrawn r4 engine put the same layer on every launch's path, another reporter got RaceRoom in grayscale and a third had Five Nights at Freddy's freeze, so it is offered under Advanced rather than applied. On the maintainer's M1 Pro the same DLL runs Five Nights at Freddy's without a freeze (2026-09-18). RaceRoom itself is not installed here (74 GB)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Freezes on the pre-race screen after the track loads, VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST (reported on an M3, macOS 15.8, engine r2)", "cause": "reported: the engine's Direct3D 9 layer (DXVK-Kegworks 1.10.4); DXVK 3.1.1's d3d9.dll does not lose the device", "fix": "From 0.9.27 an optional fix on the game's page (Advanced, never applied by Play) copies the DXVK-MacOS 3.1 Direct3D 9 beside RRRE64.exe for this game only. One reporter's sessions run on it, another got grayscale, so try it and remove it if the picture goes gray."}, {"symptom": "Stuck on the first loading screen with the logo, or on the splash screen with its music playing (reported on an M1, macOS 27.0.1, engine r5, DXVK, highball#498)", "cause": "not diagnosed. Not graphics: the splash draws correctly. The game's menu is an embedded Chromium (CEF) browser, and its log under Wine shows network calls failing (errors 10042 and 10045) and 'Unable to allocate frame for first frame capture'", "fix": "none confirmed. Tried on r28 with msync in a fresh environment: Wine's own Direct3D crashes at start, DXVK stays on the splash with music and no loading progress"}, {"symptom": "Pre-race screen freezes after the track loads, VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST in the Direct3D 9 log (default layer)", "cause": "reported: the DXVK-Kegworks 1.10.4 Direct3D 9 loses the Metal device on this game", "fix": "apply this optional fix under Advanced on the game's page; if the picture turns grayscale, remove the copied d3d9.dll next to RRRE64.exe and the override, both reported outcomes exist"}, {"symptom": "Applying this fix changes nothing on a DXVK launch", "cause": "measured 2026-09-20 on Half-Life 2 with +loaddll: on a DXVK launch the engine's own Direct3D 9 overlay is found before the copy beside the game's executable (the launch's WINEDLLOVERRIDES outranks the per-program registry entry), so the newer layer never loads; it loads on a wined3d launch", "fix": "none shipped yet; a per-program layer choice is planned (Highball plan item 14). Setting this game's mode to Wine's own Direct3D makes the copy the Direct3D 9 in use, untested on RaceRoom"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/raceroom-racing-experience.json"},
