{"id": "raven-2", "title": "RAVEN2", "steam": null, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 1, "last": "2026-10-29"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The Epic install is a 0.16 MB starter that downloads Netmarble's own launcher (Netmarble Launcher_EPIC 1.8.0) and runs its setup. That setup stops with 'cannot be closed, please close it manually', most likely seeing the starter itself as the running launcher, and Cancel ends the install. Whether the game behind the launcher runs is unknown. The game also needs the Epic Games Launcher itself beside it. Highball installs Epic games through Legendary instead, since Epic's launcher can't install games under Wine, and in CrossOver with Epic's launcher the same setup fails, so it's out of reach for now (highball-db#775)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Netmarble's launcher setup says the launcher cannot be closed, and Cancel ends with 'An unknown error has occurred (execute)'", "cause": "assumed: the setup sees the Epic starter as the running launcher. Not measured", "fix": "none known. The game also needs the Epic Games Launcher itself, which Highball doesn't use, and the same setup failed in CrossOver with Epic's launcher (highball-db#775)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/raven-2.json"},
