{"id": "repo", "title": "R.E.P.O.", "steam": 3241660, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 6, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on the default engine after a one-minute session, and playable for two hours on DXMT on an M5. Neither reporter said whether they played online with friends. No measurement here yet. Rated perfect on an M5 Pro with DXMT over 160 minutes (highball-db#1262)."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/repo.json"},
{"id": "resident-evil", "title": "Resident Evil", "steam": 304240, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-09-29"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The 2015 HD Remaster of the 2002 remake. Reported playable on D3DMetal on an M1 with the default engine r11 after a three-minute session, with a smooth frame rate by the reporter's account. DXMT and DXVK were not tried. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "A pause the first time a door animation or the menu loads, quick after that (reported).", "cause": "most likely shaders compiling on first use, not measured here.", "fix": "none needed, it goes away after the first time."}, {"symptom": "Minor graphical glitches during door animations and in some locations (reported on D3DMetal).", "cause": "not looked at here, the reporter suspects the graphics mode.", "fix": "none confirmed. DXMT is the other mode to try."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/resident-evil.json"},
{"id": "resident-evil-2", "title": "Resident Evil 2", "steam": 883710, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-06"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The 2019 remake. Plays at 60 fps on an M3 Pro with D3DMetal. Some lights flicker in the police station. Also reported perfect on an M5 with D3DMetal over 15 minutes on the default engine (r28) (highball-db#1028)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Some lights flicker in the police station (D3DMetal, M3 Pro)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/resident-evil-2.json"},
{"id": "resident-evil-3", "title": "Resident Evil 3", "steam": 952060, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 3, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-08"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The 2020 remake. RE Engine, and Direct3D 12 since the game's 2022 update (Direct3D 11 is only on the dx11_non-rt beta branch), so D3DMetal is the mode and this page picks it. Played for 50 minutes on an M5 on the default engine. On M1 and M2, RE Engine games can need the Wine 11 engine with HB_TSSHIM_ATOMIC64=1, as the Onimusha demo does, untested for this one."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/resident-evil-3.json"},
{"id": "resident-evil-4-remake", "title": "Resident Evil 4", "steam": 2050650, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-04"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["The 2023 remake. RE Engine and Direct3D 12, so D3DMetal. On an M2 MacBook Air at 1280x832 with the in-game cap at 60, mostly mid settings, ray tracing and FSR off, it runs at 30 to 40 fps as the Mac heats up. Looking through a sniper scope drops about 10 fps for a while. An 8BitDo SN30 Pro in X-input mode works, rumble included. The reporter also set Wine's debug output off (WINEDEBUG=-all), D3DM_MTL4=1, D3DM_ENABLE_METALFX=1 and a list of DLL overrides, and says stutters on loud sounds such as shotgun fire and explosions went away after that. None of it was tested here, so it is not part of the setup Highball applies. A second report on an M5 on the Wine 11 engine r10, D3DMetal, plays for 57 minutes with some freezes, how long they last or when they come was not said. Both reports get into the game and play for about an hour, the second one on the Wine 11 engine for certain, which is worth noting against the WMV intro hang measured on Resident Evil Village on the default engine (that row), so either this game's intro does not take the same path or that engine's media reader copes with it, neither checked here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The HDR brightness setup screen is blank (reported)", "cause": "Not investigated here", "fix": "Leave HDR off in the game's display settings"}, {"symptom": "Some freezes during play (reported on an M5, Wine 11 engine r10, D3DMetal)", "cause": "Not investigated here, how long they last or what brings them on was not said", "fix": "None known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/resident-evil-4-remake.json"},
