{"id": "rollercoaster-tycoon-3-complete-edition", "title": "RollerCoaster Tycoon 3: Complete Edition", "steam": 1368820, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-11-05"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays in one report on an M1, the Epic copy, on the Wine 11 engine r30 with athei's x87sidecar on (HB_X87SIDECAR=1, which r30 and r31 carry) and DXVK mode: sound, speed and the coasters are right, 60 fps by the Metal HUD (highball-db#993). In D3DMetal or WineD3D mode a placed coaster is drawn as grey mush. Without the sidecar the sound runs slow and the game lags. On the Wine 10 engine it slows to a crawl before the legal screen. The Steam release also has a native Mac version."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The sound runs slow and the game lags (M1, Wine 11 r28, D3DMetal and WineD3D)", "cause": "most likely x87 maths, which Rosetta runs slowly", "fix": "the Wine 11 engine r30 or r31 with HB_X87SIDECAR=1 in the environment's variables (highball-db#993, 2026-11-06, credit udance4ever)"}, {"symptom": "A placed rollercoaster is drawn as grey mush (M1, Wine 11, D3DMetal and WineD3D)", "cause": "not diagnosed. The game draws with Direct3D 9, which goes through Wine's WineD3D in D3DMetal and WineD3D mode alike, so it looked the same in both (inferred, highball-db#993)", "fix": "DXVK mode on the Wine 11 engine r30 with HB_X87SIDECAR=1 draws it properly, 60 fps on an M1 (highball-db#993, 2026-11-08, screenshot, credit udance4ever)"}, {"symptom": "Slows to a crawl before the legal screen on the Wine 10 engine (M1)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "the Wine 11 engine gets past it"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/rollercoaster-tycoon-3-complete-edition.json"},
