{"id": "satisfactory", "title": "Satisfactory", "steam": 526870, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 9, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-09"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on D3DMetal on an M5 after about 90 minutes, at 40 to 60 fps at 1080p on Low settings. The reporter had to add -d3d11 to the game's Steam launch options. Nothing was measured here. A second player put over two hours into it on an M4 Max with the environment in DXVK mode and rated it playable with minor issues they did not describe, so the game runs on DXVK as well as on D3DMetal; the report does not say whether -d3d11 was needed there. A third player on an M4 played 45 minutes; the frame rate was rough at first and smooth once the Mac had warmed up, which fits shaders being compiled during the first minutes. A player on an M4 with macOS 15 also rated it perfect on D3DMetal. A fourth player rated it perfect on an M4 over 53 minutes on D3DMetal (highball-db#659). Two M5 reports with the environment in DXMT mode (D3DMetal by the report) rate it playable with frame drops, one while it first loads, the other now and then over more than 22 hours (highball-db#1079, highball-db#1101)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Does not start without a launch option.", "cause": "not established. The reporter had to force the Direct3D 11 renderer.", "fix": "add -d3d11 to the game's launch options in Steam."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/satisfactory.json"},
{"id": "sayonara-wild-hearts", "title": "Sayonara Wild Hearts", "steam": 1122720, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-09-14"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on DXMT on the default engine. Before engine r15, switching to another app lost the audio and the keyboard and mouse. The reporter confirmed that r15 fixes it (highball#182)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Switching to another app while the game runs loses audio and keyboard and mouse input, on engines before r15", "cause": "The fault found in Unity games on the Wine 10 engines (highball#182). The Mac driver left Unity believing it had no focus after a switch, and a Unity game without focus ignores input", "fix": "Fixed in engine r15, confirmed by the reporter on Highball 0.10.1. Environments on the default engine pick it up by themselves once Steam is closed"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/sayonara-wild-hearts.json"},
{"id": "scam-with-your-friends", "title": "Scam With Your Friends", "steam": 4954910, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays, then crashes partway through, after about ten minutes in one report. The crash is Wine's thread pool asserting on 'ioqueue.objcount' when the game closes an asynchronous pipe. Moritz Jost tracked it down in this game and fixed it in highball-engine patch 0025 (#17, 2026-10-19), which ships with the next Wine 11 engine revision. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The game crashes partway through a session (reported on an M4 and an M1 Pro, macOS 27.0.1, DXMT, engines r11 and r28)", "cause": "Wine's thread pool asserts 'ioqueue.objcount' (threadpool.c) when an asynchronous I/O object is closed while a completion is in flight", "fix": "highball-engine patch 0025 by Moritz Jost, in the next Wine 11 engine revision. Move the game's environment to it under Advanced, Engine once it is out"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/scam-with-your-friends.json"},
