{"id": "shift-2-unleashed", "title": "Shift 2 Unleashed", "steam": 47920, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Starts and reaches its setup screens on the default engine on an M1 Max, but has not reached a race yet. Every version uses TAGES Solidshield, which activates online through EA's servers, and its activation window stayed hidden while a second display was connected. The game needs NVIDIA's legacy PhysX, which it ships in its install\\PhysX folder. On DXVK the GPU is lost as a race starts, with MoltenVK's Internal Error 0000010d right after passes drawn with no render target, the fault Portal 2's HDR pass caused. In DXMT mode (Direct3D 9 still goes through DXVK there) the window disappears when the game changes display mode. Nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The activation window never appears after Steam's CD key dialog", "cause": "it opens off screen when a second display is connected", "fix": "disconnect the second display for the activation, as for Steam's own sign in window (highball#479)"}, {"symptom": "PhysXLoader.dll cannot be loaded", "cause": "the game needs NVIDIA's legacy PhysX runtime", "fix": "run install\\PhysX\\PhysX_SystemSoftware.exe from the game's folder with Run a Windows program… in the environment, then stop the environment"}, {"symptom": "On DXVK the game hangs as a race starts with the sound looping (MoltenVK Internal Error 0000010d, then VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST)", "cause": "a GPU fault right after passes with no render target, as in Portal 2's HDR pass; not diagnosed for this game", "fix": "none confirmed. Untested: Wine's own Direct3D for this game"}, {"symptom": "In DXMT mode the window disappears when the game changes display mode", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none confirmed. Untested: Emulate display mode changes in the game's settings"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/shift-2-unleashed.json"},
