{"id": "slashzero-demo", "title": "SlashZero Demo", "steam": 5099550, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 1, "last": "2026-11-03"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays on a Wine 11 engine with D3DMetal on an M1 once Steam's licence agreement is accepted, Low at 40 to 60 fps and Medium at 20 to 30 (highball-db#939). On the Wine 10 engine it crashes after the logo with a Fatal error window. An Unreal Engine game on DirectX 12."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Unreal Engine 'Fatal error!' crash window right after the logo (M1, D3DMetal, Wine 10 r29)", "cause": "not diagnosed. The game's log ends with 'Unhandled Exception: 0xc06d007f', which is the code a program raises when a function it loads late from a DLL isn't there, so the game most likely asks one of Wine's DLLs for a function Wine doesn't have. Which one isn't known yet", "fix": "none known on Wine 10. A Wine 11 engine runs it (see below)"}, {"symptom": "On a Wine 11 engine with D3DMetal, Steam shows a black window with white boxes at the first launch and the game never starts (M1, Wine 11 r28)", "cause": "Steam waits for the demo's licence agreement, and on the Wine 11 engines Steam's window can't draw under D3DMetal, so the agreement stays invisible. Through Open Steam it didn't show either (highball-db#939, 2026-11-06)", "fix": "the player's way (highball-db#939, 2026-11-15): set the game's graphics mode to DXMT on its page, press Play and accept the agreement in Steam's window, press Stop, set the mode back to D3DMetal and press Play again"}, {"symptom": "Highball says the demo never started, no process of its own appearing in six minutes, while the game is running (M1, Wine 11)", "cause": "not diagnosed. Highball didn't recognise the game's process", "fix": "none needed to play, the game keeps running (highball-db#939)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/slashzero-demo.json"},
{"id": "slay-the-spire", "title": "Slay the Spire", "steam": 646570, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-21"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Works, by community consensus. A report on an M2 Pro with the default engine and DXMT has very infrequent, very short stutters, only in Fullscreen and Borderless Fullscreen on a 14-inch MacBook Pro, and an 8BitDo wireless controller that works here while it does not in the game's native Mac version. The native Mac version is the simpler way to play otherwise."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Very infrequent, very short stutters in Fullscreen and Borderless Fullscreen (reported on an M2 Pro 14-inch MacBook Pro, DXMT, engine r28)", "cause": "not measured", "fix": "windowed mode, by the report"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/slay-the-spire.json"},
{"id": "slay-the-spire-2", "title": "Slay the Spire 2", "steam": 2868840, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 3, "last": "2026-11-04"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["This game has a native macOS version on Steam, so the Mac Steam app runs it directly without Highball. The Windows build was reported perfect through Highball over a four and a half hour session on an M2 Pro, mode not stated. A player on an M5 with version 107 needed three fixes of their own, listed below (highball-db#988). No measurement here yet."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "A green screen with sound at start on D3DMetal (Godot's Direct3D 12 renderer)", "cause": "by the reporter, Godot's Direct3D 12 renderer calls IDXGIFactory2::CreateSwapChainForComposition, which D3DMetal doesn't support", "fix": "put an override.cfg in the game's folder that sets rendering_device/driver=\"vulkan\", so the game uses Vulkan through MoltenVK (highball-db#988)"}, {"symptom": "Multiplayer doesn't work", "cause": "by the reporter, the multiplayer proxy DLL in the game's folder is a winmm.dll, and Wine uses its own winmm unless told otherwise", "fix": "add winmm=n,b in the environment's DLL overrides (highball-db#988)"}, {"symptom": "Online lobbies don't work when the game isn't started through the Windows Steam client", "cause": "the game's Steamworks can't reach the Mac's Steam app, only a Windows Steam client running in the same environment", "fix": "start it with Play in Highball, which goes through the Windows Steam client in the environment. The reporter also turned sync off (highball-db#988)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/slay-the-spire-2.json"},
