{"id": "steep", "title": "Steep", "steam": 460920, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-12"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Plays on DXMT, the default mode, from engine r28 (Highball 0.10.20 and later), whose DXMT gives steep.exe the highest sample count the Mac has instead of refusing its 8x texture (Sean Shmulevich's fix, highball-db#465). On older engines and the Wine 11 engines up to r27, DXMT refuses that texture and the game does not start; there D3DMetal works with DirectX 10 turned off (DLL overrides d3d10,d3d10_1,d3d10core=d). DXVK started but drew stretched menus and ran slowly. Long sessions and online play are untested."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "In D3DMetal mode the game stops at start with 'Call to unimplemented function D3D11.DLL.D3D11CoreCreateDevice, aborting'", "cause": "the game loads DirectX 10, and in D3DMetal mode the 64-bit d3d10core comes from DXMT, which needs a Direct3D 11 function D3DMetal does not export", "fix": "use DXMT on engine r28 or newer, or on an older engine set the environment's DLL overrides (Full page, Advanced) to d3d10,d3d10_1,d3d10core=d and keep D3DMetal"}, {"symptom": "DXMT refuses an 8-sample texture and the game does not start", "cause": "the Mac's GPU offers 1, 2 or 4 samples, not 8", "fix": "engine r28 or newer on the default line (Highball 0.10.18) gives steep.exe 4 samples instead, no other setting needed. On older engines and the Wine 11 engines up to r27, use D3DMetal with DirectX 10 turned off as above"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/steep.json"},
