{"id": "tale-of-wuxia", "title": "Tale of Wuxia", "steam": 377530, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 2, "last": "2026-10-06"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Menus are fast, maps crawled at about 4 fps on the default engine. The player's samples put the busy thread in the game's x87 floating-point code, which Rosetta translates slowly. On the Wine 11 engine r30 with the x87 sidecar the engine ships (HB_X87SIDECAR=1) and DXVK mode, maps run at 58 to 78 fps on an M4 (highball-db#352). The variable covers every program in the environment, Play doesn't set it per game yet."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Maps run at about 4 fps while menus run at 100 fps or more", "cause": "the game's x87 floating-point code runs slowly under Rosetta (winedbg samples in highball-db#352)", "fix": "put the environment on the Wine 11 engine r30 or r31 (Highball 0.10.26), add HB_X87SIDECAR=1 to its variables and set the game's mode to DXVK. Measured by the reporter on r30 with the engine's own sidecar: 77.54 fps at the village entrance, 58 fps in the busy village square (highball-db#352, 2026-11-07, credit w8079). On the Wine 11 engines DXMT mode hands Direct3D 9 to Wine's own implementation, which wasn't measured"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/tale-of-wuxia.json"},
{"id": "tankhead", "title": "TankHead", "steam": null, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-10-05"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported playable with workarounds at a low frame rate on an M2, an Unreal Engine game. The player's setup: the D3DMetal 4 engine r20 with D3DM_MTL4=1 (Metal 4 back end, which the engine turns off by default because it stops some Unreal 5 games) and D3DM_ENABLE_METALFX=1, nvapi64,nvngx=n,b so the game's DLSS option maps to MetalFX, Windows 11, AVX advertised, a 120 fps cap in Highball with the real cap set in game, and Engine.ini settings under AppData/Local/TankHead/Saved/Config/Windows (r.GTSyncType=1, r.OneFrameThreadLag=0, s.AsyncLoadingThreadEnabled=1, r.ShaderPipelineCache.Enabled=1 with BatchSize 10, fx.MaxNiagaraCPUParticlesPerEmitter=0, r.Tonemapper.Quality=1, r.SSR.Quality=1). Which of these matter was not tested here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Low frame rate", "cause": "Reported on an M2, not measured here", "fix": "The player's settings in the notes made it playable; which of them help was not measured (highball-db#348)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/tankhead.json"},
