{"id": "the-elder-scrolls-v-skyrim-special-edition", "title": "The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim Special Edition", "steam": 489830, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxvk"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 7, "median": 4, "last": "2026-11-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Use DXVK. One real report on an M5 with macOS 27: DXMT and D3DMetal both crash right after the Bethesda logo, DXVK runs the game well with early stutters that fade as shaders build. DXMT played on a base M1 with the default engine (r28) in three short sessions by one player, so that crash isn't on every Mac (highball-db#1239 to highball-db#1241). A second player on an M4 rated it playable after 42 minutes, with a few dropped frames in the opening cutscene and smooth play after it. A three-hour session on DXVK on an M1 Max with the XAudio overrides rated it perfect (highball-db#513)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crashes right after the Bethesda logo on DXMT and on D3DMetal (reported on an M5, macOS 27.0, engine r3)", "cause": "not diagnosed; the same machine runs the game on DXVK", "fix": "On the game's page under Advanced set the mode to DXVK"}, {"symptom": "On a MacBook's built-in screen the picture does not fill the screen (windowed and borderless stay at the top left, fullscreen is zoomed with the menus cut off), and the launcher lists only three 16:9 sizes (MacBook Air M4, Wine 11 r27)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "play on an external display (the game's display can be chosen in Highball), where fullscreen works. Untested on the built-in screen otherwise"}, {"symptom": "Sound and dialogue fade in and out. The player put it down to the mouse look not tracking well, so sounds sat off from where they were looking (M1, Wine 10 r28, DXMT, Retina pixels at 100%, highball-db#1239 to highball-db#1241)", "cause": "not diagnosed", "fix": "none known"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/the-elder-scrolls-v-skyrim-special-edition.json"},
