{"id": "the-last-caretaker", "title": "The Last Caretaker", "steam": 1783560, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-06"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\VoyageSteam-Win64-Shipping.exe\\DllOverrides", "name": "mfplat", "valueType": "REG_SZ", "data": "", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Unreal Engine 5, Direct3D 12 only. Use D3DMetal: the demo starts, shows its title and main menu at 84 to 110 fps windowed at 1280x720 on an M1 Pro (Metal HUD), with the Visual C++ 2015-2022 runtime installed in the environment first, which the game's own prerequisite check demands. On DXMT or DXVK (no Direct3D 12) it cannot reach the menu, which is the most likely cause of the reported crash. From 0.9.26 Play picks D3DMetal for Unreal 5 builds on its own. Gameplay past the menu is not measured here yet. The black screen turned out to be the menu's video, not the renderer: with the recipe's per-executable mfplat override the menu renders on r5 and on r6 alike (2026-09-19, by eye). An earlier blind reading that r6 drew where r5 was black was the demo's first run, before the video starts, and is withdrawn. On a base M3 with 8 GB a player sees severe stutter when turning the camera, which is a lot of Unreal 5 for that much memory. The full game is reported perfect on an M2 over 188 minutes with D3DMetal and the recipe on the default engine (r28) (highball-db#1023).", "The menu plays a 4K 60 fps video (Content/Movies/Menubgvideo4k60.mp4) through Windows Media Foundation. Under Wine the decoded frames reach D3DMetal as a texture it has no Metal format for: Metal refuses the descriptor (invalid pixelFormat 0), the thread that asked dies, and the game's main thread then waits on it forever, so the window stays black at idle GPU. With Media Foundation's platform library disabled for the game's executable only, the media player fails to open the file, the menu comes up without its background video, and the game plays. Nothing else in the environment changes."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Starts, then crashes before the main menu (reported on an M3 Ultra, Highball 0.9.23)", "cause": "most likely the environment's DXMT mode, which has no Direct3D 12; the game is Direct3D 12 only", "fix": "On the game's page, Advanced, set the mode to D3DMetal. The next release does this on its own for Unreal 5 games"}, {"symptom": "'Microsoft Visual C++ 2015-2022 Redistributable (x64) is required' dialog at launch", "cause": "Unreal's prerequisite check; the runtime was not in the environment", "fix": "Environment settings, Windows components, install the Visual C++ runtimes, then Play again"}, {"symptom": "Steam's own window goes blank after the game's mode is set to D3DMetal (reported on 0.9.23)", "cause": "on 0.9.23 the Steam client starts with the game's mode, and D3DMetal has no 32-bit Direct3D 11 for Steam's browser, so it drew nothing", "fix": "0.9.26 (beta) routes 32-bit Direct3D 11 to DXMT on D3DMetal, so Steam keeps drawing; on 0.9.23 stop the environment and Play again"}, {"symptom": "Black window at idle GPU once the game reaches its menu (the demo's second run onward, the first shows the title before the video starts)", "cause": "measured 2026-09-19: the menu's 4K video goes through Windows Media Foundation and reaches D3DMetal as a texture with no Metal format; Metal's descriptor validation fails (invalid pixelFormat 0), that thread dies and the main thread waits on it forever (RtlpWaitForCriticalSection timeouts in the log)", "fix": "The the-last-caretaker recipe disables mfplat for the game's executable only; the menu comes up without its background video and the game plays (r5 and r6, by eye)"}], "verified": {"date": "2026-09-19", "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r5", "chip": "Apple M1 Pro"}, "source": "db/games/the-last-caretaker.json"},
{"id": "the-last-flame", "title": "The Last Flame", "steam": 1830970, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": null, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Needs the Wine 11 engine x64-crossover26.3-r11 or later (the recipe names it). Two bugs sat behind the report, both in Wine on macOS and both fixed in r11. Start did nothing because the game's save code asks Windows for the last error after a file call and, on macOS, the place Unity's Mono reads it from (%gs:0x68) held a stray pointer instead of the error code, so a missing save file became an IOException that ended the click (Player.log: IOException: Unknown error (0x...)). The menu's 2560x1440 H.264 video, played through Media Foundation and handed to Direct3D 11 as a shared texture, got no shared handle from DXMT on Wine 11 (Got null handle from IDXGIResource::GetSharedHandle) and failed inside the decoder on Wine 10. On r11 both are gone: the run starts on DXMT and on DXVK, and the video plays on DXMT. DXVK draws the board at 20 fps against DXMT's 86 and shows a still behind the menu instead of the video, so use DXMT. On the default Wine 10 engine neither fix exists, but the error path needs the save file to be missing, which is what a first run looks like: with a save already there the game plays on Wine 10 too, measured here on 2026-09-22 (M1 Pro, macOS 27.0, engine x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r5, DXMT, a full session with runs started and no exception in Player.log, the save having arrived through Steam Cloud). So the Wine 11 engine is what a new player needs, and someone whose save already exists may never see the fault.", "Needs engine x64-crossover26.3-r11 or later. Two Wine-on-macOS bugs are fixed there and nowhere else: the last-error slot Unity's Mono reads held a stray pointer, so a missing save file ended the Start click with IOException Unknown error, and the menu video's shared texture got no handle from DXMT. On the Wine 10 engines pressing Start still does nothing and no setting changes that.", "Use DXMT. DXVK also starts the run on r11 but draws the board at 20 fps against DXMT's 86 on an M1 Pro, and its menu shows a still image where DXMT plays the video."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Pressing Start or Embark does nothing on a first run; Player.log has IOException: Unknown error (0x...) from System.IO on the save file", "cause": "measured: Wine on macOS keeps GetLastError in a different thread slot from the one MSVC-built Mono reads, so a missing save file comes back as garbage instead of file-not-found. It takes a missing save, so it hits a first run and not a copy that already has one", "fix": "Engine x64-crossover26.3-r11 or later (patch 0011 keeps the two in step). On a Wine 10 engine a run started once by any other means leaves a save, and the game then plays there too."}, {"symptom": "The menu's background video does not show", "cause": "measured: the video needs a Direct3D 11 shared texture; Wine 10 fails in the decoder, Wine 11 before r11 got no handle from DXMT, and DXVK cannot share textures at all", "fix": "Engine r11 or later with DXMT (patch 0010). On DXVK the menu keeps a still image; the game plays anyway."}, {"symptom": "Pressing Start or Embark does nothing on a first run; Player.log has IOException: Unknown error (0x...) on the save file", "cause": "Wine on macOS kept GetLastError in a different thread slot from the one MSVC-built Mono reads (highball-engine patch 0011)", "fix": "This recipe's engine, r11 or later. The fault needs the save to be missing, so it hits a first run; a copy that already has a save plays on Wine 10 too (measured 2026-09-22)."}, {"symptom": "The menu's background video does not show", "cause": "Its shared Direct3D 11 texture got no handle from DXMT before r11 (patch 0010); DXVK cannot share textures at all", "fix": "r11 or later with DXMT. On DXVK the game plays with a still behind the menu."}], "verified": {"date": "2026-09-20", "engine": "x64-crossover26.3-r11", "chip": "Apple M1 Pro"}, "source": "db/games/the-last-flame.json"},
