{"id": "the-walking-dead", "title": "The Walking Dead", "steam": 207610, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 1, "last": "2026-10-26"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Telltale's 2012 game, the Steam one called The Walking Dead. Does not launch for the one report so far: right after starting, the game asks for a single block of about 2 GB, which no 32-bit program can get under Wine, and crashes when it doesn't get it. The graphics mode makes no difference, and Steam's DirectX setup did not help. Nothing was measured here beyond the memory probe described in the issue."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "WalkingDead101.exe crashes into Wine's debugger right after starting, in every graphics mode (an M1, r28)", "cause": "the game asks for one 2,056 MB block of memory at start (Wine logs 'out of memory for allocation, size 80810000'), gets nothing and writes through the null pointer. A 32-bit process cannot get a block that size: measured on the M4 with a probe in Wine 10 r28 and Wine 11 r25, the largest free block is 1,971 MB (2 GB address space) or 2,048 MB (4 GB, split at 0x7FFE0000 as on Windows). So the game sizes the block from something that reads differently under Wine, likely the memory status it is given (2,047 or 4,095 MB). Steam's DirectX setup did not change it", "fix": "none yet. The reporter plays the console versions meanwhile"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/the-walking-dead.json"},
{"id": "the-witcher-3-wild-hunt", "title": "The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt", "steam": 292030, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 5, "median": 3, "last": "2026-11-14"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["DirectX 11 build on DXMT is the reported way to play. Reported on an M4 Max: the CD Projekt RED launcher (REDlauncher.exe) that Steam starts first fails with \"Failed to create OpenGL context for QSurfaceFormat\", a Qt rendering problem in the launcher rather than the game. Workaround the reporter used, start bin/x64/witcher3.exe (the DirectX 11 build) directly, with Steam running, and the game launches on DXMT. Steam's own --launcher-skip option skips the launcher too but starts the DirectX 12 build, which needs D3DMetal, not measured here. In game the reporter sees the mouse pointer offset from where clicks and aim land, not yet resolved; running windowed at the display's own resolution is the usual remedy for that class of problem and is not verified for this game. No measurement by the maintainer yet. A second report, on an M1, rates it 4 after 23 minutes on DXMT and names no problem. A third report plays the DirectX 12 build on D3DMetal on the Wine 11 engine r27 with a player-made fix (see the known issues). Another report plays the DirectX 12 build on D3DMetal on the Wine 11 engine r31 on an M4 Pro over 39 minutes, with --launcher-skip and the same player-made DLL proxy, built from source (highball-db#1213)."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The CD Projekt RED launcher fails before the game with \"Failed to create OpenGL context for QSurfaceFormat\" (reported on an M4 Max, DXMT)", "cause": "reported, the launcher is a Qt app drawing through OpenGL and that path is not available under this Wine", "fix": "start bin/x64/witcher3.exe (the DirectX 11 build) directly with Steam running, for example by dropping it onto Highball, which runs it in the environment; --launcher-skip as a Steam launch option also skips it but picks the DirectX 12 build"}, {"symptom": "Mouse pointer drawn away from where clicks and aim land in game (reported)", "cause": "not measured", "fix": "none verified, try windowed mode at the display's own resolution"}, {"symptom": "The DirectX 12 build (patch 5.00b) shows a black screen on D3DMetal", "cause": "per the README of a player-made fix: D3DMetal crashes on one stream-output pipeline and the game's crash handler then deadlocks. Not measured here. The fix's other part, a bin/x64 link, answers a redirect CrossOver's app makes, which Highball's engines don't (checked in CrossOver 26.3's Wine source)", "fix": "the DirectX 11 build on DXMT (above), or the player-made witcher3-crossover-fix with --launcher-skip, HDR and DLSS/Reflex off and FXAA (highball-db#791). It replaces a game DLL with a proxy and has not been reviewed by Highball. Highball never changes game files, so the swap is each player's own step, and a game update or file check undoes it. A second player ran it the same way on an M4 Pro (highball-db#1213)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/the-witcher-3-wild-hunt.json"},
