{"id": "tom-clancys-the-division", "title": "Tom Clancy's The Division", "steam": 365590, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 2, "median": 3, "last": "2026-09-22"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["An online game, and signing in is where the patience goes: both reporters waited five to ten minutes at the server login, after which the first said it played near seamlessly with minor frame rate dips. Two independent reports agree on that wait, both on an M5. No frame rate measured and nothing run here.\n\nDXMT is the mode to start in. The second reporter went to D3DMetal and found the game would not open at all until DirectX 12 had been turned on inside the game's own video settings, which means first reaching those settings under DXMT."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Signing in to the game's servers takes five to ten minutes.", "cause": "not established. Reported twice, both on an M5 with macOS 27, and not reproduced here.", "fix": "None known. Both reporters' advice is to wait it out, after which the game plays well."}, {"symptom": "On D3DMetal the game does not open at all.", "cause": "the game starts in its DirectX 11 path, and D3DMetal does not serve it. Reported once, on an M5, and not reproduced here.", "fix": "Launch under DXMT first, turn DirectX 12 on in the game's own video settings, then D3DMetal will start it. Staying on DXMT avoids the whole step and is what the higher of the two reports used."}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/tom-clancys-the-division.json"},
{"id": "tom-clancys-the-division-2", "title": "Tom Clancy's The Division 2", "steam": 2221490, "status": "blocked", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["Easy Anti-Cheat"], "verdict": "blocked"}, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 3, "last": "2026-09-23"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Not playable on a Mac. The game uses Easy Anti-Cheat, which works on Linux through its runtime for Proton, and that runtime has no macOS build. The reporter confirms the anti-cheat check crashes the game window. They could only keep playing by repeatedly stopping the check from running and do not recommend it, and it is not recorded as a workaround here, since it defeats the anti-cheat and puts the account at risk."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/tom-clancys-the-division-2.json"},
{"id": "tomb-raider-game-of-the-year", "title": "Tomb Raider Game of the Year Edition", "steam": 203160, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-09"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Reported perfect on DXMT after a session of 11 minutes, so the report covers launch and the opening rather than a long run. The reporter played the Epic copy; the Steam id here is the same game on Steam. A second reporter played 6 minutes on Wine's own Direct3D on an M4 with macOS 27 and rated it playable with minor issues, so the game runs on two modes and DXMT is the one rated higher. A third report played 55 minutes on D3DMetal on the Wine 11 engine (r28) on an M2 Pro and rated it perfect. No measurement here yet."], "knownIssues": [], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/tomb-raider-game-of-the-year.json"},
{"id": "tomb-raider-iv-vi-remastered", "title": "Tomb Raider IV-VI Remastered", "steam": 2525380, "status": "community", "backends": {}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 5, "last": "2026-10-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["An OpenGL game, so the graphics mode does not matter. It crashed at launch because it asks for an OpenGL 3.2 core context without the forward-compatible bit macOS requires; the recipe sets the CrossOver switch that adds it, confirmed by the reporter. For a sharp picture set the environment's display scaling to 200 percent, Wine's Retina mode, or the game renders upscaled from 1512x982. Highball 0.9.24 sets the switch for every launch. No measurement here yet. A wired Xbox Series controller works (highball-db#502).", "An OpenGL game. It asks Wine's Mac driver for a 3.2 core context without the forward-compatible bit, which macOS requires, so the driver returned nothing and the game crashed on its first OpenGL call, on every graphics mode. The CrossOver switch the engine's Mac driver carries adds the bit (found and confirmed by the reporter of highball#136 on an M1 Pro, macOS 27). For a sharp picture set the environment's display scaling to 200 percent, which turns on Wine's Retina mode; the reporter saw an upscaled 1512x982 without it."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crashes right after launch on every graphics mode, page fault at address zero (reported on an M1 Pro, macOS 27)", "cause": "measured by the reporter with WINEDEBUG=+wgl: the game requests an OpenGL 3.2 core context without the forward-compatible bit and Wine's Mac driver refuses it", "fix": "this recipe sets CX_FWD_COMPAT_GL_CTX=1, confirmed by the reporter"}, {"symptom": "Pixelated picture, the game renders at 1512x982 and is upscaled (reported on an M1 Pro)", "cause": "Wine's Mac driver renders at the logical resolution unless RetinaMode is on", "fix": "set the environment's display scaling to 200 percent (Wine's Retina mode), reported by the same person"}, {"symptom": "Crashes right after launch on every graphics mode, page fault at address zero (reported on an M1 Pro, macOS 27)", "cause": "measured by the reporter with WINEDEBUG=+wgl: the game requests an OpenGL 3.2 core context without the forward-compatible bit and Wine's Mac driver refuses it", "fix": "this recipe sets CX_FWD_COMPAT_GL_CTX=1, confirmed by the reporter"}, {"symptom": "Pixelated picture, the game renders at 1512x982 and is upscaled (reported on an M1 Pro)", "cause": "Wine's Mac driver renders at the logical resolution unless RetinaMode is on", "fix": "set the environment's display scaling to 200 percent (Wine's Retina mode), reported by the same person"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/tomb-raider-iv-vi-remastered.json"},
