{"id": "warframe", "title": "Warframe", "steam": 230410, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": {"names": ["Unknown (Custom)"], "verdict": "warning"}, "reports": {"count": 5, "median": 5, "last": "2026-11-07"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [{"type": "registry", "key": "HKCU\\Software\\Wine\\AppDefaults\\Launcher.exe\\DllOverrides", "name": "dwrite", "valueType": "REG_SZ", "data": "", "platforms": ["mac"]}], "notes": ["Re-verified on engine r2 on 2026-09-10: the launcher updates and starts the game, Login with Steam signs in without typing anything, and the Orbiter runs at 82-94 fps at 1728x1117 fullscreen on DXMT 0.80. Apply the warframe recipe first: it turns DirectWrite off for the game's launcher only (Tools\\Launcher.exe), whose embedded browser otherwise paints a black window on this engine, the same DirectWrite problem as Sikarugir #255. With that override the launcher shows its EULA, updates the game and starts it. The game itself needs nothing. Use DXMT: the first tutorial mission, with combat, ran at about 35 fps at 1728x1117 borderless (the game's own low preset, 1280x720 render, anti-aliasing and ambient occlusion off) with the Metal HUD reading 28 ms of GPU per frame; later in the same session, past the tutorial, the maintainer's own play ran above 100 fps by the HUD. DXVK also reaches the mission but is GPU-bound at about 16 fps (51 ms GPU) with the same settings. 'Login with Steam' works; a Steam account without a Warframe account gets the game's own bind-or-create dialog, which is normal. A sleeping display stalls the game for as long as it sleeps, so keep the Mac awake for long sessions. Verified 2026-09-04 on macOS 26.6.2, M1 Pro: launcher update, Steam login, account creation, tutorial mission and later play; Exit Game shuts the process down cleanly (the game log ends with its normal shutdown). A D3DMetal report on the 0.10.4 beta on an M3 Pro with macOS 27 rates it perfect across every planet and environment with HDR on, with a frame rate drop in Duviri that the reporter says every platform shows. Which engine ran it is not settled, the id in the report matches none, and on macOS 27 D3DMetal is 3.0 on the default r19 or 4.0 beta 2 on the opt-in r20. No frame rate was given for that session. The anti-cheat map still lists Warframe with a custom anti-cheat and a warning verdict, and this reporter, like the earlier ones, played without a kick. On an M5 Pro the Orbiter ran at 75 to 90 fps with every setting maxed out, though the Mac got loud and very hot, so lower settings are kinder for long sessions (highball-db#1040).", "Warframe's Steam entry starts Tools\\Launcher.exe, an updater with an embedded browser, and that browser paints nothing under this engine's DirectWrite (a black window with no buttons). The override above disables DirectWrite for Launcher.exe alone, so the launcher draws with GDI text, shows its EULA and Play button, and updates the game. The game keeps DirectWrite. Use DXMT for the game; DXVK runs it too but at about half the frame rate. The same per-executable override was described by leontov-eng on Sikarugir issue #255 on 2026-08-24; Highball ships it as data so nobody has to find winecfg."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Frame rate drops in Duviri (reported on an M3 Pro, D3DMetal, Highball 0.10.4 beta, highball-db#308)", "cause": "Not investigated here. The reporter says the same drop happens on every platform", "fix": "None reported"}, {"symptom": "The Warframe launcher window is black; the game never updates or starts", "cause": "the launcher's embedded browser renders through DirectWrite, which paints nothing in this Wine (Sikarugir #255 has the same symptom for other CEF launchers)", "fix": "the registry step in this recipe, verified 2026-09-04: the launcher showed its EULA, updated the game and started it"}, {"symptom": "'Login with Steam' fails and a bind-or-create dialog appears", "cause": "the Steam account has no Warframe account linked yet; this is the game's own flow, not an engine problem", "fix": "choose Create New or Bind Existing in that dialog"}], "verified": {"date": "2026-09-04", "engine": "x64-sikarugir10.0_6-r1", "chip": "Apple M1 Pro"}, "source": "db/games/warframe.json"},
