{"id": "where-safety-ends-remake", "title": "WHERE SAFETY ENDS *Remake*", "steam": 2823140, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "d3dmetal"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 1, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-06"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["A Unity game that opens a fixed 1754x1240 window, set by its own script, so on most Mac screens the window runs past the bottom edge and some screens get cut off. Unity's -screen-width and -screen-height launch options and the saved Screenmanager values do not change it: the game sets the size itself and writes it back. Turn on Retina resolution in the environment's settings: Wine then counts the screen in pixels, the window becomes 877x620 points, and the whole title menu fit on a 1920x1080 display here. Retina resolution applies to every game in that environment."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "The window is larger than the screen and runs past its bottom edge, cutting off parts of the game (profiles, menus)", "cause": "the game's own ManageFullScreen script sets a 1754x1240 window whatever the screen size", "fix": "turn on Retina resolution in the environment's settings, which halves the window's size on screen (measured on an M4); confirmed by the reporter (highball-db#350)"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/where-safety-ends-remake.json"},
{"id": "where-winds-meet", "title": "Where Winds Meet", "steam": 3564740, "status": "community", "backends": {"mac": "dxmt"}, "antiCheat": null, "reports": {"count": 4, "median": 4, "last": "2026-10-15"}, "nativeMac": false, "optIn": false, "requires": [], "steps": [], "notes": ["Free to play. Reported playable on DXMT on the Wine 11 engine with Highball's frame cap at 60 on an M5 Pro, over sessions of 16 minutes and just over three hours without a crash, and one crash about two and a half minutes into a session with the in-game Store window open. Stutter in areas dense with NPCs. The crash is not a one-off, the reporter counted five in two days on highball#240, from 15 seconds to an hour and a half into a session, always with the same line in the log. It is DXMT's clear pipelines being built before the Metal device field they read was set, fixed in DXMT on 30 September. The default Wine 10 engine has carried the fix since Highball 0.10.1 and the Wine 11 engine gets it in r16, which the 0.10.4 beta ships. A later 102-minute session on D3DMetal on the same r12 had a bit of stutter and no crash in the report, which fits the crash being DXMT's. Whether that session used the game's own DirectX 12 launch option or the default one was not said. Whether the default engine runs it as well is not known, and the anti-cheat map has no entry for this game. No frame rate was given and nothing was measured here."], "knownIssues": [{"symptom": "Crashes at random, from 15 seconds to an hour and a half into a session, once with the in-game Store window open (reported on an M5 Pro, Wine 11 engine r12, DXMT, highball#240)", "cause": "DXMT built its clear pipelines before the Metal device field they read was set up, so the request went to whatever that memory held. The 'unrecognized selector sent to instance' line in the log is the signature. Fixed in DXMT on 30 September", "fix": "The Wine 11 engine carries the fixed DXMT from r16. Environments on it never change revision on their own, so pick the newest, x64-crossover26.3-r19 with Highball 0.10.10, on the environment's Full page under Advanced, Engine. The default engine has it since 0.10.1. D3DMetal avoids it, a 102-minute session there had stutter only"}, {"symptom": "Stutter in areas with many NPCs on DXMT, and a bit of stutter on D3DMetal too (reported on an M5 Pro)", "cause": "Not investigated here", "fix": "None known. The reporter plays with Highball's frame cap at 60"}], "verified": null, "source": "db/games/where-winds-meet.json"},
